'2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5317,'Brewer Consulting Group',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business,LobbyingFirm',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5318,'Washington Health Advocates',27,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business,LobbyingFirm',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5319,'AKP&D Message & Media',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','With a team of professionals experienced in every aspect of campaign message and strategy, AKP&D Message and Media, formerly Axelrod & Associates, has helped elect Democrats to every office from alderman to President â in every region across the country. And no firm in America has helped elect more mayors.\r\n\r\nFor a winning message â and the day-to-day strategies and award-winning commercials to deliver it effectively â Democratic candidates can\'t do better than adding AKP&D to their team.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5320,'Koch Industries',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Koch Industries owns a diverse group of companies involved in refining and chemicals; process and pollution control equipment and technologies; minerals and fertilizer; fibers and polymers; commodity and financial trading and services; and forest and consumer products.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5321,'Chrysler',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Auburn Hills, Mich., this company manufactures Chrysler, Jeep and Dodge vehicles and Mopar brand parts. Cerberus Capital Management purchased Chrysler, the third largest domestic auto manufacturer, in 2007 from DaimlerChrysler (since renamed Daimler A.G.). Cerebus owns 80.1% of Chrysler; Daimler holds the remaining 19.9%.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5322,'Bechtel',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:13:\"Bechtel Group\";}','Org','Four generations of family members have run the company that Warren Bechtel founded in 1898. Bechtel, headquartered in San Francisco, is engaged in a range of projects in civil infrastructure, power, petrochemicals, telecommunications and government services. Notable projects completed by Bechtel include Hoover Dam; Bay Area Rapid Transit; the Channel Tunnel connecting England and France; Jubail Industrial City in Saudi Arabia and Hong Kong International Airport. Current projects in Bechtel\'s portfolio include the waste treatment plant at the Department of Energy\'s site in Hanford, Washington; renovation of the London Underground; Romanian Highway System; and a multi-billion dollar aluminum processing facility in Oman.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5323,'C&S Wholesale Grocers',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','C&S Wholesale Grocers of Keene, New Hampshire is a distributor of food to supermarkets, retail stores and military bases. C&S is the second-largest food wholesaler in the U.S., serving independent supermarkets, regional and national chains via warehouses in Vermont, Massachusetts, Connecticut, New York, New Jersey, Pennsylvania, Maryland, Ohio, California, Hawaii, Alabama, South Carolina and Tennessee. Customers include Ahold (Stop & Shop, Giant Carlisle, Tops and Giant Landover), Albertson\'s (Shaw\'s), Big Y, Bi-Lo/Bruno\'s, BJ\'s, Great Atlantic & Pacific Tea Co., Pathmark and Safeway.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5324,'US Foodservice',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','US Foodservice, formerly a division of Royal Ahold of the Netherlands, is the second largest foodservice distributor in the United States. The company distributes both national brand products and its own private label items, ranging from meats to frozen foods. Private equity firms Kohlberg Kravis Roberts and Clayton, Dubilier & Rice acquired US Foodservice for $7.1 billion in 2007. Corporate headquarters are in Columbia, Maryland.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5325,'Semgroup',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','SemGroup LP is a midstream service company providing the energy industry means to move products from the wellhead to the wholesale marketplace. SemGroup provides diversified services for end users and consumers of crude oil, natural gas, natural gas liquids, refined products and asphalt. Services include purchasing, selling, processing, transporting and storing energy. SemGroup serves customers in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Wales, Switzerland and Vietnam.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5326,'Meijer',6,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Grand Rapids, Mich., Meijer is a large grocery and merchandise chain operating 176 Super Centers in five Midwest states (Illinois, Indiana, Kentucky, Michigan and Ohio). The Meijer family still owns the company, which it founded in 1934. Aside from its grocery operations, Meijer stores include such specialty departments as fueling centers, auto supplies, electronics, nutrition centers and floral departments. Each store also has in-store banking and pharmacy services. 				   Brands: Meijer','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5327,'HE Butt Grocery',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','HE Butt Grocery, one of the nation\'s largest privately held companies, is a large regional supermarket chain, operating over 300 stores throughout the southwest, primarily in Texas. The company also operates a handful of stores in Mexico. The Butt family founded the company in Kerrville, Texas in 1905. Charles Butt is chairman and chief executive officer. 				   Brands: Central Market, H-E-B','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5328,'Fidelity Investments',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:7:\"FMR LLC\";}','Org','Fidelity Investments is the nation\'s largest mutual fund company and one of the largest providers of financial services. Fidelity holds $3.2 trillion in customer assets, including $1.5 trillion it manages. Headquartered in Boston, Fidelity services more than 22 million individuals and employs 42,000.\r\n\r\nThe umbrella company for Fidelity\'s holdings, a company previously known as FMR Corp., was converted into a limited liability company called FMR LLC in November 2007.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5329,'Cox Enterprises',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Atlanta, Cox Enterprises\' private divisions are Cox Communications, Cox Newspapers, Cox Television, Manheim (vehicle auctions), and Cox Auto Trader. The company also has a public subsidiary, Cox Radio (NYSE: CXR), whose revenues and employees Forbes Magazine excludes in determining a ranking for Cox Enterprises among America\'s largest private companies. 				   Brands: Cox','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5330,'Flying J',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Established as a small petroleum marketing company in 1968, Flying J has grown to become the largest retail distributor of diesel fuel in North America. Flying J is a fully integrated petroleum company engaged in exploring, producing, refining, transporting, wholesaling and retail marketing of petroleum products. The company owns and operates 175 travel plazas and fuel stops in 44 states and Canadian provinces. These locations offer convenience stores, food service, showers, game rooms and other travel service amenities. Some locations also offer lodging and truck service rentals. Flying J\'s related companies offer a wide variety of services including financial services, insurance, communication services, truck fleet sales and other related interstate travel services. 				   Brands: Flying J Travel Plaza','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5331,'TransMontaigne',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','TransMontaigne, of Denver, Colorado, manages assets, distribution and supply chains for refined petroleum products, chemicals, and crude oil. Its operations are primarily in the Gulf Coast, Midwest and East Coast regions. TransMontaigne went private via a leveraged buyout by Morgan Stanley Capital Group in September 2006. Revenue estimates exclude sales from publicly traded subsidiaries.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5332,'JM Family Enterprises',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','JM Family Enterprises is a diversified automotive company. Its primary subsidiaries and divisions include Southeast Toyota Distributors, the nation\'s largest franchised distributor of Toyota vehicles; World Omni Financial; JM&A Group; JM Service Center, the company\'s internal shared services center; JM Lexus; and JMSolutions, a dealer-focused technology products and services division. Headquartered in Deerfield Beach, Florida, the company has key operations in Jacksonville, Florida; Mobile, Alabama; Commerce and Alpharetta, Georgia; and St. Louis, Missouri. 				   Brands: Toyota','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5333,'Reyes Holdings',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Reyes Holdings distributes food and beverage products throughout North, Central and South America. The company\'s beer operations in California, Illinois, Virginia, and Washington D.C. comprise the largest beer distribution system in the United States. The Martin-Brower Company, a Reyes Holdings portfolio company, is the largest supplier of distribution services to the McDonald\'s restaurant system. It is the exclusive distributor to approximately half of the McDonald\'s in the United States, and all the chain\'s restaurants in Canada, Puerto Rico, Brazil and Central America. Another Reyes Holdings\' company, Reinhart FoodService, is the third largest independent foodservice distributor in the United States. Its clients include Burger King and Subway restaurants. Reyes Holdings\' affiliates also provide logistics services and manage a portfolio of real estate properties.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5334,'Tenaska Energy',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Tenaska is an international power development company and energy marketer with expertise in power plant development, ownership and operation; natural gas and electric power marketing; and fuel procurement. Headquartered in Omaha, Nebraska, the company employs 569 people worldwide.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5335,'Advance Publications',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1922 by Sam Newhouse, Advance Publications is a holding company whose media properties include Cond','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5336,'S.C. Johnson & Sons Inc.',24,NULL,'a:11:{i:0;s:0:\"\";i:1;s:26:\"S.C. Johnson and Sons Inc.\";i:2;s:23:\"SC Johnson and Son Inc.\";i:3;s:23:\"SC Johnson and Son Inc.\";i:4;s:26:\"S.C. Johnson and Sons Inc.\";i:5;s:23:\"SC Johnson and Son Inc.\";i:6;s:26:\"S.C. Johnson and Sons Inc.\";i:7;s:23:\"SC Johnson and Son Inc.\";i:8;s:26:\"S.C. Johnson and Sons Inc.\";i:9;s:23:\"SC Johnson and Son Inc.\";i:10;s:26:\"S.C. Johnson and Sons Inc.\";}','Org','SC Johnson & Sons is a family-owned and -managed business based in Racine, Wisconsin. The company manufactures household goods and products for home cleaning, home storage, air care, personal care and insect control. Its well-known brands include Windex, Pledge, Glade, Shout, Saran, Ziploc, Edge, Scrubbing Bubbles and Raid. The 121-year old company has operations in more than 70 countries and sells products in over a 100 countries. 				   Brands: Drano, Edge, Fantastik, Glade, Grab-It, Off!, Oust, Pledge, Raid, Saran Wrap, Scrubbing Bubbles, Shout, Skintimate, Vanish, Windex, Ziploc','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-04 23:14:57',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5337,'Menard',6,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','With stores scattered throughout the Midwest, Menard is the nation\'s third-largest home improvement chain. Stores sell traditional home improvement products&mdash;such as floor coverings, hardware, millwork, paint and tools. The company has 230 stores in 11 states.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5338,'Hilton Hotels',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','With nearly 2,800 hotels and 485,000 rooms in more than 80 countries, Hilton Hotels is one of the largest hotel operators in the United States. Brands include Doubletree, Embassy Suites and Hampton, as well as the company\'s flagship Hilton brand. Private equity firm Blackstone Group bought Hilton in 2007 for about $26 billion, including debt.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5339,'Murdock Holding Company',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Murdock Holding Company is comprised of Dole Food Company and Castle & Cooke. Founded in 1851, Dole is the largest U.S. producer and marketer of fresh fruit, fresh vegetables and fresh-cut flowers. The company also markets a growing line of packaged and frozen foods. Dole operates in more than 90 countries. Castle & Cooke, and its affiliated companies, operate businesses that include real estate, transportation leasing equipment and brick manufacturing. Castle & Cooke also owns two luxury resorts in Hawaii on its 90% owned island of Lanai. 				   Brands: Dole','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5340,'Giant Eagle',11,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Giant Eagle is a large supermarket chain, operating (as of June 2007) 156 corporate and 68 franchised stores. The company also operates over 131 convenience stores under the GetGo banner. Stores are located in Pennsylvania, Ohio, West Virginia and Maryland. Founded in 1931, corporate headquarters are in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. 				   Brands: Giant Eagle','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5341,'Cumberland Farms',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1938 and still owned by the Haseotes family, Cumberland Farms, of Canton, Mass., owns and operates convenience stores and gas stations throughout New England, New York, the Mid-Atlantic States and Florida under the Cumberland Farms, Exxon and Gulf names. The company also operates a bakery and has a warehouse distribution center in Westboro, Mass. 				   Brands: Cumberland Farms, Exxon, Gulf','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5342,'Marmon Group',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Marmon Group is an international association of more than 125 business units that operate independently within diverse business sectors. The organization originated in 1953 with acquisition of the Colson Co. Today, member companies employ 21,500 people and operate more than 250 production facilities primarily in North America, the United Kingdom and China. Marmon member companies provide industrial products and services, metal products and materials, retail store equipment and services, transportation products and services, water treatment equipment and wire and cable products. Member companies include Union Tank Car, Marmon/Keystone, Cerro Flow Products, Cerro Wire & Cable, LA Darling, EcoWater Systems and Webb Wheel Products.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5343,'Southern Wine & Spirits',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Southern Wine & Spirits of America is the nation\'s largest wine and spirits distributor with current operations in 27 states. Chairman and chief executive officer Harvey Chaplin and Wayne Chaplin, president and chief operating officer, together own more than 50% of the company.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5344,'Sinclair Oil',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The roots of Sinclair go back to its 1916 founding by Harry F. Sinclair. Today over 2,600 Sinclair gas stations and convenience stores operate in the U.S. West and Midwest. The company operates three refineries and over 1,000 miles of pipeline in the Rocky Mountains. Other operations include a chain of western hotels, the Snow Basin ski resort in Utah, the Sun Valley ski resort in Idaho and a large cattle ranching operation.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5345,'CDW',3,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','CDW, formerly Computer Discount Warehouse, provides computers, accessories, and services to businesses. It went private in 2007 under Madison Dearborn and Providence Equity Partners.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5346,'Quiktrip',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Chester Cadieux started this company with one store in 1958. Today under Chester Cadieux III, chairman of the board and chief executive officer, QuikTrip owns and operates 477 convenience stores and gasoline service stations throughout nine states in the South, Midwest and Southwest. Corporate headquarters are in Tulsa, Oklahoma. 				   Brands: QuikTrip','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5347,'Freescale Semiconductor',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Freescale Semiconductor designs and manufactures embedded semiconductors for the automotive, consumer, industrial, networking and wireless markets. Based in Austin, Texas, the company has design, research and development, manufacturing or sales operations in more than 30 countries. Freescale, formerly part of Motorola, went public in July 2004. In December 2006, Freescale Semiconductor completed its merger with a group of private equity firms led by the Blackstone Group and became a private company.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5348,'Love\'s Travel Stops',19,NULL,'a:2:{i:0;s:0:\"\";i:1;s:25:\"Love\'s Country Stores Inc\";}','Org','Love\'s Travel Stops & Country Stores, a family-owned business, runs a chain of 193 interstate highway travel stops and convenience stores located in thirty-two states. Love\'s offers fuel, convenience items and branded fast-food restaurants, including A&W, Arby\'s, Baskin-Robbins, Carl\'s Jr., Godfather\'s Pizza, Hardee\'s, Subway and Taco Bell. Tom and Judy Love founded the company as the Musket Oil Co. in Oklahoma 1964. 				   Brands: Love\'s Country Stores, Love\'s Travel Stops','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-12 18:15:03',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5349,'Alticor',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','This company\'s roots date to 1959, when Jay Van Andel and Rich DeVos, a pair of direct sales veterans, launched Amway. In October 2000, the firm established Alticor, a holding company for Amway, Quixtar and other interests. Alticor manufactures markets and distributes more than 450 consumer products including soaps, cosmetics, vitamin and food supplements, and air- and water-treatment systems. It sells its products largely through a global network of over 3.6 million independent representatives. Representatives can also sell online through the company\'s Quixtar organization. Other operations include the Amway Grand Plaza Hotel in Grand Rapids, Michigan, and Access Business Group, a product development, manufacturing and logistics subsidiary. 				   Brands: Amway, Artistry, LOC, Nutrilite, Quixtar, SA8, eSpring','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5350,'Unisource Worldwide',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Norcross, Georgia, Unisource Worldwide distributes paper products, packaging materials and facility supplies throughout North America. Through a network of 75 distribution centers, the company serves publishers, copy centers, government agencies and other paper-intensive businesses. The company also operates 43 retail stores. 				   Brands: Paper Plus, Rollsource, Websources','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5351,'Gordon Food Service',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Gordon Food Service, founded in 1897, is North America\'s largest family-owned and managed broadline foodservice distributor. GFS is an international corporation offering more than 16,000 GFS and nationally branded, specialty and exclusive products to over 45,000 customers in 15 states within the U.S. and throughout Canada. The company also operates over 124 Marketplace retail stores. 				   Brands: Gordon Food Service, GFS Marketplace','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5352,'Transammonia',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Transammonia, originally part of Apco Oil in Oklahoma City, is a commodities merchandiser and trader of fertilizer products, liquefied petroleum gases (LPG), petrochemicals, methanol and petroleum products. Transammonia\'s subsidiaries include Trammochem, Sea-3, Trammo Gas, and Trammo Petroleum. Headquarters are in New York City.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5353,'Avaya',5,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Avaya is a global communications company that specializes in secure Internet Protocol (IP) telephony systems, communications software applications and services. Avaya serves more than one million customers with their two business segments, Avaya Global Services and Global Communications Solutions.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5354,'MBM',3,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','MBM is a large food service distributor with 30 distribution centers located throughout the U.S. J.R. Wordsworth started the company in 1947 as distributor to retail food stores. His sons and daughter bought the business in 1976, phased out the retail operations and began a customized food distribution business that focuses on national restaurant chains.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5355,'Allegis Group',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1983, Allegis Group is the world\'s largest privately held staffing company. Its family of companies includes Aerotek, a provider of engineering staffing, and TEKsystems, a provider of IT staffing. Headquartered in Hanover, Maryland, Allegis Group has offices in over 300 cities throughout the United States, Puerto Rico, Canada and Europe.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5356,'Kohler',6,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Kohler, Wisconsin, John Michael Kohler founded this company in 1873 when he purchased the Sheboygan Union Iron and Steel Foundry. The firm originally produced cast iron and steel implements for farmers, castings for furniture factories and ornamental iron pieces. Today Kohler manufactures and markets bath and kitchen products, engines and power generation systems, furniture and accessories, and cabinetry and tile. Additionally, Kohler operates two luxury golf and recreation resorts, Destination Kohler and Destination St. Andrews, and owns other real estate holdings. 				   Brands: Ann Sacks Tile and Stone, Baker, Baker Knapp & Tubbs, Canac, Englefield, Hytec, Jacob Delafon, Kallista, Karat, Kohler, McGuire, Milling Road, Mira, Neomediam, Robern, Sanijura, Sterling','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5357,'Save Mart Supermarkets',22,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1952, Save Mart Supermarkets currently runs 256 grocery stores under the names Save Mart, S-Mart Foods and Food Maxx (warehouse supermarkets). The stores are located in northern and central California. Other operations include refrigerated transport. In March 2007, Save Mart acquired 132 stores from Albertsons, which doubled the size of the company. The company currently has close to 25,000 employees. 				   Brands: Food Maxx, S-Mart Foods, Save Mart','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5358,'Southwire',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Southwire produces aluminum and copper rods, wires and cables for the transmission and distribution of electricity. The company dates back to 1937, when Roy Richards, Sr. started to erect power lines for the Rural Electrification Administration. In 1950, Richards founded Southwire as a supplier of wire to the original company. Southwire now operates 21 facilities in the U.S. and one in Mexico.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5359,'RaceTrac Petroleum',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Carl Bolch Sr., who opened his first independent gasoline station in St. Louis, Missouri, started this company in 1934. In 1979, the company rebranded its stores under the RaceTrac and Raceway names. Today Georgia-based RaceTrac Petroleum operates 528 convenience stores and gasoline stations in 12 states. 				   Brands: Racetrac, Raceway','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5360,'Bloomberg',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Bloomberg, L.P. is a global media company that provides economic and financial news and computerized information on securities trading. The company, headquartered in Manhattan, has interests in radio (WBBR), television, its own financial news magazine and a financial news wire service with more than 1,700 reporters and editors in 127 bureaus worldwide. The Bloomberg radio channel is available on XM, Sirius and WorldSpace satellite radio. Bloomberg Press publishes magazines and books for investment professionals. Founder Michael Bloomberg owns the company. 				   Brands: Bloomberg','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5361,'Wawa',4,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Wawa owns and operates convenience stores and gasoline stations in Pennsylvania, New Jersey, Delaware, Maryland and Virginia. These stores offer deli products, fresh produce and a Wawa line of dairy products and ice cream. The first Wawa store opened in April 1964 in Folsom, Pennsylvania. Wawa offers gasoline at 210 of its stores. Corporate headquarters are in Wawa, Pennsylvania. The company employs 16,866 people in approximately 560 stores. 				   Brands: Wawa','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5362,'Gulf States Toyota',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Gulf States Toyota is one of two independent national distributors of new Toyota vehicles, parts and accessories. Founded in 1969 by Thomas Friedkin and still owned by The Friedkin Companies, the Houston, Texas distributor serves 146 dealerships throughout Arkansas, Louisiana, Texas, Oklahoma and Mississippi.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5363,'Hearst',6,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1887 by William Randolph Hearst, the Hearst Corporation has interests in magazine, newspaper, and business publishing, as well as newspaper comics, features syndication and Internet activities. Hearst also operates radio and television stations and produces television programs. The company is a partner in several cable ventures, including Lifetime, Arts & Entertainment, The History Channel, and ESPN. Forbes\' revenue estimate for Hearst excludes cable partnerships and the firm\'s public subsidiary, Hearst-Argyle Television.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5364,'Kinray',6,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Kinray is the largest privately held wholesale pharmaceutical distributor in the world. It supplies pharmaceutical products, medical supplies and health and beauty care products to over 3,000 pharmacies in New York, New Jersey, Connecticut, Pennsylvania, Massachusetts, Rhode Island and Delaware. Stewart Rahr is chief executive officer and president.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5365,'Ergon',5,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Ergon, a privately held corporation headquartered in Jackson, Miss., operates diverse businesses. The engineered products and services group is a refiner, transporter, producer, distributor and marketer of petroleum products. The Diversified Technology (DTI) subsidiary specializes in the development and/or fabrication of equipment for markets such as communications, telephony, process control, military applications and homeland security.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5366,'Booz Allen Hamilton',19,NULL,'a:8:{i:0;s:0:\"\";i:1;s:25:\"Booz Allen & Hamilton Inc\";i:2;s:24:\"Booz Allen and Hamiliton\";i:3;s:19:\"Booz.Allen~Hamilton\";i:4;s:21:\"Booz*Allen & Hamilton\";i:5;s:19:\"Booz-Allen Hamilton\";i:6;s:21:\"Booz-Allen & Hamilton\";i:7;s:23:\"Booz-Allen and Hamilton\";}','Org','Booz Allen, founded in 1914 by Edwin Booz, is a global strategy and technology-consulting company with a staff of over 19,000 employees on six continents. The company provides services to the world\'s leading corporations, government and other public agencies, emerging growth companies and institutions. Booz Allen\'s principle areas of expertise include strategy and leadership, organization and change management, operations, innovation, sales and marketing and information technology.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5367,'Charmer Sunbelt Group',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Charmer Sunbelt Group, of New York City, is a distributor of wine, spirits, beers, bottled water, and other non-alcoholic beverages. Its affiliated independent companies operate in 15 states and the District of Columbia. In July 2006, Peerless Importers and Charmer Industries (a subsidiary of Charmer Sunbelt Group) agreed to merge and form a new entity, Empire Merchants, which will remain a subsidiary of Charmer Sunbelt Group.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5368,'Republic National Distributing Company',38,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','In May 2007, Republic Beverage acquired National Distributing Company. The combined firm operates across 20 states and Washington, DC. Republic National Distributing Company is the second largest distributor of premium wines and spirits in the United States. Corporate headquarters are in Atlanta, Georgia.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5369,'84 Lumber',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Located in Eighty Four, Pennsylvania, the company operates a chain of discount lumber-and-building-materials outlets for professional builders and do-it-yourself customers. Stores offer a no-frills atmosphere and are popular for their do-it-yourself home building kits. Founder Joseph A. Hardy Sr. opened his first store in 1956. 				   Brands: 84 Lumber','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5370,'Hallmark Cards',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Started in 1910 by Mr. Joyce C. Hall, Hallmark Cards sells greeting cards products and art supplies in 43,000 retail outlets in 100 countries. Among its subsidiaries are Crayola, which makes Crayola crayons and markers, and Silly Putty. Subsidiary Crown Media Holdings is a publicly traded company (nasdaq: CRWN) that owns and operates the Hallmark Channel. For the purposes of our Private Company rankings, Forbes excludes Crown Media in both our revenue estimate and employee count for Hallmark Cards. 				   Brands: Ambassador, Crayola, DaySpring, Expressions from Hallmark, Gift Certificate Center, Hallmark Cards, Hallmark Channel, Hallmark Hall of Fame, Hallmark Keepsake Ornaments, Image Arts, InteArt, Mahogany, Party Express from Hallmark, Shoebox, Silly Putty, Sinceramente Hallmark, Sunrise Greetings, The Picture People, Tree of Life, William Arthur','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5371,'Kingston Technology',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1987 by John Tu and David Sun, Kingston Technology is an independent packager of memory products for computers and other electronic devices. Kingston operates manufacturing facilities in Malaysia, Taiwan, China and Fountain Valley, Calif. Kingston\'s back-end processing facility, Payton Technology Corp., provides memory packaging, testing and logistics. With the advent of Payton, Kingston supports all memory processing functions&mdash;from receipt of wafer to completed module. Kingston serves a network of distributors, original equipment manufacturers and retail customers worldwide. 				   Brands: DataPak, DataTraveler, HyperX, Kingston, ValueRAM','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5372,'Schneider National',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1935, Schneider National, based in Green Bay, Wisconsin, is America\'s largest private truckload carrier. Schneider National currently operates 14,000 tractors, 40,000 trailers and has partnerships with over 6,000 carriers. Schneider Logistics, a wholly owned subsidiary of Schneider National, provides supply chain management technology, managed services, engineering services and freight payment. 				   Brands: Schneider, Schneider Logistics, Schneider National','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5373,'Carlson Cos',11,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Carlson Companies of Minnetonka, Minn., is the parent to company-owned and franchised interests in marketing, travel and hospitality. Its brands include Regent International Hotels, Radisson Hotels & Resorts, Radisson Seven Seas Cruises, T.G.I. Friday\'s restaurants, Carlson Wagonlit Travel, and Carlson Marketing, among others. For the purposes of its revenue estimate, Forbes considers only net revenues flowing back to the parent company, not total system-wide sales. 				   Brands: Carlson Wagonlit Travel, Country Inns & Suites by Carlson, Park Inn & Park Plaza, Pick Up Stix, Radisson Hotels & Resorts, Radisson Seven Seas Cruises, Regent International Hotels, TGI Friday\'s','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5374,'Red Apple Group',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','John Catsimatidis, who also owns 100% of Gristede\'s Supermarkets, a supermarket chain, owns Red Apple Group. Red Apple\'s subsidiary, United Refining, refines petroleum and operates convenience stores in New York, Pennsylvania, and Ohio. The company also has real estate interests in New York, Florida and the Virgin Islands. 				   Brands: Country Fair, Gristedes, Red Apple Food Mart, Red Apple Kwik Fill','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5375,'Roundy\'s Supermarkets',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Roundy\'s is one of the nation\'s oldest wholesale and retail food distributors. Founded in 1872, Roundy\'s provides services to retail locations in the Midwest from five wholesale distribution centers. In addition, it owns and operates grocery stores under the Pick \'n Save, Copps Food Center, and Rainbow Foods banners. The company, owned by the Chicago investment company Willis Stein & Partners, employs 21,000 associates throughout its entire network. 				   Brands: Copps, Orchard Foods, Park & Save, Pick \'n Save, Rainbow Foods, Roundy\'s','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5376,'HT Hackney',10,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1891, HT Hackney, of Knoxville, Tenn., distributes groceries to convenience stores and small grocery stores in 21 Southeastern and Eastern states. Through its subsidiaries, HT Hackney also has interests in oil distribution, furniture manufacturing and assembly, retail automation systems and natural spring water. 				   Brands: Laure, Mountain Springs','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5377,'Brightstar',10,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Brightstar Corp., headquartered in Miami, Florida, provides customers in the wireless industry with inventory management, logistics, fulfillment, Internet-based solutions, customized packaging and after-sales support. The company is the world\'s largest wireless distribution and supply chain management firm, distributing premier wireless brands such as Motorola, Sony Ericsson and LG. Brightstar operates 40 facilities in 34 countries and has recently opened offices in Dubai, India, and Singapore. R. Marcelo Claure founded the company in 1997 and remains its chief executive officer.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5378,'Global Hyatt',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Part of H Group Holding until 2005, Global Hyatt Corporation, owns, franchises and manages hotels under the Hyatt, Hyatt Regency, Grand Hyatt and Park Hyatt names. The origin of Global Hyatt Corporation goes back to 1957 and Hyatt R. von Dehn\'s Hyatt House hotel at Los Angeles International Airport. That same year, Jay Pritzker bought the hotel and expanded its presence; the Pritzker family still owns this business. In 1967, Hyatt Corporation opened the world\'s first atrium hotel and by 1969, there were 12 Hyatt hotels in the U.S. Today there are 217 Hyatt hotels and resorts in 43 countries.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5379,'Edward Jones',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Edward Jones traces its roots back to 1871. The company serves more than 7 million clients from more than 9,300 offices in the U.S. and through its affiliates in Canada and the United Kingdom. Edward Jones advises individual investors exclusively and offers a wide variety of investments, including certificates of deposit, bonds, stocks and mutual funds. Edward Jones is the principal operating company of the Jones Financial Companies.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5380,'Perdue Farms',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Arthur W. Perdue founded Perdue Farms in 1920 but the company gained national attention as a brand name when son and successor, Franklin P. Perdue, became television pitchman for the company. Perdue sells its chicken and turkey products to food retailers and food service companies located on the East Coast, as far west as Chicago and in several foreign countries, including China. Trademarked Perdue offerings include Prime Parts, Ovenstuffer, Fit \'N Easy and Cafe Perdue. Perdue also runs two soybean-processing plants that produce vegetable oils and ingredients for animal feed. 				   Brands: Boastin\' Roaster, Cafe Perdue, Carving Classics, Chef\'s Choice, Cooking Good, Fit \'N Easy, Fun Shapes, Individually Frozen, MicroStart 60, Ovenstuffer, Perdue, Perdue Done It!, Perdue Prime Parts, Perdue-AgriRecyle, Roasting Chicken, Shenandoah, Short Cuts, TenderReady','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5381,'Sheetz',6,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Bob Sheetz founded Sheetz, of Altoona, Pennsylvania, in 1952. The company currently operates 340 convenience stores in Pennsylvania, Maryland, Ohio, the Virginias and North Carolina. Stores offer a variety of items including made-to-order sandwiches and salads, baked goods, breakfast foods, a large assortment of hot and cold drinks as well as Sheetz Gasoline and other convenience items. Stanton R. Sheetz is chief executive officer. 				   Brands: Dot\'z Bakery, M.T.O., Nova Blue Water, Sheetz Coffee, Sheetz Gasoline, Sheetz Shmiscuit, Sheetz Shmuffin, Subs and Salads','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5382,'Keystone Foods',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Keystone Foods is a processor and distributor of beef and poultry and nonfood items to the quick-service restaurant industry in the U.S. Its clients include McDonald\'s, other restaurants and supermarkets. Outside the U.S., the company operates distribution centers and processing facilities in Europe, Asia, Australia and the Middle East.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5383,'Schwan Food',11,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Schwan Food Company began delivering ice cream to isolated rural families in 1952. Today, Schwan\'s fleet of over 6,000 trucks deliver a line of over 400 food items to household customers in all 48 continental states. Its Global Consumer Brands business unit produces and markets branded frozen pizzas (Tony\'s, Red Baron and Freschetta), desserts (Mrs. Smith\'s and Edward\'s), side dishes and ethnic specialties through retail and club grocery retailers in more than 50 countries. Schwan\'s Food Service business unit supplies frozen specialties, sandwiches and premium desserts to chain restaurants, schools, delicatessens and institutional customers. The company operates processing plants in Georgia, Florida, Minnesota, Kansas, South Carolina, Kentucky, Texas and in Canada, England, France and Germany. 				   Brands: Schwan\'s, Tony\'s, Red Baron, Freschetta, Larry\'s, Pagoda, Minh, Edwards, Mrs. Smith\'s , Chicago Town','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5384,'JR Simplot',10,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Based in Boise, Idaho, JR Simplot is a diversified private food and agricultural products company founded in 1955 by John Richard Simplot. An early pioneer in the production of frozen potatoes, Simplot is a large supplier of French fries to national and regional restaurant chains. Other Simplot products and services include frozen vegetables, beef cattle, processed meat, agricultural fertilizers and animal feed. The company also sells turf and horticultural products.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5385,'Consolidated Elec Distributors',30,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Consolidated Electrical Distributors, an electric-equipment wholesaler, is located in Thousand Oaks, California and has approximately 550 branches throughout the U.S. The company can trace its roots back to 1913, with the formation of Incandescent Supply. In 1958, Incandescent merged with Phillips & Edwards, forming a new company. In 1964, the company changed its name to Consolidated Electrical Distributors. In 1999, the company acquired All-Phase Electric Supply.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5386,'Raley\'s',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in West Sacramento, Calif., Raley\'s owns and operates 129 food stores under the names of Raley\'s, Bel Air Markets, Nob Hill Foods and Food Source in northern California and Nevada. Thomas P. Raley founded the company in 1935. 				   Brands: Bel Air Markets, Food Source, Nob Hill Foods, Raley\'s','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5387,'JF Shea',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','JF Shea, of Walnut, Calif., is a diversified construction company that builds homes and commercial facilities. The firm also manages commercial buildings and produces concrete. The company is one of the oldest privately held construction businesses in the U.S. and currently has eight divisions: Shea Homes, Shea Properties, JF Shea Construction, JF Shea Redding, Reed Manufacturing, Venture Capital, Shea Mortgage and Blue Star. Famous projects include the Golden Gate Bridge, the Hoover Dam and the Bay Area Rapid Transit System (BART).','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5388,'Swift Transportation',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Swift Transportation operates the largest truckload fleet in the United States. The company serves shippers and has operations in Mexico as well. Founder Jerry Moyes took the company private in 2007 by buying the remaining 61% of Swift that he and his family did not already own.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5389,'Structure Tone',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in New York City, Structure Tone develops commercial and corporate properties, providing general contracting, construction management and project management services. Lou Marino and Patrick Donaghy founded Structure Tone in 1971; today their families own the company. Structure Tone serves the financial and commercial industries, as well as the academic, mission critical, retail, science and technology, hospitality, healthcare, residential, law, and government sectors.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5390,'Ashley Furniture Industries',27,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','In 1945, Carlyle Weinberger started Ashley Furniture as a sales operation in Chicago. In 1970, Weinberger invested in Ron Wanek\'s Arcadia Furniture, a manufacturing business in Arcadia, Wisconsin. The two businesses became Ashley Furniture in 1976. The company manufactures living room, dining room, bedroom, entertainment, home office furniture and other home furnishings. The company sells its products through dealers and through more than 100 independently owned Ashley HomeStores. 				   Brands: Ashley, Ashley Casegoods, Ashley Home Stores, Ashley Upholstery, Millenium','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5391,'Amsted Industries',17,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded as American Steel Foundries in 1902 via the combination of eight steel foundries in the East and Midwest, the company changed its name to Amsted Industries in 1962. At one time, Amsted dealt principally with railroad companies, producing a variety of cast-steel components. The current product lineup ranges from cooling towers and ductile pressure pipe to steel railroad wheels and powdered metal products. Amsted went private via an employees stock ownership buyout in 1986.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5392,'Golub',5,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Golub Corp. owns and operates 116 Price Chopper supermarkets in six states&mdash;Connecticut, Massachusetts, New Hampshire, New York, Pennsylvania and Vermont. Brothers William and Bernard Golub founded the company in 1932 when they opened the first self-service supermarket in upstate New York. The Golub family owns 45% of the Schenectady, New York grocery chain; employees own the remaining 55% of the company. 				   Brands: Price Chopper, Mini Chopper','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5393,'Glazer\'s Wholesale Drug',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Glazer\'s Wholesale Drug is a large distributor and wholesaler of wine, distilled spirits and malt beverages. The company operates in twelve states: Arizona, Arkansas, Illinois, Indiana, Iowa, Kansas, Louisiana, Mississippi, Missouri, Ohio, Oklahoma and Texas.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5394,'Grant Thornton International',28,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','From its modest beginnings as Alexander Grant & Company in 1924, Grant Thornton International has become one of the six global accounting, tax, and business advisory firms. Headquartered in Chicago, Illinois, Grant Thornton International today serves clients through 521 offices in 113 countries.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5395,'Schreiber Foods',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1945, Schreiber Foods of Green Bay, Wisconsin, is the largest privately held producer of cheese, the second-largest producer of cream cheese and a yogurt producer. The company distributes products from 20 plants in the United States, Germany, Mexico, India and Brazil. 				   Brands: American Heritage, Cache Valley, Clearfield, Cooper, Raskas','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5396,'Vistar',6,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Vistar is a national foodservice distributor with 35 supply centers and two core divisions: Roma Foods, which focuses primarily on the independent pizza, Italian, Mexican and other selected restaurant operators; and Specialty Markets, which distributes food to local and national vending, theater, office coffee, and specialty retail operators. Roma Foods sells its products under the Roma, Piancone, Assoluti and Luigi brands. Vistar Specialty includes candy, snack, and convenience foods and beverages. The Company was a unit of International Multifoods until September 2002, when Wellspring Capital and certain members of management acquired this business. A recapitalization of the company in 2007 resulted in 67% ownership by Blackstone Group, 22% ownership by Wellspring, and 11% ownership by existing management.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5397,'WinCo Foods',11,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','WinCo Foods operates 57 grocery stores in five states (Washington, Idaho, California, Nevada and Oregon). A typical store is 80,000 square feet in size. WinCo also operates a new 900,000 square foot distribution facility in Woodburn, Oregon and a 100,000 square foot nonfood distribution center in Myrtle Creek, Oregon. In 1985, its Employee Stock Ownership Plan (ESOP) purchased WinCo from the founding family. 				   Brands: WinCo Food Stores','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5398,'ABC Supply',10,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','With over 340 distribution centers in 45 states, plus the District of Columbia, this Beloit, Wisconsin supplier of exterior building products has tripled in size since 1996. ABC Supply is now the largest roofing and vinyl siding wholesale distributor in the U.S. Also known as American Builders & Contractors Supply Co., the company uses a fleet of over 3,300 delivery units to bring materials directly to contractors and builders.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5399,'E&J Gallo Winery',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Ernest and Julio Gallo started E&J Gallo Winery in 1933. Julio, who died in 1993, was in charge of making the wine, and Ernest was in charge of selling it. Ernest remains chairman of the company. Gallo wines include Turning Leaf, Twin Valley, Single Vineyard, Red Bicyclette and Ecco Domani. The company has four wineries in California. 				   Brands: Gallo Sonoma County, Gallo Twin Valley, Gallo of Sonoma, Single Vineyard, Turning Leaf','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5400,'DeBruce Grain',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1978,DeBruce Grain, stores, handles and sells grain and fertilizer. Headquartered in Kansas City, Missouri, the company operates high-speed grain handling facilities, grain elevators, fertilizer distribution terminals and retail fertilizer operations in the United States and Mexico.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5401,'Linens \'N Things',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Clifton, New Jersey, Linens \'n Things is a national retailer of home furnishings merchandise, selling a broad range of housewares and house accessories. Stores sell brands such as Braun, Krups, Calphalon, Waverly and Laura Ashley. The company operates 571 stores in 47 states and six Canadian provinces. Publicly traded until early 2006, Linen \'n Things was acquired by private equity firm Apollo Management. Robert J DiNicola is the new chief executive.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5402,'Alex Lee',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1931, and based in Hickory, North Carolina, Alex Lee is a holding company whose primary operations are in food distribution and retailing. Subsidiaries include Merchants Distributors, Lowe\'s Food Stores, Consolidated Services and Institution Food House. Boyd L. George is chairman and chief executive officer.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5403,'Gilbane',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Gilbane is a full-service construction and real estate development company offering innovative facility solutions including site selection, financing, programming, construction, and relocation management. The firm is involved in important public and private construction markets: higher education and K-12 schools, life sciences, healthcare, corporate, mission critical, sports and recreation, criminal justice and transportation. Founded in 1873, the fourth-generation, family-owned company has annual revenues of more than $3 billion and employs approximately 2,000 people. Gilbane\'s corporate headquarters are located in Providence, Rhode Island, and it has offices in 28 cities across the United States and in Puerto Rico. Some of Gilbane\'s best-known projects include the U.S. Capital Visitors Center, National World War II Memorial, National Air and Space Museum and Vietnam Veterans Memorial in Washington, D.C. and buildings in Lake Placid, New York for the 1980 Winter Olympics.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5404,'Scoular',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Scoular Co., of Omaha, Nebraska, is an employee-owned agricultural trading company specializing in the handling of grain, feed and food ingredients. Privately held since its incorporation in 1927, Scoular has offices in 18 U.S. states, as well as facilities in Canada and Mexico.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5405,'Sports Authority',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Sports Authority opened its first sporting goods store in Florida in 1987. The company now operates 419 sporting goods stores in 45 states under the Sports Authority brand. In May 2006, Sports Authority became a private company via a buyout from management and private equity firm Leonard Green & Partners. Corporate headquarters are in Englewood, Colorado.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5406,'Parsons',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Parsons is an engineering and construction company involved in diverse markets such as infrastructure, transportation, advanced technologies, telecommunications, aviation, commercial, water and wastewater, environmental, planning, industrial manufacturing, pharmaceuticals, data management, vehicle inspection and homeland security. Parsons provides technical and management solutions to federal, regional, and local government agencies as well as private industries worldwide.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5407,'Bass Pro Shops',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Bass Pro Shops sell outdoors equipment at 38 retail stores, an internet site and through over 100 million catalogs distributed yearly. Retail stores are located in 21 states and Canada. The site of the original store in Springfield, Missouri brings in over 4 million visitors yearly and is the state\'s top tourist attraction. 				   Brands: Bass Pro Shops, Outdoor World, Redhead, Uncle Buck\'s, Worldwide Sportsman, XPS','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5408,'Mansfield Oil',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1957, Mansfield Oil is a nationwide transportation and power generation fuels wholesaler. The company delivers more than 1.5 billion gallons of petroleum products annually to customers throughout the United States. Headquarters are in Gainesville, Georgia.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5409,'Reader\'s Digest Association',27,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founders DeWitt and Lila Wallace published their first issue of Reader\'s Digest in 1922. Now Reader\'s Digest is the largest-selling magazine in the world, appearing in 50 editions and 21 languages. The company also sells more than 25 other magazines, including Every Day with Rachael Ray and Taste of Home. An investor group led by Ripplewood Holdings acquired the company for $1.6 billion in 2007.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5410,'Travelport',10,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Travelport travel companies offer services to businesses and consumers. Its brands include Galileo, a global distribution system; Gulliver\'s Travel Associates, a wholesaler of travel content; and consumer travel websites Orbitz and Cheaptickets.com in the US, and ebooker.com in Europe. The Blackstone Group bought the company from Cendant for $4.3 billion in a sale that closed in August 2006. Revenue figure excludes publicly traded subsidiary Orbitz.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5411,'Fry\'s Electronics',17,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','In 1985, brothers John, David, and Randy Fry and a fourth partner, Kathy Kolder, founded Fry\'s Electronics in Sunnyvale, California to provide a one-stop shopping experience for the hi-tech person\'s needs. Twenty years later, Fry\'s is doing business online and in nine states with 34 stores, each decked out in fantasy themed motifs. 				   Brands: Fry\'s Electronics','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5412,'Golden State Foods',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Golden State Foods, based in Irvine, California, is a food processor and distributor to the food service industry. The company provides one-stop shopping to over 2,900 McDonald\'s Restaurants. As a food processor, GSF produces frozen beef patties, cooked beef crumbles, pork sausage, sandwich sauces, salad dressings, ketchup, dipping sauces, dessert toppings and other food items. Golden State supplies over 150 products to 45 countries, and has foreign operations in Egypt, Australia and Malaysia. In 2004 the company completed a deal by Wetterau Associates, the St. Louis investment group led by GSF Chief Executive Officer Mark Wetterau, to purchase the 50.3% stake in the company formerly held by business partner, Yucaipa Companies. 				   Brands: Chef Gold','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5413,'Winwholesale',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','WinWholesale is a wholesale distributor of parts and equipment for plumbing, industrial pipes, valves and fittings, heating, cooling, electrical, electronics, water works, pumps and fasteners. The company also provides business services and computer and hardware solutions to the wholesaling industry. WinWholesale has more than 530 U.S. companies that serve professional contractors, plant maintenance personnel and others. Headquarters are in Dayton, Ohio.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5414,'Milliken & Co',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Milliken & Co. traces its roots to the Deering Milliken Co., a woolen fabrics jobbing firm founded in Portland, Maine by Seth Milliken and William Deering in 1865. The company now has 60 manufacturing facilities worldwide, producing 38,000 textile, carpet and chemical products for use in apparel, automotive interior and household furnishings and other applications.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5415,'JE Dunn Construction Group',26,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','John Ernest Dunn, Sr. founded this company in 1924. Today, JE Dunn Construction consists of six construction companies, with 17 offices across the country. The company builds a wide range of industrial, commercial, retail and residential facilities&mdash;ranging from commercial offices and warehouses to hotels, multi-unit residences, prisons, and sports and entertainment facilities. 				   Brands: JE Dunn Group','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5416,'Sammons Enterprises',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','In 1962, Charles A. Sammons started Sammons Enterprises, a financial services and insurance company. The primary holdings of the Dallas, Texas company include Midland National Life Insurance Co. in Sioux Falls, South Dakota and North American Co. in Chicago. It also owns Briggs Industrial Equipment, Briggs Construction Equipment and Grove Park Inn. Sammons Enterprises is an employee-owned company.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5417,'Tower Automotive',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1993 as R.J. Tower Corporation, Tower Automotive is a global designer and producer of auto parts and assemblies used by leading original equipment manufacturers, including, BMW, Chrysler, Honda, Toyota, Volkswagen and Volvo. Products include body structures and assemblies, lower vehicle frames and suspension components. Tower emerged from Chapter 11 in July 2007 as an affiliate of Cerberus Capital Management. The company has 39 facilities in 13 countries in North and South America, Europe and Asia.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5418,'Quintiles Transnational',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Quintiles Transnational, headquartered in North Carolina, is the largest pharmaceutical outsourcing services company in the U.S., and one of the world\'s top contract research organizations. The company provides product development and commercial services. Founded in 1982, the company was taken private in 2003 by its chairman and chief executive officer Dennis Gillings.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5419,'Tishman Construction',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1898, Tishman Construction is a builder, developer and facilities manager. Since its creation, its affiliated companies have built over 400 million square feet of space. Tishman\'s most famous projects include the redevelopment of JFK International Airport, the renovation and restoration of Carnegie Hall in New York City, the John Hancock Center in Chicago, the Century City Theme Center in Los Angeles and the Epcot Center in central Florida. Tishman, which built the original World Trade Center towers, will manage the construction of the Freedom Tower in New York City\'s financial center.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5420,'Grocers Supply',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded by the Levit family in 1923, Grocers Supply distributes food and other grocery store products. The company services more than 650 grocery stores, 1,200 convenience stores and 200 schools in a 350-mile radius of Houston. The company\'s headquarters are in Houston, Texas; Max Levit is the chief executive officer. In 2004, Grocers Supply acquired grocery stores chain Fiesta Mart. 				   Brands: Fiesta Mart','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5421,'Golden Living',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Golden Living operates nursing homes and provides services related to rehabilitation therapy, hospice and home health, and temporary staffing. Its Golden LivingCenters division runs 333 skilled nursing sites and 17 assisted living facilities in 23 states. Catering to Golden LivingCenters is Golden Living\'s other big division, Golden Innovations, whose companies include Aegis Therapies, AseraCare Hospice and Home Health, Aedon Staffing, Ceres Purchasing Solutions, and Vizia Healthcare Design Group.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5422,'HP Hood',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','In business for 160 years, HP Hood is a national branded dairy operator and distributor of milk, cultured foods, citrus, extended shelf-life dairy, frozen desserts and non-dairy and specialty drinks. Based in Lynnfield, Massachusetts, the company operates eight brand plant locations and owns Crowley Foods of Binghamton, New York; Kemps, of Minneapolis, Minnesota; and Crystal Cream & Butter Company, of Sacramento. 				   Brands: Carb Countdown, Coffee-mate, Crowley, Heluva Good, Hood, Kemps, LACTAID, Nesquik','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5423,'MGA Entertainment',17,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','MGA Entertainment makes toys and games, dolls, consumer electronics, home d','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5424,'Services Group of America',25,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Services Group of America, located in Scottsdale, Arizona, is a diversified privately held corporation specializing in foodservice distribution and marketing. Founder and owner, Thomas J. Stewart is its chairman and chief executive officer. The company\'s subsidiaries include Food Services of America and Systems Services of America (foodservice distributors); Amerifresh (fresh produce marketer); S&P Meats (custom meat processing, sales and distribution); Development Services of America (commercial real estate development and management) and Misty Isle Farms Natural Black Angus Beef (beef production and sales to foodservice companies). Services Group of America companies provide distribution services to foodservice operators in the 16 western and midwestern states plus Alaska, Hawaii, Georgia, the Pacific Rim and Mexico. 				   Brands: Black Angus beef, Blackstone 1890, Columbia Valley Farms, Della Vite, Elite, Flying Flag, Food Services of America, Madrona Market, Misty Isle Farms Natural Black Beef Angus, Pride, Rio Viejo, Signature, Tender Cut','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5425,'Dot Foods',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Robert F. Tracy founded Dot Foods (originally Associated Dairy Products) in 1960, and the company is still family owned. Dot Foods operates 800 trucks that distribute more than 60,000 products to other food wholesalers in all 50 states. The company has facilities in California, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland, Missouri, New York, Oklahoma and Texas. Corporate headquarters are in Mount Sterling, Illinois.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5426,'Medline Industries',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Medline, headquartered in Mundelein, Illinois, manufactures and distributes more than 100,000 products to hospitals, extended-care facilities, surgery centers, home care dealers and agencies and other markets. Medline has more than 800 dedicated sales representatives and 56 wound care specialists nationwide to support its broad product line and cost-management services.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5427,'Mervyns',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Hayward, California Mervyn\'s is a large fashion and housewares retailer with 173 stores in 8 states. Founder Mervin Morris, opened his first store in San Lorenzo, California in 1949. The company went public in 1971 and merged with Dayton Hudson in 1978. In September 2004, Target Corporation, formerly known as Dayton Hudson, sold the company for $1.7 billion to an investor group led by Sun Capital Partners, Cerberus Capital Management and Lubert-Adler and Klaff Partners.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5428,'Leprino Foods',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Leprino Foods, based in Denver, is the world\'s largest producer of mozzarella cheese, with nine plants in California, Nebraska, New Mexico, New York, Michigan and Colorado. The firm also operates a plant in Northern Ireland and a plant in Wales, which are both part of a joint venture. The company also manufactures whey protein concentrate for protein bars, smoothies and other uses.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5429,'Rich Products',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','With the creation of the first non-diary topping, Rich\'s Whip Topping, Robert E. Rich founded Rich Products in 1945. The company, still family-owned, is a supplier to the food service, in-store bakery and retail marketplaces. Rich\'s three core business groups: Rich\'s US/Canada, Rich Products and Rich International, sell more than 2,300 products in more than 85 countries, including China, Mexico, India, Korea, Brazil, the U.K., South Africa, Russia, Thailand and Israel. Headquartered in Buffalo, New York, Rich Products also has interests in three professional minor league baseball teams&#8212;the Buffalo Bisons, Wichita Wranglers and Jamestown Jammers. 				   Brands: Allen, Bahama Blast, Bettercreme, Byron\'s Barbecue, Casa DiBertacchi, Coffee Rich, Della Suprema Pizza, Farm Rich, Jon Donaire, Morningstar Food\'s Whipped Topping, Mother\'s Kitchen, Mrs. Rich\'s Bakery, On Top Topping, Rich\'s Whip Topping, Rich-SeaPak, SeaPak, Smoothie Simple','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5430,'Schnuck Markets',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1939, Schnuck Markets, of St. Louis, is still family owned. The company operates 102 supermarkets in Missouri, Illinois, Indiana, Wisconsin, Tennessee, Mississippi and Iowa. Most are combination food and drugstores, which sell dry groceries and packaged foods, over-the-counter drugs, baked goods, seafood, produce, meat and deli products. Ninety-nine stores have in-store full service pharmacies. Most locations also contain florist shops. Scott Schnuck is chief executive officer. 				   Brands: Schnucks, Logli','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5431,'Asplundh Tree Expert',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Asplundh, founded in 1928 by brothers Griffith, Lester and Carl Asplundh, is still family-owned and managed. The company\'s first contract was to trim 500 trees for Pennsylvania Power & Light. Customers now include over 250 electric utilities, telecommunications companies, municipalities, pipelines and railroads in 50 states and four foreign countries. About 70% of revenues come from trimming trees near customers\' lines. Asplundh recently established UtiliCon Solutions Ltd., whose subsidiaries offer a range of utility services, including underground utility location, line construction, meter reading, infrared inspection, utility pole maintenance and GPS mapping.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5432,'General Parts',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Located in Raleigh, N.C., General Parts is a distributor of automotive replacement parts, supplies, tools and equipment for automobiles, trucks and buses, including farm and industrial vehicles. Through 40 distribution centers General Parts supplies 3,400 Carquest Auto Parts stores, 1,600 of which are company-owned. Eighty percent of Carquest\'s revenues come from professional installers, body shops, fleets and farmers. 				   Brands: Carquest','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5433,'Follett',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Follett, based in River Grove, Illinois, provides educational solutions, services, and products to schools and libraries. The company\'s Higher Education Group operates 750 bookstores on college campuses and is a wholesaler of used college textbooks. Follett\'s Education and Distribution Group serves schools and public libraries with textbooks, library books and audiovisual products. Follett\'s Technology Solutions and Distribution Group provides software and digital products to support school libraries.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5434,'McCarthy Building Cos',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','McCarthy, founded in 1864, is one of the oldest general contracting companies in the U.S. In 2002, the company became 100% employee owned. Headquartered in St. Louis, McCarthy maintains full-service regional offices in Phoenix, Arizona; Atlanta, Georgia; Las Vegas, Nevada; Newport Beach, San Diego, San Francisco and Sacramento, California; and Dallas, Texas. McCarthy builds health care facilities, semiconductor plants, corporate facilities, hotels, correctional facilities, entertainment complexes, research laboratories, heavy industrial plants and parking structures.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5435,'Ebsco Industries',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Ebsco Industries is a diversified conglomerate comprised of over forty diverse business units. Its primary businesses include providing journal and magazine subscription services to libraries and corporations and the manufacturing of fishing lures and hunting-related products. Ebsco\'s other operations include commercial printing, publishing, commercial and residential real estate development, steel joist manufacturing, promotional products distribution, other light manufacturing and service-related businesses. The word \"EBSCO\" is an acronym for Elton B. Stephens Co. Stephens and his wife, Alys, founded the company in 1944. The company started out providing the U.S. military with magazines, personalized magazine binders and display stands. Today F. Dixon Brooke, Jr., president and chief executive officer heads the company, and J.T. Stephens remains its chairman. 				   Brands: Ebsco','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5436,'O\'Neal Steel',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','O\'Neal Steel is the United States\' largest family-owned metals service center. It stocks a range of carbon, stainless, and alloy steel, as well other metal products. Processing services include sawing, laser cutting, coil leveling, welding and drilling. The company and its subsidiaries operate in over 60 locations in the United States, United Kingdom and continental Europe.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5437,'Petters Group Worldwide',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded by chief executive Thomas Petters in 1988, Petters Group Worldwide owns or has investments in a variety of companies. Notable holdings include uBid.com, Fingerhut Direct Marketing and Polaroid.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5438,'Quality King Distributors',25,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1960 by Bernard Nussdorf, Quality King Distributors has grown from a small shop in Queens, New York to a large distributor of pharmaceuticals and health and beauty care products. Clients include drugstore and supermarket chains, grocery distributors, wholesale clubs and mass-merchant discounters. Glenn Nussdorf is chief executive of family-owned Quality King. Headquarters are in Ronkonkoma, New York.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5439,'Unigroup',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','UniGroup is a transportation and moving services company. Its main operating units are United Van Lines LLC (founded in 1947), and Mayflower Transit LLC (founded in 1927). Other subsidiaries include Vanliner Insurance, Total Transportation Services, and UniGroup Worldwide. Active agents and senior management of United Van Lines and Mayflower Transit own UniGroup. H. Daniel McCollister is chairman and chief executive; Richard H. McClure is president. Corporate headquarters are in Fenton, Missouri. 				   Brands: United Van Lines, Mayflower Transit','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5440,'Bausch & Lomb',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Rochester, New York, Bausch & Lomb is an international eye healthcare products company. Its core products include soft and rigid gas permeable contact lenses and lens care products, and ophthalmic surgical and pharmaceutical products. The company employees 13,000 people worldwide. Affiliates of Warburg Pincus completed the acquisition of Bausch & Lomb, taking it private in October 2007.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5441,'Mary Kay',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Mary Kay develops, manufactures and markets over 200 personal care products in six categories (body care, color cosmetics, facial skin care, fragrances, nail care and sun protection). More than 1.7 million Mary Kay independent beauty consultants in more than 30 global markets sell its products. Mary Kay Ash started the company in 1963, and it went private in 1985. Mary Kay\'s son Richard Rogers retired as chief executive officer in April 2006 and now serves as the company\'s executive chairman. David Holl succeeded Rogers and now serves as president and chief executive officer. 				   Brands: Mary Kay, Mary Kay InTouch','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5442,'ShopKo Stores Operating',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','James Ruben, a pharmacist, founded this company in 1962. With two divisions located throughout 13 states in the U.S., this Green Bay, Wisconsin business operates more than 135 ShopKo discount stores and three ShopKo Express Rx drug stores. ShopKo discount stores are multi-department retail outlets supplying a range of quality goods and services, ranging from apparel to furniture. The ShopKo Express Rx stores are individual drugstores featuring drive-thru pharmacies, health and beauty aids, cosmetics, fitness products, over-the-counter medications, convenience foods as well as general merchandise. In 1991, the company became public; in December 2005, an affiliate of Sun Capital Partners took the company private.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5443,'Yates Cos',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1964, Yates Companies are commercial builders specializing in industrial, institutional, hospitality, multifamily housing, heavy, marine, electrical and highway projects. The company has branch offices in Alabama, Florida, Georgia, Louisiana, Mississippi, Tennessee and Texas. Its subsidiaries include WG Yates & Sons, Blaine Construction, Jesco Construction, and an electrical unit. Corporate headquarters are in Philadelphia, Mississippi.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5444,'Software House Intl',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The company, founded by Leo Koguan in 1989, is a global procurement outsourcing firm and a business-to-business solutions provider. Software House fulfills orders for over 100,000 hardware and software products. The company has locations in the U.S., Canada, Europe and Asia. 				   Brands: SHI','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5445,'NTK Holdings',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1967, Nortek Holdings, Inc., the primary subsidiary of NTK Holdings, is a manufacturer of residential and commercial buildings products. The company operates two principal segments: residential building products (fans, range hoods, trash compactors, cabinets and more), air conditioning/heating products and home technology equipment (audio/visual, lighting and security control products). Nortek sells its products in the U.S., Canada and Europe. Investment company Kelso & Co., and management took the company private in January 2003. Affiliates of Thomas H. Lee Partners, L.P., together with members of the Company\'s management, purchased the former Nortek Holdings from affiliates and designees of Kelso & Company L.P. in August 2004.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5446,'JM Huber',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1883, JM Huber Corporation is a diversified, multinational supplier of engineered materials, natural resources and technology-based services. Customers span industries ranging from energy and plastics to construction. The company offers total solutions in hydrocelloids, inorganic chemistry, engineered wood composites, food ingredients and other specialties. JM Huber\'s business groups include Huber Engineered Materials, Huber Engineered Woods, Huber Resources, Huber Energy, Shelterwood Financial Services, Demica and CP Kelco. Corporate headquarters are in Edison, New Jersey.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5447,'Petco Animal Supplies',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','A specialty retailer of pet food, supplies and services, Petco operates more than 850 stores in 49 states and the District of Columbia. In October 2006, private equity firms Texas Pacific Group and Leonard Green & Partners took the company private. 				   Brands: Petco','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5448,'Baker & Taylor',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','In business since 1828, Baker & Taylor is a wholesale distributor of books, music, games, and video products to schools, libraries, and retailers. In 2006, New York private equity firm Castle Harlan acquired the company for $455 million.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5449,'Black & Veatch',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Black & Veatch Corporation is a large global engineering, consulting and construction company specializing in infrastructure development in energy, water and government markets. Founded in 1915, Black & Veatch develops tailored infrastructure solutions for clients through conceptual and preliminary engineering services, engineering design, procurement, construction, financial management, asset management, information technology, environmental, security design, and management consulting services. Black & Veatch has completed projects in more than 100 countries. This employee-owned company has more than 100 offices worldwide.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5450,'Demoulas Super Markets',22,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Demoulas Super Markets operates 58 supermarkets and superstores throughout Massachusetts and New Hampshire under the names DeMoulas and Market Basket. The company has warehouse facilities in Lawrence (250,000 square feet) and Tewksbury, Massachusetts (450,000 square feet). Brothers George and Telemachus DeMoulas founded the company in 1917. 				   Brands: DeMoulas Super Markets, Market Basket','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5451,'Rosen\'s Diversified',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Rosen\'s Diversified of Fairmont, Minn. is an agricultural holding company with interests in meatpacking, chemicals and fertilizer. The company merged its meat processing business with American Foods Group in 2005. 				   Brands: Array, Impressive DB','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5452,'Ben E Keith',11,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1906, this private company distributes beer to 60 Texas counties. It is a large distributor of Anheuser-Busch beer in the U.S. Ben E Keith, based in Dallas, Texas, also distributes food to hospitals, schools and restaurants in eight states and is the ninth largest company of its kind in the U.S.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5453,'HealthMarkets',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','HealthMarkets, formerly named UICI, is a life and health insurance provider that focuses on typically underserved individuals, including small business owners and the self-employed. The company helps its customers comparison shop for the best prices and quality. Founded in 1985, HealthMarkets now operates in 44 states.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5454,'Hensel Phelps Construction',26,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1937 by Hensel Phelps, the company is a nationwide general contractor with a diverse range of projects including construction and renovation of commercial office, airport, distribution and industrial, correctional, public assembly, sports, health care, educational, institutional, residential, mixed use, retail, hospitality, mass transportation, entertainment, micro-electronics, research and development and laboratory facilities.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5455,'Truman Arnold Cos',17,NULL,'a:2:{i:0;s:0:\"\";i:1;s:23:\"Truman Arnold Companies\";}','Org','Founded in 1964, Truman Arnold Companies is a petroleum marketer and aviation services provider. With product terminals in Little Rock, Arkansas and Caddo Mills, Texas, its TAC Energy unit sells almost 1.5 billion gallons of refined product annually in 48 states. Its TAC Air unit operates 12 aviation fixed base operations in nine states. Other corporate interests include real estate, ranching and banking.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5456,'Hunt Consolidated/Hunt Oil',26,NULL,'a:3:{i:0;s:0:\"\";i:1;s:16:\"Hunt Oil Company\";i:2;s:8:\"Hunt Oil\";}','Org','The primary business of Hunt Consolidated/Hunt Oil is exploring, developing and refining of oil and gas. Headquartered in Dallas, Texas, Hunt has both domestic and foreign operations. The bulk of the company\'s foreign operations are in Yemen and Canada. Subsidiaries include Hunt Financial Corp., Hunt Investment Corp., Hunt Oil Company, Hunt Overseas Oil Company, Hunt Realty and Hunt Refining Company. Other related entities are Hunt Power, Hunt Private Equities Group and Hunt Ventures. 				   Brands: Hyatt Hotels','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-13 23:43:57',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5457,'WL Gore & Associates',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1958 by Wilbert and Genevieve Gore, WL Gore & Associates develops fluoropolymer-based products for use in apparel, electronics, medical implants and industrial components. Gore brand names include Gore-Tex, Windstopper, and CleanStream. Gore\'s manufacturing operations are in the U.S., Germany, Scotland, Japan and China. 				   Brands: CleanStream, Elixer, Gore-Tex, Remedia','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5458,'Smart & Final',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Smart & Final owns and operates 255 warehouse stores that sell food and food preparation equipment in California, Oregon, Washington, Arizona, Idaho, and northern Mexico. In May 2007, Smart & Final became a private company following its purchase by Apollo Management. Smart & Final tailors its services to the needs of both households and businesses. Etienne Snollaerts is the current president and chief executive.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5459,'Altivity Packaging',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Altivity Packaging, a combination of the assets of Smurfit-Stone\'s Consumer Packaging Division, and Field Container Company, is a manufacturer of consumer packaging products. The company manufactures folding cartons, multiwall and consumer bag packaging, plastic packaging and laminations for a variety of consumer and industrial companies. Altivity also makes high quality, decorative gift boxes for department stores and retail establishments.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5460,'Brookshire Grocery',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Brookshire Grocery originally began in 1928 with three stores as a part of the Brookshire Brothers chain. In 1939, Wood Brookshire broke away his portion and started Brookshire Grocery. In 2001, the company introduced Ol','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5461,'Heico Cos',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Heico Companies is a holding company with varied interests, including construction equipment, steel, telecommunications, plastics and sewer and drain cleaning. Among its individual units are Pettibone, and CopperCom. Michael Heisley founded the company in 1979.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5462,'World Wide Technology',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','World Wide Technology, based in St. Louis, Missouri, provides information technology and supply chain solutions as a value-added reseller of such products and services. The company\'s supply chain solutions consist of a full range of procurement and logistics services, including product warehousing and distribution; equipment staging and configuration; and just-in-time shipping.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5463,'Bashas\'',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1932, Bashas\' Family of Stores is Arizona\'s hometown grocer. The family-owned company operates more than 150 stores in six formats, including AJ\'s Fine Foods, Bashas\' supermarkets, Bashas\' Dine, Food City, Ike\'s Farmer\'s Market, and Sportsman\'s Fine Wine & Spirits. 				   Brands: AJ\'s Fine Foods, Bashas\', Bashas\' Dine Markets, Food City','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5464,'Discount Tire',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','With more than 650 stores in 20 states, Discount Tire is a large retailer of leading-brand and private-label tires. The company operates a majority of its stores under the Discount Tire brand; in Oregon and parts of California, it uses the America\'s Tire banner. In addition, the company also operates Discount Tire Direct, an e-commerce and mail order division. Bruce T. Halle, the current chairman, founded Discount Tire in 1960. 				   Brands: America\'s Tire, Discount Tire, Discount Tire Direct','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5465,'Young\'s Market',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Young\'s Market, of Orange, California, is a wholesaler of wine, spirits, and beer in several western and northwestern states and Alaska. John G. Young founded the company in 1888. In 1990 the Underwood family&mdash;part of the extended Young family&mdash;purchased the company from Young\'s descendants.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5466,'Life Care Centers of America',28,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Forrest L. Preston founded Life Care Centers of America in 1976. The company manages more than 260 assisted and independent living facilities, retirement centers and nursing facilities in 28 states. Life Care also provides home care agency services. Corporate headquarters are in Cleveland, Tennessee.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5467,'JM Smith',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','JM Smith began in 1944 as Smith Drug Company. The Smith Drug Company evolved into a wholesale distributor to over 700 independent pharmacies. Today JM Smith serves the Carolinas and Georgia, providing data processing services. The company created QS/1 Data Systems in 1990, which develops computer systems for pharmacies and home medical equipment providers. Smith Premier Services provides a range of prescription services for employees and insurance carriers. Its online division, CornerDrugstore.com has become an important provider of internet transactions for regional chain pharmacies.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5468,'Delaware North Cos',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Delaware North Companies is one of the world\'s largest hospitality and foodservice providers. Its family of companies includes TD BankNorth Garden, a sports and events facility in Boston, and several companies operating under the Delaware North banner. The latter includes Parks & Resorts, Travel Hospitality Services, Sportservice, International and Gaming & Entertainment. Every year Delaware North serves half a billion customers in the United States, Canada, Australia, New Zealand and the United Kingdom. 				   Brands: America Park N\' Swap, CA One Services, Delaware North Companies Parks & Resorts, Delta Quees Steamboat, FleetCenter, Sportservice, Sportsystems','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5469,'Guitar Center',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Westlake Village, Guitar Center is a chain of musical instrument retailers founded in 1959 by Wayne Mitchell as The Organ Center. The company now operates more than 210 Guitar Center stores across the U.S. Private equity firm Bain Capital bought the company in June 2007.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5470,'Quad/Graphics',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1971, in an abandoned millwork factory in Pewaukee, Wisconsin, Quad/Graphics operates an international network of print production facilities. The company serves the catalog, magazine, book, insert and direct mail markets. Services range from front-end design and photography through digital imaging, printing, list management, finishing and distribution.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5471,'Maines Paper & Food Service',27,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1919, Maines Paper & Foodservice is a foodservice distributor, delivering over 12,700 products to 10,750 customers. Clients include fast food and casual dining restaurants, colleges, hospitals and cruise lines. The Maines family owns the company, headquartered in Conklin, New York.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5472,'Bose',4,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Massachusetts Institute of Technology professor of electrical engineering Dr. Amar G. Bose founded Bose Corporation in 1964. The company manufactures music and home theater systems, and loudspeakers for the home, vehicles and professional venues. Bose also makes noise reduction headsets for aviation and consumer use. 				   Brands: Acoustimass, Bose, Direct/Reflecting, Wave Radio','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5473,'Brasfield & Gorrie',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Brasfield & Gorrie LLC is a general contractor headquartered in Birmingham, Alabama, with regional offices in Atlanta, Georgia; Orlando, Florida; Nashville, Tennessee; and Raleigh, North Carolina. The company provides general contracting and construction-management services to clients throughout the Southeast.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5474,'Red Man Pipe & Supply',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Red Man Pipe & Supply Company is a minority-owned, full-service, multi-store, oilfield and industrial supply company. Lewis Ketchum, a Delaware Native American, founded the company in 1977. The company\'s two main business segments include the distribution of oil country tubular goods and line pipe, and the operation of service and supply centers which distribute maintenance, repair and operating products utilized in the energy industry as well as industrial products consisting of line pipe, valves, fittings and flanges.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5475,'Hunt Construction Group',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Originally established in 1944, the former Huber, Hunt & Nichols became the Hunt Construction Group in 2000. Hunt\'s portfolio encompasses nearly every type of construction project: aviation facilities, advanced technology, colleges and universities, convention centers, government structures, healthcare, hotels and resorts, manufacturing facilities, office buildings, schools, sports arenas and stadiums. Landmark projects include the new Indianapolis International Airport Midfield Terminal; the baseball stadium in Phoenix, Arizona; Case Western Reserve University in Cleveland, Ohio; Procter & Gamble Health Care Research Center in Cincinnati, Ohio; Toyota Center in Houston, Texas; San Francisco City Hall; Conseco Fieldhouse in Indianapolis, Indiana; Merrill Lynch Hopewell Campus in Hopewell, New Jersey; and the LAC+USC Medical Center in Los Angeles, California.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5476,'Bradco Supply',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Bradco Supply distributes roofing, windows, lumber, siding and building materials, including asphalt roof shingles, concrete and clay tile, vinyl windows, wood siding, shutters and skylights. Founded in 1966, the company now has 154 branches, including Wickes Lumber, in 29 states. Bradco also exports material to the Caribbean and Latin America.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5477,'JD Heiskell & Co',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1886 by Jefferson Davis Heiskell, JD Heiskell & Company ranks among the top five feed manufacturers in the U.S.Altogether the company runs a total of 10 operations across 7 states .The Tulare, Calif.-based-firm feed handling assets in Pixley California, Ontario California, Wendell Idaho, Bliss Idaho, Mountain Home Idaho, Wiggins Colorado, Friona Texas, and Portales New Mexico and dynamic trading offices in Elkhorn Nebraska and Minneapolis Minnesota.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5478,'Renco Group',11,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Renco Group of New York City is a diversified holding company with interests in mining, metal production, material handling and other business. Among its subsidiaries are Doe Run Resources, US Magnesium and Unarco Material Handling. The Renco Group owns a 40% stake in defense contractor AM General, maker of the military\'s all-terrain vehicle the Humvee, and its civilian counterpart, the Hummer. Forbes does not include estimated revenues of AM General in its sales estimate for the Renco Group. 				   Brands: HumVee, Hummer','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5479,'SAS Institute',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','SAS Institute provides software and services that enable customers to transform data from all areas of their business into useful information. SAS offers business analytic software solutions to help companies manage their customer relationships, finances, human resources, supply chains, warranty operations and other processes. Headquartered in North Carolina, SAS Institute has over 400 offices worldwide and customers in over 100 countries. 				   Brands: SAS Software','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5480,'Houchens Industries',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Ervin G Houchens founded Houchens Industries as BG Wholesale in 1994. Today the company owns and operates supermarkets under several banners&mdash;such as Houchens, Food Giant, IGA, IGA Express, IGA Crossroads and Piggly Wiggly. Houchens Industries also has interests in a wide range of other businesses, including warehousing, construction, recycling and insurance. Corporate headquarters are in Bowling Green, Kentucky. 				   Brands: Food Giant, Foodland, Houchens Markets, IGA, IGA Express, Jr. Food Stores, Malibu, Montclair, Piggly Wiggly, Riveria, Save-A-Lot, Sonoma, Tobacco Shoppes, USA Gold','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5481,'National Gypsum',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Charlotte, North Carolina, National Gypsum is a supplier of wallboard, interior finishing products and cement board to the construction industry. It has a network of 31 plants in North America, as well as its own paper mills and gypsum mines and quarries. 				   Brands: Gold Bond gypsum wallboard and joint treatment compounds','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5482,'Academy Sports & Outdoors',25,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Academy Ltd., which does business as Academy Sports & Outdoors, owns and operates 95 sports and outdoors goods stores across the South and Southeast. The company traces its beginning to 1938 when founder Max Gochman opened the Academy Tire Shop in San Antonio, Texas. After a few years, Gochman began selling military surplus in his shop. In 1973, his son, Arthur Gochman, began developing similar stores in Houston, Texas. In the early 1980\'s, Academy added sports and outdoors items to its assortment of products, and the company evolved into a full line sporting goods store. 				   Brands: Academy Sports & Outdoors','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5483,'Holiday Cos',11,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Holiday Companies, founded 1928, owns and operates over 320 corporate-owned gasoline and convenience stores, and franchises over 100 other stores under the Holiday Stationstores name. Stores of the Minneapolis, Minnesota company are located throughout 12 states in the northern and northwestern region of the U.S. Ronald A. Erickson is the chairman and chief executive officer. 				   Brands: Holiday Stationstores','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5484,'Foster Farms',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','In 1939, Max and Verda Foster founded Foster Farms, now the largest poultry processor in California. Headquartered in Livingston, California, the company operates hatcheries, ranches, feed mills, processing plants and delivery systems in California, Oregon and Washington. It also runs Foster Farms Dairy, which processes and distributes 3.8 million gallons of milk a week via eight facilities located throughout California. 				   Brands: Foster Farms','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5485,'Koch Foods',10,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1973, Koch Foods is a poultry processor headquartered in Chicago, Illinois. In addition to its processing facilities, the company operates its own feed mills and hatcheries. Koch markets its products under the Koch Foods, Antioch Farms, Preferred Foods, and Rogers Royal brand names, and other custom and private labels. 				   Brands: Antioch Farms, Koch Foods, Preferred Foods, Rogers Royal','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5486,'Red Chamber Group',17,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Red Chamber Group, of Vernon, Calif. is a large importer, exporter and processor of seafood and other fine foods. The Group\'s companies include Neptune Foods, OFI Markesa International, Tampa Bay Fisheries, Kitchens of the Oceans and Mid-Pacific Seafoods, California Specialty Cheese Company and the Ice Creamery. 				   Brands: Captain Neptune, Fisherman\'s Choice, Fresh From the Seas, Markesa, Neptune, Ocean Bistro, Ocean Cafe, Ocean Superior','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5487,'D&H Distributing',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1918, D&H Distributing is a full-line, multi-national distributor of computers, consumer electronics, educational products and security products. Clients range from large, national accounts to small independent businesses. Corporate headquarters are in Harrisburg, Pennsylvania, with shipping locations in Harrisburg, California, Florida, Illinois and Texas.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5488,'Drummond',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Using mules hauling small carloads of coal from the mines, Heman Drummond founded this Birmingham, Alabama company in 1935. Drummond now operates mines in Alabama and Colombia. The company mines both steam coal (for sale to electric utilities) and metallurgical coal. Drummond\'s ABC Coke plant in Tarrant, Alabama is the largest single producer of foundry coke in the U.S. The firm\'s real-estate arm is involved in the construction of commercial and residential developments.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5489,'Rooms To GO',11,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','After selling Seaman\'s Furniture in 1987, Jeffrey and Morty Seaman founded Rooms To Go in 1991. Now one of the nation\'s largest furniture retailers, Rooms To Go has five distribution centers and more than 100 furniture stores in Florida, Georgia, North Carolina, South Carolina, Tennessee, Texas, Alabama, Mississippi and Louisiana. The company\'s Rooms To Go Kids stores specialize in children\'s furniture. 				   Brands: Rooms To Go, Rooms To Go Kids','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5490,'Landmark Communications',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Norfolk, Va., Landmark Communications does business in television broadcasting, cable programming, and newspapers, as well as educational and marketing services. Notable holdings include the Weather Channel, The Virginian-Pilot and the Roanoke Times. Tennessee native Samuel L. Slover founded the company in 1905.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5491,'Shamrock Foods',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Shamrock Foods is a full-line food distributor. The company distributes fresh and frozen foods, specialty items and gourmet foods to food service customers as well as dairy products to supermarkets and convenience stores in the southwestern states. Shamrock also manufactures its own dairy products under the Shamrock Farms label. 				   Brands: Rattleshakes, Shamrock Farms, Sunland','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5492,'McWane',6,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Based in Birmingham, Alabama, McWane makes ductile iron pipe, fire hydrants, propane tanks, water valves and related products. Among the company\'s subsidiaries are Clow Water Systems, Tyler Pipe, Canada Pipe, and Manchester Tank & Equipment.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5493,'Marsh Supermarkets',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','In 1974, a Marsh Supermarket in Troy, Ohio, became the first supermarket in the world to process a purchase using a modern point-of-sale barcode scanner. Today, Marsh Supermarkets owns and operates supermarkets, convenience stores, florists, and catering and banquet services in Indiana and Ohio. Its supermarkets include retail operations in both discount and high-end concepts. Sun Capital Partners, through its affiliate MSH Supermarkets, completed its acquisition of Marsh Supermarkets in September 2006.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5494,'McJunkin',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1921 and based in Charleston, West Virginia, McJunkin distributes industrial pipe, valves, fittings, and specialty products to a broad range of industries. Subsidiaries include McJunkin Appalachian Oilfield Supply, McJunkin-Nigeria Ltd., and McJunkin-Puerto Rico.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5495,'Berwind',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1874 as a coal mining company, Berwind, of Philadelphia Penn., now manages a portfolio of companies doing business in specialty chemicals, office and craft supplies, natural resources, and real estate. Among its holdings: Elmer\'s Products, which sells the well-known glue. 				   Brands: Elmer\'s Products','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5496,'Warren Equities',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Warren Equities&mdash;a holding company for six separate entities&mdash;is one of the largest independent gasoline and convenience store marketers in the northeastern U.S. and one of the largest independent wholesale petroleum marketers in the Northeast. Warren Equities also distributes tobacco, groceries and confectionary products in New England, and provides environmental services. The company employs 1961 people. 				   Brands: Xtra Mart','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5497,'Catalent Pharma Solutions',25,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','In April 2007, the Blackstone Group acquired the Pharmaceutical Technologies and Services segment of Cardinal Health and formed Catalent Pharma Solutions. Catalent offers a full range of development services for other drug companies, such as pre-clinical support, analytical services, drug delivery development, clinical manufacturing and packaging services.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5498,'Arctic Slope Regional',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Arctic Slope Regional Corporation is a diversified company with subsidiaries providing energy services, petroleum refining and marketing, engineering and construction, technical services for government customers, and natural resource development. ASRC is a private, for profit, corporation representing the business interests of the Arctic Slope I','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5499,'LPL Financial Services',22,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','LPL Financial Services is the largest independent brokerage firm in the US. In 1989, Linsco (Boston) and Private Ledger (San Diego) merged to form LPL Financial Services. The company is self-clearing and provides services in stocks and bonds, mutual funds, commodities, options, annuities, real estate investment trusts (REITs), and other investment vehicles. LPL supports over 10,000 independent registered representatives at more than 6,000 branch offices nationwide.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5500,'Conair',6,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in East Windsor, New Jersey, Conair is a manufacturer and distributor of small kitchen appliances, and professional and personal beauty products. Conair\'s important brands include Conair, Jheri Redding, Cuisinart, Interplak, BaByliss, Sc','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5501,'Parsons Brinckerhoff',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:11:\"PB Americas\";}','Org','Parsons Brinckerhoff (PB), founded in 1885, is one of the oldest engineering consulting firms in the U.S. The company employs more than 10,000 professionals in more than 150 corporate and project offices worldwide. Parsons Brinckerhoff provides multidisciplinary planning, engineering, program and construction management, design and build, operations and maintenance services for transportation infrastructure, buildings, power facilities and other infrastructure projects in both the public and private sectors.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5502,'Swinerton',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Swinerton\'s family of companies provides general contracting, construction management, design-build and property management services to developers, architects, and public and private owners of office buildings, hotels, health care facilities, sporting facilities, industrial plants and clean rooms. Founded in 1888, Swinerton is an employee-owned business with more than 1,260 staff members throughout the western United States.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5503,'Crown Equipment',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Crown Equipment manufactures heavy-duty electric lift trucks (forklifts). Founded in 1945 by Carl H. Dicke and his son James F. Dicke, the company started out as a manufacturer of temperature controls for coal-burning furnaces. Later it diversified into making forklifts. In the United States, Crown has 39 factory-owned sales and service operations, and 64 independent dealers. The company has 10 manufacturing plants located in the U.S., Germany, Mexico, Australia and Ireland. Corporate headquarters are located in New Bremen, Ohio; regional headquarters are in Munich, Germany, and Sydney, Australia.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5504,'Ardent Health Services',22,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Ardent Health Services operates 12 acute care hospitals, providing a full range of medical and surgical services to patients ranging from children to adults. Located in Nashville, Tenn., the company is majority owned by investment company Welsh, Carson, Anderson & Stowe.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5505,'Zachry Construction',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Zachry Construction is an industrial and civil construction and maintenance company headquartered in San Antonio, Texas. Founded in 1924, as a road-building company, the business expanded into other industrial construction projects, including facilities for utilities, processing companies and dams. Zachry also has diverse operations in cement, aggregates, ranching, real estate and hospitality.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5506,'Tang Industries',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Tang Industries is a diversified holding company based in Las Vegas, Nevada. Through its operating subsidiaries and affiliates, Tang Industries is involved in steel service centers, steel stamping, scrap trading, aluminum extrusions, die casting and recycling, metal fabrication, office furniture manufacturing, pharmaceutical research and various investment activities. Cyrus Tang is chairman, president and chief executive officer.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5507,'Rexnord',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, Rexnord is a worldwide manufacturer of highly engineered precision motion technology products, primarily focused on power transmission. Products include flattop chains, industrial bearings, industrial chains, couplings and gears, and aerospace bearings and seals. Formerly a subsidiary of Invensys, the Carlyle Group acquired Rexnord in 2002. In 2006 Apollo Management bought Rexnord. The company has approximately 7,100 employees worldwide.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5508,'Soave Enterprises',17,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Detroit-based Soave Enterprises is a holding company formed in 1998. The company\'s focus is in steel processing and in the scrap metal business. Other interests include industrial and remediation services, real estate development, beverage distribution, auto dealerships, and logistics and inventory management. Anthony Soave is chief executive.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5509,'Latham & Watkins',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:20:\"Latham & Watkins LLP\";}','Org','Latham & Watkins is a global, full-service law firm specializing in corporate finance, merger and acquisitions, technology law and complex business litigation. Founded in 1934, Latham & Watkins has over 2,100 lawyers in 24 offices worldwide. Latham & Watkins is one of the 10 largest law firms in the world.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany,LobbyingFirm',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5510,'Hobby Lobby Stores',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Arts and crafts king Hobby Lobby Stores operates over 390 stores in 32 states. The company\'s stores stock more than 60,000 items including arts and crafts supplies, fashion fabrics, baskets, silk flowers, party supplies, furniture and home accent. Chief Executive David Green founded the company 1972. 				   Brands: Endless Possibilities, Hobby Lobby Creative Centers, Fashion Gear','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5511,'Verso Paper',11,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Verso Paper consists of the former Coated and Supercalendered Paper division of International Paper, which International Paper sold in August 2006 to the private equity firm Apollo Management for $1.4 billion. Verso primarily manufactures paper for the magazine and catalog industry.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5512,'Hoffman',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1922, Hoffman is a construction manager and general contractor operating in the Northwest U.S. An employee-owned company, Hoffman provides project management, field supervision and design-build services for commercial, medical, institutional, industrial and high-technology clients. Hoffman\'s project resume spans from airports to semiconductor factories. The company tackles projects costing less than $1 million to those over $100 million.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5513,'Oxbow',5,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Oxbow\'s primary businesses are the mining and marketing of energy and bulk commodities such as coal, natural gas, petroleum, metallurgical and calcined coke. The company markets petroleum coke, a byproduct of the oil refinery process. Uses for petroleum coke include power generation, cement kilns, sugar mills and aluminum manufacturing. The company trades in other carbon and industrial products such as coal, gypsum, bauxite, and clinker. William Koch founded the company in 1983.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5514,'Reynolds and Reynolds',21,NULL,'a:2:{i:0;s:0:\"\";i:1;s:24:\"Reynolds & Reynolds Inc.\";}','Org','Reynolds and Reynolds Company provides software and services designed for the automobile industry. In October 2006, automobile management systems dealer became a private company when it merged with Universal Computer Services. The combined entity will market products under the Reynolds and Reynolds brand name, and have headquarters in Kettering, Ohio.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5515,'US Oil',6,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1950, US Oil Company is a family of businesses that operates as a marketer of petroleum products and a wholesale distributor of automotive parts and tires, and heating, ventilating and air conditioning equipment and supplies. Headquartered in Combined Locks, Wisconsin, its primary operations are in the upper Midwest region of the United States and include 19 Express Convenience Centers.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5516,'Barnes & Noble College Booksellers',34,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Barnes & Noble College Bookstores owns and operates nearly 500 campus bookstores that sell textbooks, collegiate clothing, emblematic merchandise and school supplies. The company also markets books and related supplies via the Internet. The company is owned by chairman Leonard Riggio. 				   Brands: Barnes & Nobles College Bookstores','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5517,'Viewsonic',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','James Chu founded ViewSonic in 1987 as Keypoint Technology. For the first ten years, the company primarily focused on selling CRT monitors to businesses. Today, the company is a well-known provider of computer LCD monitors, LCD TVs, projectors and peripherals, as well as advanced mobile and wireless products, such as ruggedized PDAs and wireless displays. Headquartered in Walnut, California, ViewSonic has offices in the U.K., France, Germany, Taiwan, China and Canada. 				   Brands: Optiquest, ViewSonic','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5518,'DPR Construction',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','DPR Construction, Inc. is a national commercial contractor and construction manager specializing in technically challenging and environmentally complex projects. It builds advanced technology, biopharmaceutical, corporate office, healthcare facilities, and buildings that have a special emphasis on energy and environmental efficiency. The company has offices in Arizona, California, Georgia, Texas and Virginia.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5519,'American Tire Distributors Holdings',35,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','With roots going back to 1935, American Tire Distributors has 73 tire distribution centers in 36 states. The company also distributes and retails aftermarket wheels, parts, accessories and automotive service equipment. 				   Brands: Dynatrack, ICW Racing, Magnum, Pacer, Regal, Winston','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5520,'Global Aero Logistics',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','ATA Airlines emerged from bankruptcy in 2006 following a restructuring. As part of its reorganization, the company changed its name to Global Aero Logistics. It formerly operated a major hub at Chicago\'s Midway Airport and a minor hub at Indianapolis, but now operates a largely decentralized network that connects cities served by Southwest Airlines to non-Southwest cities. It also runs a substantial charter transport business.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5521,'SSA Marine',10,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1949, SSA Marine is the world\'s largest U.S.-owned container terminal operator. The company has 120 locations worldwide but operates primarily on the West Coast of the United States.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5522,'AG Spanos Cos',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','AG Spanos Cos. builds apartments and housing communities in the U.S. Corporate headquarters are in Stockton, Calif.; construction division offices are in Florida, Georgia, Nevada and California. Chairman and owner Alex G. Spanos also owns the San Diego Chargers, a National Football League team.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5523,'Vought Aircraft Industries',26,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Vought Aircraft Industries is a descendant of one of the pioneer companies in the aviation industry. Under the ownership of Carlyle Group since July 2000, Vought is one of the largest independent suppliers of airplane parts. Headquartered in Dallas, Texas, the company provides wings, fuselage subassemblies, thrust reversers and other components for prime manufacturers of aircraft. Vought also has operations in Hawthorne and Brea, California; Grand Prairie, Texas; Stuart, Florida; Milledgeville, Georgia; Nashville, Tennessee; North Charleston, South Carolina; and Everett, Washington.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5524,'Knowledge Learning',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Knowledge Learning Corporation, started in 1983 as Children\'s Discovery Centers, is a national early childhood care and education company, serving 300,000 children in the U.S. The company operates through nearly 1,900 community centers, 600 school-partnership sites and 123 employer-partnership centers.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5525,'David Weekley Homes',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','David Weekley Homes is a homebuilding and design company founded in 1976 by current chairman, David Weekley. The company specializes in the construction of upscale single-family homes in Texas, Colorado, Florida, Tennessee, North Carolina, South Carolina, Georgia, and has recently expanded into Phoenix, Arizona.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5526,'LL Bean',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Leon Leonwood Bean founded the company in 1912 as a means to sell his \"Maine Hunting Shoe.\" Today, LL Bean is one of the largest catalog and online retailers of outdoor specialty goods in the world. The company also sells home furnishings and apparel for men, women and children. In addition to its flagship retail store in Freeport, Maine, which is open 24 hours a day, 365 days a year, the company has 15 factory outlets, a hunting and fishing store, 9 other retail stores in the U.S. and 17 retail stores in Japan. 				   Brands: LL Bean','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5527,'Pella',5,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1925 as Rolscreen Company, and well known for its \"disappearing\" window screens, Pella manufactures premium-quality wood and vinyl windows and doors. Pella sells its products through lumberyards, home improvement stores and through its own retail outlets. 				   Brands: Pella','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5528,'BE&K',4,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1972, BE&K provides engineering, construction and maintenance services to the manufacturing, industrial, chemical process, hydrocarbons and telecommunications industries. Subsidiary BE&K companies include BE&K Engineering and Construction Group, providing engineering, construction and maintenance services to customers in both the U.S. and internationally; BE&K Building Group, a general contractor specializing in healthcare, education, entertainment, food, general manufacturing, office and retail; and BE&K Federal Group, a general contractor working with various agencies of the Federal government. Among other BE&K subsidiaries: North Star Communications Group, providing wireline, wireless and network installation services; and Allstates Technical Services, providing contract staffing personnel for the engineering, information technology and telecommunications industries. Domestic offices are located in Birmingham, Alabama; Newark, Delaware; Raleigh, North Carolina; and Houston, Texas. International offices are located in Finland, Poland and Russia.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5529,'Dart Container',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Although its roots go back to Dart Manufacturing Company, a small machine shop started in 1937, the foam cup business started in 1963, with the founding of Dart Container by William F. Dart. Today, the company manufactures polystyrene foam cups and other disposable food-service materials in six countries.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5530,'MA Labs',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1983, MA Laboratories distributes computer components, specializing in memory modules. MA Labs distributes a wide range of PC hardware and software including central processing units, motherboards, storage products, optical drives, video cards, networking equipment, monitors, input devices and notebook systems.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5531,'Newegg.Com',10,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 2001, Newegg.com is an online retailer of computer hardware, software, and consumer electronics. With more than 8 million registered customers, it specializes in catering to the tech-savvy crowd that builds and repairs computers themselves. Headquartered in City of Industry, California, Newegg owns 8 warehouses in 3 states, offices in Shanghai and Chengdu, and a global product management center in Taipei, China.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5532,'Plastipak Holdings',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Plastipak Packaging was founded in 1967 and supplies containers and packaging products to leading consumer products companies. Its manufacturing facilities operate in nine U.S. states: Alabama, California, Florida, Illinois, Louisiana, Massachusetts, Michigan, Ohio and Texas. The company also operates in Europe and South America.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5533,'William Lyon Homes',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','William Lyon Homes and its joint ventures have sold over 68,000 new homes since the founding of its predecessor in 1956, making it one of the largest homebuilders in the United States. The company designs, constructs and sells single-family detached and attached homes in five geographic divisions: Southern California, Northern California, San Diego, California, Arizona and Nevada.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5534,'Camac International',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Camac International and its subsidiaries are primarily involved in the exploration, production, and trading of crude oil for markets in Africa and Europe, and the wholesale trading of electric power and natural gas in the United States. Camac also provides transportation services in South Africa. Founded in 1986 and headquartered in Houston, Texas, the company has offices in Columbia, England, South Africa, and founder and chief executive Kase L. Lawal\'s birthplace, Nigeria.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5535,'GNC',3,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','General Nutrition Centers, founded in 1935 by David Shakarian, who opened a Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania health food store called Lackzoom. In the 1960s, the company changed the name of its outlets to General Nutrition Centers. Today General Nutrition is the largest global specialty retailer of vitamin, mineral, herbal and sports nutrition supplements, as well as many personal care and related products. GNC operates or franchises more than 5,900 retail outlets globally.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5536,'ContiGroup Cos',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','ContiGroup Companies, headquartered in New York, has operations in cattle feeding, and poultry and pork production. Wayne Farms, the fifth largest poultry company in the United States, is ContiGroup\'s largest business. Its Five Rivers Ranch Cattle Feeding, a 50-50 joint venture with publicly traded Smithfield Foods, is one of the world\'s largest feedlot enterprises. The company has an investment arm called ContiInvestments. Chief Executive Paul Fribourg and his family own the company.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5537,'Haworth',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Holland, Michigan, Haworth is one of the nation\'s largest furniture manufacturers. Products include partitions, desks, chairs, tables and storage products. Brands include Berlin, If, Places and X99. Haworth, a family-owned company, has roots going back to 1948.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5538,'Ilitch Holdings',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Detroit, Ilitch Holdings\' primary operation is Little Caesar Enterprises, a pizza restaurant chain. The company opened its first Little Caesar restaurant in 1959 in Garden City, Michigan. Today company-owned and franchised Little Caesar restaurants operate in all 50 states as well as locations abroad. Other holdings include two professional sports teams, the Detroit Tigers (baseball) and Detroit Red Wings (hockey), as well as Olympia Entertainment. The latter unit manages Joe Louis Arena, Comerica Park and other Detroit-area venues and restaurants. 				   Brands: Blue Line Distributing, Detroit Red Wings, Detroit Tigers, Fox Theatre, Little Caesar, Uptown Birmingham 8, Uptown Palladium','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5539,'Pinnacle Foods',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Cherry Hill, New Jersey, Pinnacle Foods Group is a producer and distributor of branded products in the frozen foods and dry foods segment. Its branded foods include Aunt Jemima, Celeste, Duncan Hines, Lender\'s, Log Cabin, Mrs. Butterworth\'s, Mrs. Paul\'s, Open Pitt, Swanson, Van de Kamp\'s, and Vlassic. In March 2006, Pinnacle added Armour Foods to its roster, when it acquired the canned meat company from Dial Corporation. Jeffrey P. Ansell became chief executive in June 2006. In April 2007, private equity group Blackstone purchased the company. 				   Brands: Great Starts, Fun Feast, Vlasic, Open Pit, King\'s Hawaiian, Swanson, Hungry-Man, Traditional Favorite, Potato Topped','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5540,'Crowley Maritime',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1892, Crowley Maritime, based in Oakland, California, is a family- and employee-owned company providing four operating lines of business: liner services, logistics, marine services and petroleum services. Its liner shipping services moves ocean cargo to and from the United States, Alaska, Puerto Rico, the Bahamas, the Caribbean, Central America and Russia. Crowley\'s logistic services include supply chain management and transportation management service. Crowley is the largest independent operator of petroleum barges and tankers in the United States.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5541,'Maritz',6,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Maritz provides marketing research, communications, learning solutions, incentive initiatives, meetings and event management, rewards and recognition, travel management services and customer loyalty programs to companies worldwide. Maritz helps companies train, understand, motivate and reward employees.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5542,'Kum & GO',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1959, Kum & Go owns and operates nearly 450 convenience stores in 13 states&mdash;Iowa, Kansas, Minnesota, Missouri, Montana, Nebraska, North Dakota, Oklahoma, South Dakota, Colorado, Arkansas, Wyoming and Wisconsin. Kum & Go sells its store brand products, such as gourmet coffee, water, beef jerky, potato chips, sandwiches and snack nuts, under the Hiland name. It also offers private label Java Ridge coffee, and Napa Creek and Sea Ridge wines.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5543,'Estes Express Lines',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1931 by W.W. Estes, this company is a multi-regional less-than-truckload carrier that services coast to coast from 185 terminals in 46 states and the Caribbean. Beyond its direct service, Estes Express Lines also covers key commercial markets in Mexico as well as the rest of the U.S., and all of Canada through its membership in the ExpressLink service network. Robey Estes, Jr. is chief executive of this family-owned, Richmond, Virginia company.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5544,'Weitz',5,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Weitz Company is a construction company that provides general contracting, design-build and construction management services to clients throughout the U.S. Started in 1855, the Weitz family owned the company until 1995, at which time management completed an employee buyout. Based in Des Moines, Iowa, Weitz operates in 14 locations across the country.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5545,'Goody\'s Family Clothing',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','With headquarters in Knoxville, Tennessee, this company operates 383 apparel stores in the 21 states in the Southeast, Midwest and Southwest U.S. In January 2006, New York investment firms GMM Capital and Prentice Capital Management purchased the company in a deal that took the company private.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5546,'Sigma Plastics Group',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Based in Lyndhurst, New Jersey., Sigma Plastics Group is a manufacturer of industrial and commercial plastic film. The company, consisting of several film extrusion businesses, produces stretch film, merchandise bags, garment bags and converter-grade packaging, industrial film and bags. 				   Brands: Sigma Stretch Film','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5547,'Apex Oil',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1932, Apex Oil and its affiliates distribute, store, and trade petroleum and petroleum products including asphalt, kerosene, fuel oil and gasoline. The company operates oil terminals mostly along the East and Gulf Coasts.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO `orgs` VALUES (5548,'Towers Perrin',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Stamford, Connecticut, Towers Perrin is a global professional services firm specializing in human resources and management consulting. In human resources, the company provides consulting services in areas such as employee benefits, compensation, communication, change implementation and employee research. Its Tillinghast division provides management and actuarial consulting to the insurance and financial service industries. Towers Perrin also operates a global reinsurance business. The company has offices and business partner locations in the U.S., Canada, Europe, Asia, Latin America, South Africa, Australia and New Zealand. 				   Brands: Tillinghast, Towers Perrin HR Services, Towers Perrin Reinsurance','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5549,'M A Mortenson',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1954, M A Mortenson Company, of Minneapolis, Minn., provides a complete range of services, including planning, development, program management, preconstruction services, general contracting, construction management, design-build, engineering/procurement/construction, maintenance and operations. Its important projects, among others, include the Denver Art Museum, the new baseball stadium for the Minnesota Twins and the Walt Disney Concert Hall in Los Angeles.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5550,'Day & Zimmermann',16,NULL,'a:2:{i:0;s:0:\"\";i:1;s:15:\"Day & Zimmerman\";}','Org','Founded in 1901 and headquartered in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, Day & Zimmermann operates from more than 150 worldwide locations. The company provides architecture, engineering, procurement and construction services; plant maintenance and modification services; manufacturing, storage and demilitarization of ammunition; protective services to government installations, utilities and industrial customers; technology staffing services; and validation services to the pharmaceutical and biopharmaceutical industries. 				   Brands: Day & Zimmerman, Day & Zimmerman NPS, Mason & Hanger Group, Yoh','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5551,'FHC Health Systems',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Norfolk, Virginia\'s FHC Health Systems is a group of companies delivering health care services. Its subsidiaries specialize in managed behavioral health care, alternative treatment services, drug testing, pharmacy benefits management, web-based outcomes tracking and reporting and online medical reports.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5552,'The Kraft Group',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Kraft Group is a family owned holding company, which has interests in five specific areas: the distribution of forest products, paper and packaging manufacturing, sports and entertainment, real estate development and private equity investing. Together, the Rand-Whitney Group and International Forest Products do business in more than 80 countries annually and form one of the largest privately owned paper packaging and distribution companies in the world. The Kraft Group\'s sports and entertainment division owns and operates the New England Patriots (football), the New England Revolution (soccer) and Gillette Stadium. Their real estate development team is developing a 1.3 million square foot lifestyle and entertainment center in Foxborough, Mass., called Patriot Place.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5553,'Buffets',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Started in 1983, Buffets operates and franchises buffet-style restaurants. The Company operates 642 company-owned restaurants and 18 franchised locations in 42 states. In October 2000, the private equity firm Caxton-Iseman Capital took the company private. On November 1, 2006, Buffets merged with Ryan\'s Restaurant Group, forming the second largest restaurant company in the family dining industry. 				   Brands: Country Buffet, Country Roadhouse, Tahoe Joe\'s, Old Country Buffet, Hometown Buffet, Original Roadhouse Grill','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5554,'Barton Malow',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1924, Barton Malow provides design, program and construction management, general contracting, technology and rigging services. The company specializes in building industrial, energy, health care, educational and special-event facilities. Barton Malow is headquartered in Southfield, Michigan, and has regional offices in Detroit and Oak Park, Michigan; Chicago, Illinois; Orlando and Jacksonville, Florida; Baltimore, Maryland; Atlanta, Georgia; Chantilly, Virginia; Phoenix, Arizona; and Columbus, Ohio.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5555,'Les Schwab Tire Centers',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1952 and headquartered in Prineville, Oregon, Les Schwab Tire Centers, one of the largest independent tire companies in the United States, has 333 company-owned stores and 77 franchised stores located mostly in the Pacific Northwest. Founder les Schwab passed away in 2007, at the age of 89. 				   Brands: Les Schwab','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5556,'Great Lakes Cheese',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Great Lakes Cheese, based in Ohio, is a cheese manufacturing and distribution business. In addition to the 60 types of natural and processed cheese the company produces, it also sells imported cheeses. Founded in 1958, Great Lakes operates six processing plants, the majority in the Northeast and Midwest. The company is owned by chairman and founder Hans Epprecht and Great Lakes employees. 				   Brands: Great Lakes Cheese','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5557,'Dunavant Enterprises',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Dunavant Enterprises, of Memphis, Tenn., is one of the largest cotton merchandisers in the world, handling six million bales of U.S. and foreign cotton per year. The company has ginning and warehousing operations and owns a commodity trading company, real estate development companies, a truck brokerage company and various other businesses. Dunavant Enterprises is 99% employee-owned.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5558,'MediaNews Group',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','MediaNews Group publishes 57 daily and about 95 non-daily newspapers in 12 states, with combined daily and Sunday circulation of approximately 2.6 million and 2.9 million, respectively. In August 2006, it acquired four newspapers from McClatchy Co., including the San Jose Mercury News. The company also operates a CBS-affiliate television station in Anchorage, Alaska, and operates radio stations in Texas.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5559,'New Balance Athletic Shoe',25,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','New Balance Athletic Shoe, which began as a company selling arch supports early in the 20th century, makes footwear and apparel for running, walking, cross training, basketball, tennis and adventure. Its brands include New Balance, Brine, Aravon, Dunham, PF Flyers and Warrior Sports. 				   Brands: Aravon, Dunham, New Balance, PF Flyers, Warrior Lacrosse','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5560,'Bain & Co',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1973, Bain & Company is one of the world\'s global business consulting companies. With headquarters in Boston and offices in big cities throughout the world, Bain has worked with thousands of corporations from every economic sector through 37 offices in 24 countries.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5561,'Beall\'s',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','R.M. Beall, Sr., grandfather of the present Chairman and chief executive, Robert M. Beall, II, founded this company in 1915 in Bradenton, Florida. In 1954, E.R. Beall, son of the founder, envisioned a chain of stores and convinced his father to open the second Beall\'s Department Store in Bradenton. This business has grown and evolved steadily since then. In 1987, Beall\'s created the Outlet division for retailing off-price branded merchandise. Today, the Beall family operates over 564 retail store sites across the Sun Belt, from Florida to California. 				   Brands: Beall\'s Department Stores, Beall\'s Outlet, Burke\'s Outlets, My Gift Cottage','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5562,'Jones Day',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:28:\"Jones, Day, Reavis and Pogue\";}','Org','Jones Day is an international law firm with more than 2,100 lawyers in 30 locations around the world. The company provides a full range of legal services, including complex business transactions; single-plaintiff and complex, multi-jurisdictional litigation; tax issues; and a broad range of regulatory matters. Jones Day acts as a principal outside counsel to public and private corporations, financial service companies, investment firms, health care providers, retailers and individuals.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5563,'Big Y Foods',11,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1936, Big Y Foods is a supermarket chain with 55 stores scattered throughout southern New England. Big Y also owns several Table & Vine and Town & Country stores, which sell gourmet foods and liquor. The D\'Amour family owns and operates the company. 				   Brands: Big Y Supermarket, Big Y World Class Market, Table & Vine, Town & Country Liquors','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5564,'Mercedes Homes',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded by housing industry veteran Howard Buescher in 1983, Mercedes Homes, named for Buescher\'s wife, is now the nation\'s largest 100 percent employee-owned homebuilder. The company operates in 130 locations in Florida, Texas, and North and South Carolina and maintains four subsidiary operations, MHI Mortgage, BDR Title, Space Coast Truss and Solid Wall Systems.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5565,'Printpack',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Atlanta, Georgia-based Printpack, founded in 1956 by J. Erskine Love, Jr., is a manufacturer packaging materials for the food, beverage, pharmaceutical and agricultural industries. Consumer companies using Printpack\'s products include Frito-Lay (PepsiCo), Georgia-Pacific, General Mills, Hershey Foods, Kraft, Unilever, Sara Lee, Coca-Cola, Nestle, Del Monte and Dole. Printpack operates 25 manufacturing facilities in the U.S., Mexico and the U.K.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5566,'Concentra Operating',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Serving the occupational, auto, and group healthcare markets, Concentra provides employers, insurers, and payors with services that include employment-related injury and occupational health care, in- and out-of-network medical claims review, access to specialized preferred provider organizations, case management and other cost containment services. Concentra provides services to over 220,000 employers and 1,500 insurance companies, health plans and third party administrators nationwide. Investment company Welsh, Carson, Anderson & Stowe took Concentra private in 1999.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5567,'Honickman Affiliates',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1957, Honickman Affiliates is one of the nation\'s largest private bottlers. The company bottles and distributes Pepsi-Cola, Cadbury Schweppes, Snapple, Mott\'s, SoBe and Coors beverages. It serves Maryland, New Jersey, New York, Ohio and Virginia through 11 facilities.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5568,'Gate Petroleum',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Started by Herbert H. Peyton in 1960, Gate Petroleum operates over 150 service stations with convenience stores in the southeastern United States. The company has other interests in real estate, construction materials, and clubs and a resort in Florida. Corporate headquarters are in Jacksonville, Florida. 				   Brands: Gate','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5569,'Wirtz',5,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Wirtz Corporation owns and manages liquor distributorships. The company also owns the Chicago Blackhawks hockey team, has a half-interest in Chicago\'s United Center sports arena and has real estate holdings in the Chicago area. William Wirtz died in September 2007; his son W. Rockwell \"Rocky\" Wirtz now heads the company.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5570,'Freeman',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Freeman supports the power of face-to-face marketing by providing full service design and production resources for corporate events, exhibit programs, expositions and conventions across North America. Corporate headquarters are in Dallas, Texas, and the company has offices in 40 locations throughout the U.S. and Canada.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5571,'Foodarama Supermarkets',22,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Freehold, New Jersey, Foodarama Supermarkets operates ShopRite supermarkets, liquor stores, a garden center, a bakery and a food-processing plant, which supplies its stores with meat and various prepared foods. In 2006, an investor group that included the founding family, the Sakers, took Foodarama private.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5572,'Remy International',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Anderson, Indiana, Remy International, formerly known as Delco Remy International, manufactures, remanufactures and distributes starters, alternators, engines, transmissions, torque converters, traction control systems and fuel systems for automobiles and trucks. Customers include General Motors, Advance Auto Parts, Ford Motor and AutoZone. Remy also manufacturers and remanufactures diesel engines and remanufactures parts for locomotive diesel engines. The company sells its products principally in North America, Europe, Latin America and the Asia-Pacific region. Citicorp Venture Capital took this former division of General Motors (nyse: GM) private in 2001. 				   Brands: Delco Remy','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5573,'Thorntons',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Thorntons is an independent gasoline and convenience chain retailer, marketing under the brand name of Thorntons QuickCaf','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5574,'Associated Materials',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Associated Materials is a manufacturer of exterior residential building products, which it distributes directly to independent distributors and dealers and company-owned supply centers across the country. The Company produces a range of vinyl siding and vinyl windows, as well as vinyl fencing, vinyl decking and vinyl garage doors. Alside, which was founded in 1947, introduced the first residential aluminum siding. The company went public in 1998; in 2002, the investment firm of Harvest Partners took the company private. 				   Brands: Alside','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5575,'Dawn Food Products',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Dawn Food Products makes and distributes bakery supplies and ingredients, including mixes, dough, toppings, icings, frozen products and ready-to-bake sweets. Clients include Mrs. Fields, Starbucks, Krispy Kreme and other restaurants, supermarkets and institutional bakeries. In addition, Dawn manufactures and distributes baking equipment. In 2004, Dawn acquired the bakery business of competitor Bunge North America. Corporate headquarters are in Jackson, Michigan.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5576,'PC Richard & Son',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','PC Richard & Son is an electronics, appliance and computer retailer serving the New York and New Jersey metropolitan area. Peter Christian Richard, an immigrant from Holland, started with a small hardware store in Brooklyn in 1909. His decedents now own the company. 				   Brands: PC Richard','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5577,'Michael Foods',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Michael Foods, headquartered in Minnesota, is the largest producer of processed egg products in the U.S. Other lines of business include potato products and distribution of refrigerated foods. Brand names include Better \'n Eggs, Table Ready and Easy Eggs. The Michael family, management, Vestar Capital Partners and Goldner Hawn Johnson & Morrison took the company private in April 2001. In November 2003, Thomas H. Lee Partners, LP and management bought the company. 				   Brands: All Whites, Better \'n Eggs, Crystal Farms, Diner\'s Choice, Easy Eggs, Papetti\'s, Simply Potatoes, Table Ready','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5578,'Indalex',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Indalex is involved in the extrusion and supply of aluminum around the world. The company operates 15 extrusion facilities, 39 extrusion presses, 9 electroplastic paint lines and 4 anodizing lines. Its principal facilities are in the United States and Canada. Sun Capital Partners acquired this firm\'s parent company, Indalex Holdings Finance, in February 2007.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5579,'GSC Enterprises',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Sulphur Springs, Texas-based GSC Enterprises (Grocery Supply Company) distributes food to convenience stores, supermarkets and military bases. Almost 60% of its customers are chain stores. The company has four operating divisions: GSC Sulphur Springs, GSC San Antonio, GSC Southeast and Fidelity Express. The company serves over 17,000 retail outlets in 17 states in the Southwest, Southeast and Midwest. Curtis McKenzie, Kenneth McKenzie and Woodrow Brittain founded GSC Enterprises in 1947.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5580,'Schottenstein Stores',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Schottenstein Stores is the holding company for discount furniture stores (Value City Furniture), which retail American Signature furniture (a Schottenstein affiliate). The company also specializes in liquidating merchandise through its SB Capital Group affiliate. Schottenstein Stores also has a large ownership stake in Value City Department Stores, which includes Filenes and DSW shoe warehouse stores. 				   Brands: Value City Department Stores.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5581,'Cinemark USA',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Plano, Texas, Cinemark USA, is a motion picture operator. Worldwide it operates 396 theaters with 4,488 screens located in the U.S., Argentina, Brazil, Canada, Chile, Colombia, Costa Rica, Ecuador, El Salvador, Honduras, Mexico, Panama, Peru and Taiwan. 				   Brands: Cinemark','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5582,'Suffolk Construction',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Suffolk Construction is a general building contracting company that provides pre-construction, construction management, general contracting and design-build services nation-wide, with offices in Boston, Massachusetts; Irvine, California; Miami, Naples, and West Palm Beach, Florida. Construction projects include both new construction and renovations in the hospitality, education, residential, healthcare, assisted living, public work, entertainment, retail and commercial market sectors.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5583,'Topa Equities',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','John Anderson started Topa Equities in 1956 with the purchase of the Topa Topa Ranch in Ojai, Calif. The business has since grown to include 37 subsidiaries with business segments in insurance, real estate, beverage distribution, automobile dealerships, agriculture and manufacturing. Headquarters are in Los Angeles.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5584,'Euramax International',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Euramax International is an international manufacturer and supplier of fabricated aluminum, steel, vinyl and fiberglass building, recreational vehicle and transportation products. The company operates from 62 locations in the U.S. and 8 locations in Europe. The history of Euramax goes back to a 1996 buyout of the Alumax Fabricated Products Group. In April 2005, Goldman Sachs Capital Partners acquired the company from Citibank\'s private equity division.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5585,'Advanced Drainage Systems',25,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Advanced Drainage Systems manufactures plastic pipes and other related products for commercial infrastructure and development projects, particularly for storm water drainage. The company is the world\'s largest producer of high-density polyethylene (HDPE) corrugated plastic pipes.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5586,'Beaulieu of America Group',25,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1977, Beaulieu of America was the first manufacturer to use polypropylene yarns to make moderately priced area rugs. Beaulieu continues to produce its own polypropylene and nylon yarns, as well as polyester fiber from recycled bottles. From those raw materials, Beaulieu produces a wide variety of broadloom carpet, and distributes a majority of its products throughout North America. 				   Brands: Beaulieu, Coronet, Laura Ashley, Peerless','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5587,'Gateway Health Plan',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded as an alternative to the Department of Public Welfare\'s Assistance Program in Pennsylvania, Gateway Health Plan provides managed health care services to more than 260,000 recipients of medical assistance in 39 counties throughout Pennsylvania as well as to Medicaid recipients in Ohio.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5588,'Micro Electronics',17,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Micro Electronics subsidiaries sell computers and related supplies primarily at the retail level. The company\'s business units include Micro Center, Micro Center Online, PowerSpec, Redemtech and WinBook. Micro Center has 21 retail outlets in 13 states. WinBook offers laptop computers, home theater PCs and LCD televisions. PowerSpec primarily offers desktop PCs, while Redemtech recycles and resells previously owned information technology assets. 				   Brands: Micro Center, PowerSpec, RedemTech, WinBook','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5589,'North Pacific Group',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Established in 1948, North Pacific Group\'s primary business is the wholesale distribution of wood products and building materials. Products include hardwood and softwood lumber, structural and architectural panels, engineered wood products and other specialized building materials. The company also distributes utility poles and pilings, agricultural products and chemicals, and food ingredients and products. With headquarters in Portland, Oregon, the company conducts business from locations throughout the U.S. and from offices in Canada, Chile and Mexico.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5590,'SavaSeniorCare',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Separated from its parent company, Mariner Healthcare, in 2005, SavaSeniorCare operates 184 nursing and assisted living facilities in 19 states.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5591,'Ash Grove Cement',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1882, Ash Grove Cement manufactures, markets, stores and ships cement, limestone, rock and shale from nine states across the country. Corporate headquarters are in Overland Park, Kansas. Ash Grove\'s shares are thinly traded in the over the counter market, but the company does not file financial documents with the Securities and Exchange Commission.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5592,'Goya Foods',10,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Goya Foods, founded in 1936, is a processor and distributor of Hispanic foods. Products include more than 1,200 varieties of beans, rice mixes, spices, frozen foods and packaged meals. In 2006, Goya launched its online store at www.goya.com. Headquarters are in Secaucus, New Jersey 				   Brands: Goya','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5593,'MTD Products',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1932 and based in Cleveland, Ohio, MTD Products is a manufacturer and marketer of outdoor power equipment such as lawn mowers and garden tractors. In 1999, the company sold its auto parts division to Shiloh Industries, of which MTD had a 53% stake. In July of 2000, the company acquired Ryobi Limited\'s outdoor products business in North, Central and South America. MTD brand names include Yard-Man, Club Cadet and White Outdoor. 				   Brands: Cub Cadet, White Outdoor, Yard Machines, Yard-Man','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5594,'Visant',6,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Visant is a marketing and publishing services enterprise servicing the school affinity, direct marketing, fragrance and cosmetics sampling, and educational publishing markets. Formerly named Jostens, the company changed its name in 2005 to reflect the combination of Jostens, Von Hoffmann, Leigh and Arcade Marketing under the ownership of Kohlberg, Kravis Roberts & Co., and DLJ Merchant Banking Partners III, L.P.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5595,'Sutherland Lumber',17,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Kansas City, Mo., Sutherland Lumber operates 68 lumber and home improvement stores in 13 states. Sutherland\'s subsidiary, Housemart.com, offers more than 40,000 items online.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5596,'Boscov\'s',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Boscov\'s is the largest family-owned, independent department store chain in the United States, operating 50 stores in Pennsylvania, New York, New Jersey, Maryland, Delaware and Virginia. Stores offer a full line of goods as well as special service departments including travel agencies, hair salons, restaurants, and optical and hearing aid centers. Boscov\'s corporate headquarters are in Reading, Pennsylvania. 				   Brands: Boscov\'s','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5597,'Roseburg Forest Products',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Oregon-based Roseburg Forest Products is a subsidiary of RLC Industries. Roseburg produces lumber, plywood, particleboard products and engineered wood. Kenneth W. Ford founded the firm in 1936. Allyn Ford is the current chief executive officer.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5598,'Kimball Hill',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','D Kimball Hill Sr. began building homes in the Chicago area in 1939. His son, David Kimball Hill, continued the tradition, founding Kimball Hill Homes in 1969. The company currently constructs single-family homes, attached town homes, attached luxury town homes and single-family attached mid-rise condominiums in eight states. Corporate headquarters are in Rolling Meadows, Illinois.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5599,'Deseret Management',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Organized in 1966, Deseret Management is a for-profit holding company affiliated with the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints (the Mormons). Among the company holdings are Bonneville International (radio and television broadcasting), Deseret Book (book retailing, publishing), Deseret Morning News (a daily newspaper), and Beneficial Financial Group (insurance and investments).','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5600,'Bozzuto\'s',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Adam J Bozzuto founded Bozzuto\'s in 1945, which continues to be family owned. It distributes food to retailers in five Northeast states and operates a small number of supermarkets under the names of IGA and Adam\'s Super Food Stores. Corporate headquarters are in Cheshire, Connecticut. 				   Brands: IGA, Adam\'s Super Food Stores','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5601,'Nypro',5,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Nypro designs, builds molds and molds plastics parts and assemblies for healthcare, electronics, telecommunications, automotive, consumer and industrial products and contract manufacturing. Nypro has 50 facilities in 16 countries.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5602,'24 Hour Fitness Worldwide',25,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in San Ramon, Calif., 24 Hour Fitness serves over 3 million members in more than 380 health clubs across 14 different states and 4 Asian countries. 				   Brands: 24 Hour Fitness','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5603,'Pliant',6,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Pliant Corp., formerly Huntsman Packaging, is a producer of plastic film packaging materials for personal care, medical, agricultural and industrial applications. The company produces specialty films for personal care products such as diapers; films used with foil, paper and other packaging materials; barrier films for cookie, cracker and cereal box liners; and films for the frozen food and agricultural markets. The company operates 23 manufacturing and research development companies worldwide. In July 2006, Pliant Corporation announced that it has completed its previously announced financial restructuring and has exited Chapter 11 Bankruptcy protection.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5604,'Alsco',5,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','A textile services company founded in 1889, Alsco supplies flat linens, uniforms, chef\'s outfits, cleanroom garments, dust control items, paper supplies and related items. The company has 145 service centers in 10 countries.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5605,'Ritz Camera Centers',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Ritz Camera Centers, of Beltsville, Maryland, operates a chain of approximately 1,100 photography stores located in 45 states and the District of Columbia. These stores offer a variety of photography products and services, including one-hour photofinishing, digital imaging and equipment. Outlets include Ritz Camera, Wolf Camera, Kits Camera, Inkleys and the Camera Shop. The company also owns Boater\'s World Marine Centers, a chain of 125 stores that sells fishing, water speed motors, marine electronics and other boating supplies. 				   Brands: Boater\'s World Marine Centers, Inkleys, Kits Camera, Ritz Camera, The Camera Shop, Wolf Camera','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5606,'Warren Equipment',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Warren Equipment Company makes heavy duty pumps, compressors, generators and other equipment for the energy industry and other industries.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5607,'Laureate Education',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Laureate Education enrolls over 243,000 students at schools throughout the Americas, Europe, and Asia in programs that range from traditional liberal arts to hospitality management. The company went private in 2007 through a consortium of investors led by the company\'s chief executive, Douglas L. Becker.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5608,'Gould Paper',11,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Harry E. Gould Sr. Today founded Gould Paper in 1924. Today, the company is a large distributor of fine paper, newsprint, and packaging material to publishers, catalog houses, printers, end-users and redistributors. Gould Paper has operations in the United Kingdom, France, Finland, Dubai, Singapore, Australia, New Zealand, Hong Kong, China and the Philippines. Subsidiaries include BRW Paper, Diamond Paper, WWF International UK Limited, Gallium EURL, Salehurst Limited, Price & Pierce and Weiss-McNair. Harry E. Gould, Jr. is chairman, president and chief executive officer.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5609,'Kirkland & Ellis',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:20:\"Kirkland & Ellis LLP\";}','Org','For nearly 100 years, Kirkland & Ellis has handled complicated litigation, corporate, intellectual property, restructuring, tax, and counseling matters for leading national and international clients. Today, Kirkland & Ellis continues to work with a long-standing base of clients engaged in industries such as manufacturing, transportation, telecommunications, private equity, pharmaceuticals, technology, energy, health care, real estate, chemicals, food products, finance, insurance, e-commerce, advertising, sales and marketing and accounting.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany,LobbyingFirm',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5610,'Affinion Group',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','In 2005, Apollo Management, an investment banking firm, and company management purchased this operation from Cendant Corp. Affinion Group develops and manages affinity marketing programs, such as credit card loyalty rewards and shoppers\' clubs. It also markets insurance to members of those groups.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5611,'Drees Co',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Drees Company, headquartered in Northern Kentucky, builds single family, entry level, condominium and luxury homes in greater Cincinnati, Dayton and Cleveland, Ohio; Dallas and Austin, Texas; Washington D.C.; Frederick, Maryland; Raleigh, North Caroline; Indianapolis, Indiana; Nashville, Tennessee; and Jacksonville, Florida. The company also has interests in land development and mortgage financing.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5612,'Teamhealth',10,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Knoxville, Tennessee, Team Health is among the largest national providers of outsourced physician staffing and administrative services to hospitals and other healthcare providers in the United States. Team Health provides permanent staffing, management and administrative services to approximately 600 hospitals, medical imaging centers, surgery centers, clinics and military treatment facilities in 44 states. Originally called Southeastern Emergency Physicians (SEP), the company was founded in 1979. In a recapitalization transaction in March 1999 Team Health, which had been part of MedPartners Inc., was sold to private equity firms Madison Dearborn Partners, Cornerstone Equity Investors and Beecken Petty & Co. In November 2005, the Blackstone Group acquired Team Health.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5613,'Brookshire Brothers',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1921 Brookshire Brothers Ltd. shares the same ancestry as Brookshire Grocery Co. (A split between the founding brothers resulted in separate companies). The company has 73 stores under the names of Brookshire Brothers, B&B Food Store and Budget Choppers in Texas and Louisiana. Most stores also offer gasoline service. 				   Brands: B&B Food Store, Brookshire Brothers, Budget Chopper','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5614,'Genmar Holdings',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Genmar Holdings, based in Minneapolis, is engaged in the manufacturing and marketing of leisure powerboats. Some of Genmar\'s divisions have been building boats since the early 1900s. The company markets 12 brands of recreational powerboats and fishing boats. Irwin Jacobs is chairman, chief executive officer and the largest (40%) shareholder of Genmar, which went private in 1988 under the name Minstar. Following a financial restructuring in 1993, Genmar became Minstar\'s parent company 				   Brands: Aquasport, Carver, Champion, Crestliner, Enviro-Care, Trailer Care, First Mate +, Four Winns, Hydra-Sports, Javelin, Lowe, Seaswirl, Stratos, Glastron, Larson, Logic, Lund, Nova, Ranger, Scarab, Trojan, VEC (Virtual Engineered Composites), Wellcraft','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5615,'RGIS Holdings',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1958 as Retail Grocery Inventory Service, the company later changed its name to RGIS Holdings. RGIS offers inventory and retail services through 400 offices globally. It provides 450,000 inventory counts annually for retail clients like Wal-Mart, Home Depot and Target. In May 2007, the Blackstone Group acquired a majority stake in the company.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5616,'Steve and Barry\'s',17,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Steven Shore and Barry Prevor founded this company in 1985 and they still run it. The business began as an endeavor to sell college logo shirts out of a pick-up truck at the University of Pennsylvania in 1985, and has since become a chain of over 200 stores across 33 states, and plans to add 100 more outlets in 2007. Stores feature licensed merchandise from 350 colleges and brands like Marvel Comics, World Wide Wrestling Entertainment, General Motors, Ford, Kellogg\'s, Hershey\'s and Coors. Stores also feature Sarah Jessica Parker\'s Bitten line and Stephon Marbury\'s Starbury line of athletic wear. A Boston private equity firm, TA Associates, owns a minority stake of the Port Washington, New York company.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5617,'Swagelok',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Swagelok Company, based in Solon, Ohio, develops and manufactures fluid system components used in analytical and process instrumentation, biopharmaceutical production, the oil and gas, power generation, semiconductor manufacturing, maritime and other industries. 				   Brands: Swagelok','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5618,'Wells\' Dairy',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Fred H, Wells founded this company in 1913, and family members still own this Le Mars, Iowa business. Wells\' Dairy makes more than 500 different ice cream and novelty desserts in its five manufacturing plants. Under the Blue Bunny brand, it sells these products in convenience stores, restaurants and supermarkets throughout the U.S. and in twenty other countries. 				   Brands: Blue Bunny','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5619,'Keane',5,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Keane, of Boston, Mass., provides outsourcing and information technology consulting services. The company offers a range of business process outsourcing (BPO) services through its Keane Worldzen subsidiary. Other services include application development, consulting, project management and strategic staffing.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5620,'Appleton Papers',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1907, Appleton manufactures and distributes paper and paper products from its facilities in Wisconsin, Ohio, Pennsylvania, Massachusetts and the United Kingdom. The company\'s specialties include carbonless paper, thermal paper and security paper. In 2001 employees bought the company from its foreign owners; Appleton is now 100% employee-owned. 				   Brands: Appleton, Docucheck, NCR Paper, Optima','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5621,'McKee Foods',11,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Best known for its more than 80 varieties of Little Debbie snack food line, McKee Foods, of Collegedale, Tennessee also makes Sunbelt snack foods. O.D. McKee and his wife, Ruth founded the company in 1934 during the Great Depression. Mike McKee is president and chief executive officer. 				   Brands: Little Debbie, Sunbelt','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5622,'Lifetouch',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Celebrating its 70th birthday in 2006, Lifetouch Inc. of Eden Prairie, Minnesota, is the largest employee-owned photography company in the nation. The company, which specializes in school, church and family portraits, has 22,000 employees and operations in all 50 states and Canada. 				   Brands: Lifetouch','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5623,'Plastech Engineered Products',28,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Plastech Engineered Products began in 1988 when its president and chief executive officer, Julie Nguyen Brown, purchased a single plastic injection molding plant in Cairo, Michigan. The company is a Tier 1 and Tier 2 automotive supplier of interior, exterior and underhood components. Its process capabilities include injection and blow molding, interior and exterior painting, metal stamping and extrusion. Plastech\'s products include bed extenders, body claddings, grille panels, spoilers, interior consoles, modular overhead systems, battery trays and fan shrouds. In February 2004, Plastech acquired smaller competitor LDM Technologies.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5624,'Samsonite',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Samsonite is one of the world\'s largest manufacturers and distributors of luggage. It went private in October 2007, via a buyout by CVC Capital Partners.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5625,'Shapell Industries',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Shapell Industries is a diversified homebuilder and real estate development company operating exclusively in California. Nathan Shapell, chairman and chief executive officer, started the company with his brother David and his brother-in-law Max Webb in 1955. Webb is still a partner in the firm. The company went private in 1984.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5626,'MWH',3,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Broomfield, Colorado, MWH is an employee-owned business with approximately 6,000 employees worldwide. The company provides water, wastewater, energy, natural resource, program management, consulting and construction services to industrial, municipal and government clients globally. MWH is the result of a merger of Montgomery Watson and Harza Engineering in 2001.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5627,'Marc Glassman',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Marc Glassman operates 60 Marc\'s discount drugstores throughout Ohio and Connecticut. Stores range in size from 25,000 to 53,000 square feet and most locations have in-store pharmacies. Products sold include closeout merchandise, health and beauty aids, food items, sundries and cosmetics. 				   Brands: Marc\'s Deep-Er-Discount, Xpect-Discount Drugs','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5628,'Bally Total Fitness',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','With roots dating back to 1962, Bally Total fitness is an international operator of health centers and sports clubs. Bally has fitness centers in South Korea, China and the Bahamas, as well as the United States. As of December 2006, Bally had about 375 fitness centers worldwide. The company filed for Chapter 11 bankruptcy in the summer of 2007 and by October 1, 2007 announced its emergence from bankruptcy court protection under 100% ownership by Harbinger Capital, a hedge fund.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5629,'Forever 21',10,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Trendy retailer Forever 21 operates 355 stores under the Forever 21, Forever XXI, For Love 21 and Gadzooks banners. Stores, located primarily in the United States and Canada, sell men\'s and women\'s clothing and accessories. Forever 21 is headquartered in Los Angeles, California. 				   Brands: Fashin XXI, Forever 21','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5630,'Minyard Food Stores',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','A.W. Minyard, who opened his first store in 1932, founded Minyard Food Stores. This grocery chain now operates 61 supermarkets, primarily in the Dallas/Fort Worth market. Its 23 Minyard Foods Stores are combination food stores, which average 40,000 square feet. The chain\'s 14 Sack\'n Save Stores offer low-cost alternative shopping and its 24 Carnival Food Stores follow an ethnic store format. The company also owns 15 gasoline station centers, known as On the Go, and 36 pharmacies. 				   Brands: Carnival Food Stores, Minyard Food Stores, On the Go Fuel Centers, Sack \'n Save Food Stores','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5631,'Crete Carrier',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Lincoln, Nebraska transportation carrier operates in 48 states from 15 terminals located mostly in the eastern part of the US. Crete\'s other two divisions are Shaffer Trucking, which transports temperature controlled loads, and Hunt Transportation, which delivers heavy cargo on trailers. The company manages approximately 5,400 tractors and over 13,000 trailers. Founded in 1966, Tonn M. Ostergard is the current chief executive officer.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5632,'Orgill',6,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1847 by William Orgill and RT Lamb as Orgill Brothers & Co., the company continues to be owned members of the Orgill family, Joseph Orgill and his cousin Michael McDonnel. The company is the largest independent hardware distributor in the U.S. Orgill has distribution centers in Georgia, Illinois, West Virginia and Tennessee, which service retail stores in 48 states and more than 60 countries. Ronnell S. Beal is president and chief executive officer. 				   Brands: Most major national brands in all categories','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5633,'Pacific Coast Building Products',31,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Fred Anderson started with a single lumberyard in 1953 in Sacramento, California. Today, Pacific Coast Building Products is a family of diverse manufacturing and distribution companies providing building materials and services to the residential, commercial and industrial markets. Pacific Coast has expanded into 10 western states as well as Hawaii and Canada. Products include concrete block, terra cotta, insulation, brick, wallboard, clay pipe, roofing products, lumber and trusses. Corporate headquarters are in Rancho Cordova, California. 				   Brands: Basalite, Pabco','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5634,'Inserra Supermarkets',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1961 Inserra Supermarkets operates one supermarket and 21 superstores under the ShopRite name. Company stores are located in northern New Jersey and southeastern New York. Lawrence R. Inserra, Jr. is president and chief executive officer; Company headquarters are in Mahwah, New Jersey. 				   Brands: Shoprite','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5635,'Key Safety Systems',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Investment group, Ewing Management, controls Key Safety Systems, part of the Key Automotive Group. The company designs and produces airbags, seatbelts, steering wheels and fully integrated safety systems. More than 300 vehicle models across 60 vehicle makes throughout North America, Europe and Asia use parts from Key. Founded in 1987 (formerly known as Breed Corp), Key Safety Systems, headquartered in Sterling Michigan, now operates 36 manufacturing, technical and sales facilities in 12 countries. 				   Brands: MOMO','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5636,'Clubcorp',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1957 under the name Country Clubs by Robert H. Dedman Sr., ClubCorp is the world\'s largest owner and manager of private clubs, resorts and public golf courses. The company operates 97 country clubs, three destination golf resorts and 64 business/sports clubs in 27 states and three countries. It derives revenues in its hospitality segment from membership dues and fees, food and beverage sales, golf operations and lodging facilities. The company also receives fees for managing third-party operations. In 2006, the private equity firm KSL Capital Partners, acquired ClubCorp from the Dedman family, outside investors and ClubCorp employees.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5637,'Stewart\'s Shops',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Stewart\'s Shops began in 1935 when Percy W. Dake and Charles V. Dake started making Dake\'s Delicious Ice Cream in Greenfield, New York. Today the company includes Stewart\'s Processing Corp. and Stewart\'s Shops Corp. The company operates more than 322 Stewart\'s Shops selling ice cream and other dairy products, groceries and convenience foods. Many outlets include gasoline pumps as well. 				   Brands: Stewart\'s Shops, Bonfare','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5638,'BrandsMart USA',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in South Florida, Brandsmart USA, is a discount retailer of consumer appliances, electronics and housewares. BrandsMart USA sells television, large and small appliances, audio, video, home theater, projection television, car stereo, computers, cellular telephones, satellites, and entertainment furniture. The company operates eight stores in Florida and Georgia. 				   Brands: BrandsMart','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5639,'Columbia Forest Prods',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Employee-owned Columbia Forest Products is a large North American manufacturer of hardwood plywood and veneers used in the production of furniture, cabinetry and architectural millwork. Founded in 1976, the company originally consisted of a full-scale hardwood plywood manufacturing plant in Klamath Falls, Ore. and two rotary hardwood veneer operations in the northeastern U.S. Since then it has acquired or built 19 additional plants situated in the U.S. and Canada. Today, it manufactures solid wood, engineered wood and laminate flooring products. 				   Brands: Appalachian Traditions, CFP 60\'s, Columbia Adler, Columbia Chic, Columbia Choice, Columbia Flooring, EcoColors, Europly','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5640,'Hampton Affiliates',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Hampton Affiliates is one the nation\'s largest privately-held timber firms. The company owns 167,000 acres of timberland and has mills in Washington, Oregon, and British Columbia.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5641,'Interstate Battery Systems of America',37,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1952, Interstate Battery Systems of America markets and distributes all battery types, including automotive, marine, RV, motorcycle, lawn and garden, specialty, consumer, alkaline and related products. The company sells its products to 328 distributors and 200,000 dealers in the U.S. and Canada. Corporate headquarters are in Dallas, Texas. 				   Brands: Interstate','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5642,'Utility Trailer Manufacturing',29,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1914 Utility Trailer Manufacturing builds and sells refrigerated trailers, known within the industry as reefers. The company also produces dry-freight trailers, flatbeds and curtain-sided trailers. Utility Trailer has five plants in the U.S. and one in England.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5643,'PricewaterhouseCoopers',22,NULL,'a:3:{i:0;s:23:\"Pricewaterhouse Coopers\";i:1;s:24:\"Price-Waterhouse-Coopers\";i:2;s:24:\"Price-Waterhouse Coopers\";}','Org','In 1998 Price Waterhouse and Coopers & Lybrand merged and formed PricewaterhouseCoopers, the largest such company in the world. As one of the Big 4 accounting firms, PricewaterhouseCoopers provides assurance, tax and advisory services to clients in 148 countries.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany,LobbyingFirm',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5644,'Mars',4,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Started in 1911, Mars is one of the largest manufacturers in each of its main businesses: branded snack foods, pet foods, rice and drink vending equipment. Among better-known Mars brand names are, M&M\'s, Snickers, Milky Way, 3 Musketeers, Pedigree, Skittles, Starburst, Whiskas, Sheba and Uncle Ben\'s foods. With products sold in more than 100 countries, the company has offices and manufacturing facilities in over 65 countries. Members of the Mars family own the company; Paul Michaels is company president. 				   Brands: 3 Musketeers, Combos, Dove, Kal Kan, Kudos, M&Ms, Milky Way, Pedigree, Sheba, Skittles, Snickers, Starburst, Twix, Uncle Ben\'s, Whiskas','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5645,'Enterprise Rent-A-Car',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Jack Crawford Taylor founded Enterprise Rent-A-Car in 1957 in St. Louis, as an auto leasing service. The company started with 17 cars, and within a few years, the business expanded into daily rentals, focusing on customers whose regular vehicles were in the repair shop. In August 2007, Enterprise acquired Vanguard Car Rental with its National Car Rental and Alamo Rent A Car businesses.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5646,'Capital Group Cos',17,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:17:\"Capital Group Cos\";}','Org','Through its subsidiaries, the Capital Group of Companies manages and underwrites mutual funds in the American Funds family group and provides other financial services. Founded in 1931 by Jonathan Bell Lovelace, the company has more than 75 years of asset-management experience.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5647,'Platinum Equity',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1995, Platinum Equity specializes in acquiring and operating businesses throughout the world. Platinum Equity\'s portfolio companies are primarily mission-critical service and solutions providers. The company acquires businesses that share common characteristics across a variety of industries, such as steel services, communications equipment and services, software, telecommunications services, insurance services, transportation and logistics, and chemical manufacturing. The Platinum Equity portfolio is comprised of 19 businesses, with over 45,000 employees.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5648,'Pro-Build Holdings',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Denver, Colorado, Pro-Build is the nation\'s largest supplier of building materials to professional builders, with more than 500 dealer locations in 40 states throughout the U.S.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5649,'HY-Vee',6,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1930 and headquartered in West Des Moines, Iowa, Hy-Vee is a large Midwestern chain of 224 stores including 198 supermarkets and 26 Hy-Vee Drugstores. Hy-Vee Food outlets range from 40,000 to 83,000 square feet. Most new stores are 80,000 square feet in size and are a combination food and drugstore format. 				   Brands: Grand Selections, Hy-Vee, Midwest Country Fare','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5650,'Boise Cascade',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Boise, Idaho, Boise Cascade manufactures engineered wood products, lumber, plywood and particleboard and distributes a broad line of building materials, including wood products manufactured by the company. Boise also manufactures a wide range of specialty and premium papers, including imaging papers for the office and home, papers for pressure-sensitive applications, printing and converting papers, containerboard and corrugated boxes, newsprint and market pulp.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5651,'Guardian Industries',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Guardian Industries, based in Auburn Hills, Michigan, manufactures float glass and fabricated glass products for the commercial and residential construction industries. Guardian Automotive provides exterior systems to the global automotive industry. Guardian\'s Building Products Group, headquartered in Greenville, South Carolina, includes a substantial fiberglass insulation manufacturing operation and occupies a significant and growing position in the building materials distribution business, with more than 100 distribution centers and brokerage offices in the United States and Canada. Guardian employs 19,000 people and operates facilities throughout North America, Europe, South America, Asia, Africa and the Middle East.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5652,'Colonial Group',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1921 by Raymond M. Dem','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5653,'Neiman Marcus Group',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Neiman Marcus Group is one of the nation\'s largest retailers of luxury and fashion goods. It operates 39 Neiman Marcus stores nationwide, two Bergdorf Goodman stores in New York City, and catalogs and e-commerce websites under each store name. The company also sells home furnishings and accessories through Horchow.com. Private equity groups Texas Pacific Group and Warburg Pincus acquired the company in October 2005.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5654,'OSI Group',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','OSI Group is a holding company of meat processors that service the retail and food service industries. Subsidiaries include Carolina Culinary Foods, David Berg, Fair Oaks Farms, Nation Pizza Products, Oakland Foods, OSI International Foods and Otto & Sons. Products include meat patties, bacon, hot dogs, pizza, fish, poultry and vegetable products. The company traces its history back to 1909.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5655,'CH2M Hill Cos',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Denver, employee-owned CH2M HILL is a global company providing engineering, construction, operations and related technical services to public and private clients. CH2M Hill\'s work is concentrated in the areas of transportation, water, energy, environment, communications, construction and industrial facilities. The company has more than 17,000 employees in 200 offices worldwide.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-21 23:00:29',NULL,0,'deleted',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5656,'InterTech Group',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1978, InterTech Group is a diversified chemical manufacturer. Products include elastomerics, packaging and sealing devices, gaskets, battery separator sheets, woven and nonwoven fabrics. InterTech\'s Rem Grit subsidiary manufactures handheld tools. Corporate headquarters are in North Charleston, South Carolina.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5657,'BI-LO Holdings',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','In January 2005, Lone Star Fund, based in Dallas, acquired the Bi-Lo and Bruno\'s divisions from Dutch retail conglomerate, Ahold for $660 million and consolidated operations. Bi-Lo Holdings, also known as Bi-Lo/Bruno\'s, operates supermarkets in South Carolina, North Carolina, Georgia, Tennessee, Florida and Alabama. In addition to the Bi-Lo and Bruno\'s banners, the family of stores included Food World, FoodMax and Food Fair. 				   Brands: Bruno\'s, Food World, FoodMax, Food Fair','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5658,'Stater Bros',11,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1936, Stater Bros Markets became a privately held company in 1987. The company operates 163 supermarkets in southern California. Jack Brown, chairman, president and chief executive officer, is the majority shareholder in La Cadena Investments, which owns 100% of the stock in the parent company. Corporate headquartered are in San Bernardino, Calif. 				   Brands: Stater Bros Markets','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5659,'Whiting-Turner Contracting',26,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Based in Baltimore, Maryland, Whiting-Turner Contracting has been in business since 1909. It is one of the nation\'s largest construction management and general contracting companies. The company provides the full spectrum of construction services on projects small and large in markets such as retail, office, education, healthcare, life sciences, technology, transportation and utilities. Whiting-Turner has 24 regional offices nationwide.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5660,'VWR International',17,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','VWR International supplies materials to research laboratories around the world. It distributes over 1,200,000 products&mdash;such as scientific equipment, supplies, and chemicals&mdash;to over 250,000 customers in North America and Europe. Its principal customers are big pharmaceutical, biotechnological and chemical companies; universities and research institutes; and governmental agencies.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5661,'Clark Enterprises',17,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Clark Enterprises (CEI) is holding company of various Clark Companies. Based in Bethesda, Maryland, Clark Companies include real estate investments, commercial, heavy and residential construction companies, venture capital and private equity businesses.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5662,'Berry Plastics',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1967, Berry Plastics, of Evansville, Indiana, manufactures injection-molded plastic products: containers, aerosol overcaps, closures, drink cups and housewares for the commercial and consumer markets. Berry owns 62 manufacturing facilities worldwide. In June 2006, Berry announced that private equity firms Apollo Management and Graham Partners joined with senior management to acquire the company. In April 2007, Berry Plastics merged with another Apollo holding, Covalence Specialty Materials, under the Berry Plastics name.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5663,'Jeld-Wen',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Based in Klamath Falls, Oregon, Jeld-Wen\'s main business is the manufacturing of windows, doors and other millwork products. Other areas of activity are real estate and wholesale distribution of building materials. The company, founded in 1960, also operates numerous title insurance companies under the AmeriTitle name. Roderick Wendt is the chief executive officer. 				   Brands: Alterna Exterior Doors, Bend Door Company, Challenge, Donat Flamand, DoorCraft, Elite Garage Doors, Elite Interior Doors, International Wood Products, Nord Door Company, Norma, Norco Windows & Patios Doors, Pozzi Wood Windows, Summit Window & Patio Door, Wenco Windows & Patio Doors, United Window, Yamikma Door, Caradco Windows & Doors, Willmar Windows','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5664,'Eby-Brown',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Eby-Brown distributes tobacco, candy and general merchandise to convenience stores. Founded in 1887, Eby-Brown Company is the second largest convenience product distributor in the U.S., servicing over 14,000 retail locations from eight distribution centers throughout the Midwest, Mid-Atlantic and the Southeast. Thomas G. Wake and Richard Wake are co-presidents of the company.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5665,'International Data Group',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','A media, research, and events company, International Data Group (IDG) publishes 300 magazines and newspapers devoted to information technology. The company also maintains 450 technology-specific Web sites and produces 750 computer-related conferences and events worldwide. 				   Brands: CIO, Networkworld, Macworld, Comnet, Bio IT World, Computerworld, InfoWorld, Macworld, Network World, PC World','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5666,'Andersen',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1903 by Danish immigrant Hans Andersen and his family as Andersen Lumber Company, Andersen Corporation, headquartered in Bayport, Minnesota, is now the biggest U.S. manufacturer of vinyl and wood windows, patio and storm doors. 				   Brands: Andersen, EMCO, Forever, Frenchwood, KML, Renewal by Andersen','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5667,'Walsh Group',11,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Walsh Group has practiced general building construction since 1898, and has been a family held business since that time. The Chicago company provides general contracting, construction management and design and build services to clients nationwide through the operations of its two subsidiaries, Walsh Construction and Archer Western Contractors.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5668,'US Oncology',11,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','In 1999, American Oncology Resources and Physician Reliance Network merged to form US Oncology, a health services network focused exclusively on cancer treatment and research. US Oncology serves 1,067 affiliated physicians at 425 sites in 37 states, and owns a pharmaceutical distribution business. Welsh, Carson, Anderson & Stowe took the company private in 2004.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5669,'Central National-Gottesman',26,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1886, Central National-Gottesman distributes pulp and paper. The company\'s Central National division specializes in the sale of pulp, paper, paperboard and newsprint in the U.S. and overseas. The Lindenmeyr division is engaged in the merchant distribution of fine papers in the U.S. Products from this operation include papers for printing and writing, books, magazines and catalogs. Central National-Gottesman, headquartered in Purchase, N.Y., has 26 U.S. offices and 17 overseas offices with representatives in more than 40 additional countries. 				   Brands: Lindenmeyr Book Publishing, Lindenmeyr Central, Lindenmeyr Munroe','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5670,'Graham Packaging Holdings',25,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Graham Packaging Holdings designs and manufactures blow-molded plastic containers for the food, household and personal care and automotive lubricant markets. The company has 87 plants in North America, Europe and South America. Graham Packaging, headquartered in York, Pennsylvania, is majority owned by the Blackstone Group.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5671,'Anderson Cos',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Begun in 1917 as a newsstand in Florence, Alabama, the Anderson Companies now do business in several areas. Anderson Media Corporation is the largest U.S. distributor and merchandiser of consumer magazines, pre-recorded music and books. TNT Fireworks is the country\'s largest importer and distributor of consumer fireworks. Anderson Press publishes children\'s books and houses Anderson units, Whitman Publishing and H.E. Harris, which sells books and supplies for coin and stamp collecting. C.R. Gibson sells binders and blank books for photo albums, diaries and other collections. For the purposes of its revenue estimate, Forbes excludes Books-A-Million (nasdaq: BAMM), a publicly held company in which the Anderson family is the majority stockholder.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5672,'Cooper-Standard Automotive',26,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Novi, Michigan, Cooper-Standard Automotive manufactures body sealing, fluid handling, and noise, vibration and harshness control systems. The company operates in 62 locations in 15 countries around the world.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5673,'Affinia Group',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Ann Arbor, Michigan, Affinia Group is a designer, manufacturer, and distributor of motor vehicle components. The company\'s brands include WIX, Raybestos, Aimco, McQuay-Norris, Nakata and Quinton Hazell. Affinia Group operates in North and South America and Europe.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5674,'Infor',5,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 2002, Infor delivers business-specific software to 70,000 customers worldwide in wide range of industries. It covers supply chain planning and execution, customer and supplier relationship management and business intelligence solutions. Infor has 9,200 employees and is led Jim Schaper its chief executive officer.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5675,'Newpage',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','In 2005, MeadWestvaco Corp. sold its papers business and associated assets to a new company controlled by Cerberus Capital Management L.P., a private, New York investment firm. This business, renamed NewPage, is the largest coated paper manufacturer in North America, based on production capacity. Primary uses for coated paper include media and marketing applications, such as corporate annual reports, high-end advertising brochures, magazines, catalogs and direct mail advertising. The company also produces carbonless copy paper for business forms, as well as uncoated paper, digital printing paper and market pulp, a component used in the manufacturing of paper. NewPage operates integrated pulp and paper manufacturing mills in Escanaba, Michigan; Luke, Maryland; Rumford, Maine; and Wickliffe, Kentucky. These mills have a combined annual capacity of approximately 2.2 million tons of coated paper. Big customers include publishers such as Hearst Publications, McGraw-Hill Companies and Pearson Education; commercial printers such as Banta Corporation, QuadGraphics, QuebecorWorld and RR Donnelley; specialty retailers such as Williams-Sonoma, and paper merchants such as Unisource Worldwide and Xpedx.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5676,'G-I Holdings',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1886 as the Standard Paint Company, G-I Holdings later evolved into GAF Corp. The company became private in 1989 via a leveraged buyout. In 1997, it spun off its specialty chemicals business to ISP Holding, Inc. GAF\'s remaining subsidiary, Building Materials Corporation of America, manufactures roofing and other building materials. The operation does business under the name GAF Materials Corporation, and its brand names include Timberline, Sovereign, Slateline, Grand Sequoia and Weather Stopper. 				   Brands: Slateline, Sovereign, Timberline, Weather Stopper','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5677,'Select Medical',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:19:\"Select Medical Corp\";}','Org','Select Medical is comprised of a national network of specialized acute health care facilities and services, including long-term acute care hospitals, inpatient and outpatient rehabilitation and contract therapy services. The company currently operates 92 long-term acute care hospitals in 26 states, four acute medical rehabilitation hospitals, and 544 outpatient clinics in 19 states and the District of Columbia.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5678,'Dresser',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Dresser manufactures and markets highly engineered energy infrastructure and oilfield products and services around the globe. Headquartered in Dallas, Texas, Dresser has a sales, manufacturing and support presence of 6,100 employees in more than 100 countries. 				   Brands: Ashcroft, Consolidated, Waukesha Engine, Wayne, Grove, Masoneilan, Consolidated, Ledeen, Becker Precision, Texsteam, TK Valve, Wheatley, Tom Wheatley, Ring-O Valve, Nil-Cor, Control Seal, LVF, International Valve, ROOTS, Dresser Piping Specialties, Mooney Controls, Willy, Ebro, Weksler, FloSystems','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5679,'Ingram Industries',17,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Ingram Industries, headquartered in Nashville, has interests in book wholesaling (Ingram Book Group), inland marine transportation (Ingram Marine Group), print-on-demand book manufacturing (Lightning Source), and digital content services (Ingram Digital Group).','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5680,'Metals USA',10,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1996, this Texas metal service company is a provider and distributor of value-added processed steel, aluminum, and metal components. It operates from 77 locations within the United States. The company has three operating units: Flat Rolled Group, Plates and Shapes Group, and Building Products Group. Metals USA offer a range of products and services including manufacturing and distributing aluminum products, processing and selling structural shapes in a number of alloy grades and sizes, as well as manufacturing and selling metal building products for the home and commercial building industry. Metals USA first went public in 1997 and private in late November 2005 after an acquisition by Apollo Management L.P.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5681,'Boston Consulting Group',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1963, The Boston Consulting Group (BCG) is a global management-consulting firm. Boston Consulting has helped companies achieve competitive advantages by developing and realizing unique strategies. Headquartered in Boston, the firm employs 3,300 consultants in 66 offices throughout 38 countries.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5682,'CC Industries',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Crown family owns Chicago-based CC Industries. Its largest subsidiary is truck trailer manufacturer, Great Dane Trailers. The company\'s other interests include farm equipment maker Bull Hog, casual metal furniture manufacturer Woodard Furniture, and real estate. CC Industries has been in business for nearly 60 years. 				   Brands: Great Dane','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5683,'Carpenter',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Carpenter Co., formerly ER Carpenter, is a manufacturer of polyurethane foam used in comfort cushioning. The company makes foam materials for furniture, bedding, consumer products, carpet cushioning and other industries. Carpenter, based in Richmond, Virginia, also manufactures urethane chemicals for its own use as well as for sale to manufacturers of products such as insulation, packaging and tires. This business has facilities throughout the U.S., Canada, Denmark, France, Germany, Sweden, Poland and the United Kingdom.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5684,'Wilbur-Ellis',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Wilbur-Ellis started in 1921 as a fishery by-products trading company. This San Francisco firm is now a large distributor of farm agricultural chemicals, fertilizers, seeds and animal feed. Through its Connell Brothers unit, it markets and distributes specialty industrial chemicals in the Pacific Rim.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5685,'Electro-Motive Diesel',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','In April 2005, Greenbriar Equity Group, Berkshire Partners and certain related parties acquired Electro-Motive Diesel from General Motors. Founded in 1922, Electro-Motive Diesel is one of two U.S. original equipment manufacturers of diesel-electric locomotives. Headquartered in LaGrange, Illinois, with additional facilities in London, Ontario, EMD designs, manufactures and sells diesel-electric locomotives for all commercial railroad applications and has sold its products in more than 70 countries worldwide. The company is also a global provider of diesel engines for marine propulsion, offshore and land-based oil drilling rigs and stationary power generation.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5686,'Merit Energy',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1989, Merit Energy Company makes direct investments in oil and gas assets on behalf of equity-based limited partnerships. The company now operates wells and other energy facilities in thirteen states, the Gulf of Mexico and Canada.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5687,'Taylor',6,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1975 and headquartered in North Mankato, Minnesota, Taylor Corp. is a holding company with interests in marketing, printing, direct mail and technology. Taylor\'s products and services cover a wide range of commercial printing, direct mail products, incentive and award programs and commemorative print items.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5688,'TIC Holdings',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Based in Steamboat Springs, Colorado, employee-owned TIC Holdings has two wholly owned subsidiaries. The first, TIC&mdash;The Industrial Company, is a highly diversified contractor, involved in industrial markets, such as power, mining, oil, gas, chemicals, pulp and paper, heavy equipment erection and food and beverage. Western Summit Constructors, Inc. focuses primarily on water and wastewater treatment projects. TIC also has an international unit, specializing in power generation, mining, petrochemical and water and wastewater operations. This unit operates in Mexico and Latin America, Asia Pacific, Europe and the Middle East.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5689,'Washington Cos',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Washington Companies is a group of individual companies in which Montana businessman Dennis R. Washington holds a controlling ownership position. Since Mr. Washington\'s beginnings in the construction industry in 1957, the Washington Companies have grown and diversified into mining and construction, rail transportation, marine transportation, heavy equipment sales, aviation products and real estate development. Revenues from public subsidiaries are not included in total revenues calculated by Forbes.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5690,'Duane Reade',11,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Named after the two streets where its first store was located in 1960, Duane Reade is the largest drug store chain in the metropolitan New Work City area. Oak Hill Capital Partners took the company private in mid 2004.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5691,'K-VA-T Food Stores',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1918, K-VA-T Food Stores\' unique name reflects the locations of its supermarkets in Kentucky, Virginia and Tennessee. This 16%-employee-owned private company has 95 grocery stores operating under the Food City and Super Dollar Supermarkets names. K-VA-T Food Stores has its own 1,070,000-foot distribution center, Mid-Mountain Foods, located in Abingdon, Virginia. The company also offers customers private label choices of Food Club, Top Crest and Valu Time through its participation in the Topco cooperative. 				   Brands: Food City, Super Dollar Supermarkets','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5692,'Cook Group',10,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Cook Group, headquartered in Bloomington, Indiana, is a manufacturer and distributor of minimally invasive medical products and interventional devices for radiology, cardiology, oncology, neurology, general surgery, critical care, urology, vascular access and endovascular procedures. The corporation, founded in 1963, includes two companies developing commercial medical products through biotechnology. More than 40 companies in the U.S., Europe, Canada, Australia and Asia produce, manufacture and distribute Cook medical devices. Key divisions include Cook Incorporated, Cook Urological, Wilson-Cook Medical, Sabin Corp., Cook Biotech, Cook Myosite, William Cook Europe, Cook Ireland, Cook Canada, William A. Cook Australia, Cook Vascular and K-Tube Corp. 				   Brands: Zenith, Flexor, Surgisis, Spectrum, Tulip, Zillver, ATB, Detach','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5693,'Guthy-Renker',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Established in 1988, Guthy-Renker originally launched as a television direct marketer by co-chief executives Bill Guthy and Greg Renker. The company is now considered one of the world\'s largest direct response companies. The company sells products to U.S. and international consumers through infomercials on broadcast television, cable and satellite, as well as via telemarketing, direct mail and retail channels.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5694,'International Specialty Products',32,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','International Specialty Holdings is a manufacturer and supplier of chemicals for personal care, pharmaceutical, food, plastics and other applications. It produces over 400 specialty chemicals for over 6000 customers in over 90 countries. International Specialty Holdings is a wholly owned subsidiary of International Specialty Products. It recently acquired Milker & Gruning, Progiven S.A.S., Creative Food Systems, and BP Amoco Chemical Company.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5695,'Vertis',6,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','In July 2000 three advertising and marketing companies: TC Advertising, LTC Group and Webcraft merged and formed Vertis. The company, which has since consolidated these units under the Vertis name, provides advertising and marketing services, including consumer and media research, media planning and placement, creative services, digital media production, direct marketing programs and strategic media consulting. Vertis Retail & Newspaper Services is one of the country\'s largest printers of newspaper advertising inserts. Corporate headquarters are in Baltimore, Maryland.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5696,'Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','In 1924, Metro Pictures, Goldwyn Pictures and Louis B. Mayer Productions merged to form Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer (MGM). Today, the company\'s library has 4,000 titles, including \"Annie Hall,\" \"Dances With Wolves,\" \"Midnight Cowboy,\" and \"The Silence of the Lambs.\" In April 2005, an investor group comprised of Sony Corporation of America, Providence Equity Partners, Texas Pacific Group, Comcast Corporation and DLJ Merchant Banking Partners acquired the company.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5697,'KAR Holdings',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Carmel, Indiana, this company has two main subsidiaries: Adesa and IAAI. Adesa is a provider of wholesale vehicle auctions and used vehicle dealer financing. IAAI specializes in automotive loss salvage service. Adesa\'s operations span North America, with 57 used vehicle auction sites and IAAI has 42 auction sites for salvage vehicles. A private equity group, led by Kelso & Co., acquired Adesa, the parent company, in April 2007.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5698,'Roll International',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Based in Los Angeles, Roll International owns Teleflora (flowers-by-wire), Fiji Water, Paramount Agribusiness (nuts, citrus fruits), Pom Wonderful (fresh pomegranates and juice), and Suterra (pest-control products).','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5699,'Turner Industries Group',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1961, Turner Industries is a general industrial contractor engaged in the maintenance and construction of oil refineries, chemical and petrochemical plants, and pulp and papermills. Corporate headquarters are in Baton Rouge, Louisiana.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5700,'ICC Industries',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','ICC Industries manufactures and trades chemicals, plastics, pharmaceuticals, flavors, fragrances and paints. Founded in 1950, the company has expanded through small acquisitions. Privately held subsidiaries include Dover Chemical, ICC Chemical, ICC Trading, Primex Plastics, O\'Neil Color & Compounding, Pace Industries, Konsyl Pharmaceuticals, Inc. and S.C. Azur.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5701,'Education Management',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Education Management, in business for over 35 years, provides private post-secondary education to over 80,000 students. The company has primary campus locations in 24 states in the U.S. and two Canadian provinces. Its schools offer a broad range of programs culminating in associates through doctoral degrees. Providence Equity Partners and Goldman Sachs\' private equity group acquired Education Management on June 1, 2006.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5702,'Sierra Pacific Industries',25,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','R.H. \"Curly\" Emmerson founded the predecessor of Sierra Pacific Industries in the late 1920s. With his son \"Red\" Emmerson, he built Sierra Pacific into one of the largest lumber companies in the United States. Sierra Pacific, a fully integrated lumber producer, owns 1.7 million acres of timberland throughout California and Washington.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5703,'Austin Industries',17,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','In 1918, the grandfather of Austin Industries\' current chairman, William Solomon, founded Austin Bridge Company. Today Austin Industries is a large, diversified construction company with three subsidiaries&#8212;Austin Bridge & Road, Austin Commercial and Austin Industrial. These divisions engage in civil, commercial and industrial construction. Austin Industries builds commercial and industrial projects such as office buildings, semiconductor factories, airport terminals and petrochemical plants. Dallas projects include the 72-story Bank of America Plaza, the 56-story Texas Commerce Tower and the American Airlines Center (home of the NBA Dallas Mavericks and NHL Dallas Stars). The company became 100% employee owned in 2000.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5704,'ASI Corp.',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','ASI distributes more than 8,000 computer hardware and software products throughout North America. These goods come from companies such as Intel, Microsoft, ViewSonic, Western Digital, Asus, Sony and Samsung. ASI also offers training, marketing, technical support and telemarketing services. Headquartered in Fremont, California, ASI has 14 sales and distribution sites.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:39:56',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5705,'Rooney Holdings',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Formed in 1984 to acquire the Manhattan Construction Company and other assets, Rooney Holdings has since expanded its business to include electronics, concrete place and finish, bridge building and insurance. The company also runs a financial investment subsidiary in Rooney Finance, which invests in various venture capital, real estate and other investment opportunities. Rooney Holdings has operations in the U.S., Mexico, Central America and the Bahamas. L.F. Rooney III is the chairman and chief executive officer of the company, which has its executive offices headquartered in Naples, Florida with administrative offices in Tulsa, Oklahoma.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5706,'NCO Group',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','NCO Group is a global provider of business outsourcing services, focused on accounts receivable management and customer relationship management. NCO provides services through over 100 offices in the United States, Canada, the Philippines, Panama, the Caribbean, India, the United Kingdom and Australia.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5707,'Goss International',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Goss International designs and manufactures web offset printing press systems for newspapers, advertising inserts and commercial printing. The company has foreign operations in Australia, Europe and Asia.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5708,'Bartlett & Co',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Privately held since its incorporation in 1907, Bartlett and Company\'s primary business is grain merchandising, with revenue also generated from flour milling and cattle feeding. Corporate headquarters are in Kansas City, Missouri.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5709,'Williamson-Dickie Manufacturing',31,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1922 in Texas by C.N. Williamson and E.E. \"Colonel\" Dickie, Williamson-Dickie Manufacturing makes branded work clothes, school uniforms, as well as outdoor and casual apparel. Its garments range from its staple work pants and work shirts to items such as women\'s workwear, chore coats and denim jeans. 				   Brands: Dickies','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5710,'Mayer Brown',11,NULL,'','Org','Mayer, Brown, Rowe & Maw LLP employs more than 1,500 lawyers in 14 big cities worldwide including London, Frankfurt, Paris, Chicago, New York, Washington D.C. and Hong Kong. The firm practices in a wide-range of corporate law fieldsâfrom anti-trust to mergers and acquisitions. This company is a combination of two limited liability partnerships, each named Mayer, Brown, Rowe & Maw LLP, one established in Illinois, and one incorporated in England.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany,LobbyingFirm',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-07 06:21:59',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5711,'Safety-Kleen Systems',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Headquartered in Plano, Texas, Safety-Kleen is a provider of industrial waste management services&mdash;collecting, recycling, managing and disposing wastes and industrial chemicals as well as re-refining approximately 160,000,000 gallons of used motor oil each year. Safety-Kleen has more than 200 collection and processing facilities throughout the United States, Canada and Puerto Rico. The company emerged from bankruptcy as a private company in December 2003.','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5712,'Colby College',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Colby is an elite 4-year liberal arts college located in Waterville, Maine','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5713,'SEIU',4,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:37:\"Service Employees International Union\";}','Org','','Org,LaborUnion',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5714,'Public Health Service',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',14640,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5716,'National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency',39,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:39:\"National Geospatial Intelligence Agency\";}','Org','','rg,GovernmentBody',14609,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-22 00:19:04',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5717,'Office of the Chief Information Officer',39,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',14603,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5718,'Assistant Secretary for Administration',38,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',14603,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5719,'National Gallery of Art',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',14635,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5720,'Civilian Health and Medical Program of the Uniformed Services',61,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',14609,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5721,'Immediate Office of the Secretary of Labor',42,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',14682,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5722,'Office of Assistant Secretary for Management and Budget',55,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',14640,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5723,'Wasserstein Perella & Co.',25,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',37041,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5724,'Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee',43,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:59:\"Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee - Contributions\";}','Org','The Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee (DCCC) is the official campaign arm of the Democrats in the House. The DCCC is the only political committee in the country whose principal mission is to support Democratic House candidates every step of the way through this critical election year. Supporting the DCCC is the single most effective step you can take to continue leading our country in a new direction. By securing and strengthening our Democratic majority in 2008 through protecting our Democratic members and electing new progressives to Congress we can keep moving America forward.\r\n\r\nThe DCCC is currently chaired by Congressman Chris Van Hollen (MD-08). Chris Van Hollen was elected to the United States Congress from Maryland\'s 8th District in November 2002. Congressman Van Hollen serves on the Committee for Education and the Workforce and the Committee on Government Reform. He is also the Vice Chair of the Renewable Energy and Energy Efficiency Caucus, a Co-Chair of the Congressional Chesapeake Bay Watershed Task Force, and a Vice-Chair of the Democratic Task Force on Tax Policy and the Budget.','Org,PoliticalFundraising,OtherCampaignCommittee',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5725,'Veterans Employment and Training Services',41,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',14682,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(5726,'National Commission on Libraries and Information Science