','Org,PoliticalFundraising,OtherCampaignCommittee',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9016,'Obama-Biden Transition Project',30,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Obama-Biden Transition Project is the organization supporting the President-elect and Vice President-elect in their transition to power.  The organization is provided for by the Presidential Transition Act of 1963, which authorizes the General Services Administration to provide support for the orderly transition to power of a newly-elected President.  \r\n\r\nThe Presidential Transition Project is the enormous effort of hundreds of people coming together to lay out the agenda and priorities for the Obama Administration. Led by President-Elect Barack Obama, Vice-President Elect Joe Biden, a transition advisory board, and respected leaders from both the public and private sector, the transition is responsible for ensuring that the transfer of power from the current administration to the Obama Administration is smooth and that the continuity of leadership is preserved.\r\n\r\nThe Transition Project is also tasked with reviewing hundreds of agencies and programs in the federal government and selecting new personnel to manage these important offices. Among the personnel that will be selected will be new Cabinet members, national security and federal law enforcement officials, non-career appointments, and other heads of agencies across the Executive Branch.\r\n\r\nWe will keep this transition process transparent, so that you will know which officials are being selected to serve in this administration and lead the country for the next four years. All staff appointments chosen for this administration will be committed to fulfilling Obamaâs campaign promises, to rebuilding our government, and to serving the American people again.','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9017,'The Albright Group',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','A business consulting firm with a global bent, founded by former Secretary of State Madeline Albright in 2001.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9018,'Alliance for Climate Protection',31,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded by Al Gore, among others, the organization is backing a major campaign to reduce greenhouse gas emission and find and implement solutions to the climate crisis.','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9019,'Brookings Institution',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:14:\"Brookings Inst\";}','Org','','Org,NonProfit,ThinkTank',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-08 06:37:55',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9020,'The University of Michigan Law School',37,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9021,'Cosmos Club',11,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,MembershipOrg,SocialClub',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9022,'United States Court of Appeals for the Federal Circuit',54,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9023,'Federal Reserve Bank of New York',32,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',15957,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9024,'Economic Policy Working Group',29,NULL,'','Org','Developing policy options and initiatives to enable the President-elect to tackle both the immediate economic crisis and the long term economic goals set during the campaign.  Also developing a two-year economic recovery plan that will create or save 2.5 million jobs by rebuilding crumbling roads and bridges, modernizing schools, investing in alternative energy, and providing immediate relief to middle class families.','Org,GovernmentBody',33161,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-07 06:21:59',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9025,'Center for a New American Security',34,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Center for a New American Security (CNAS) is a Washington, D.C.-based think tank established in 2007 by co-founders and former Clinton Administration officials MichÃ¨le Flournoy and Kurt M. Campbell. It specializes in U.S. national security issues and its self-described orientation is towards  \"pragmatic and principled national security and defense policies that promote and protect American interests and values.\"','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9026,'American Patrons of Tate',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Philanthropy,Cultural',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9027,'Americans for Jobs, Health Care and Progressive Values',54,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','527 formed to take out Howard Dean in 2004\r\n\r\nhttp://query.nytimes.com/gst/fullpage.html?res=9F02E2D9113CF935A25751C1A9659C8B63','Org,Pac',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9028,'Skull & Bones',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Skull and Bones is an elite secret society based at Yale University, in New Haven, Connecticut. The society\'s alumni organization, which owns the society\'s real property and oversees the organization\'s activity, is known as the Russell Trust Association, and is named after General William Huntington Russell[1] founding member of the Bones\' organization along with fellow classmate Alphonso Taft. In conversation, the group is known as \"Bones\", and members have been known as \"Bonesmen\".[2]','Org,MembershipOrg',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9029,'Milton Academy',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9030,'American Bar Association',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,IndustryTrade',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9031,'National Bureau of Economic Research',36,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:4:\"NBER\";}','Org','','Org,ThinkTank',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-22 00:29:34',NULL,0,'deleted',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9032,'President\'s Economic Recovery Administration',44,NULL,'','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',28677,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-07 06:21:59',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9033,'Northfield Mount Herman',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9034,'Chicago Stock Exchange',22,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9035,'AREVA, Inc',10,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9036,'The Abraham Group LLC',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9037,'American Research and Development Corporation',45,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9038,'Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum',31,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,NonProfit,Cultural',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9039,'New England Aquarium',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,NonProfit,Cultural',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9040,'Obama Transition Economic Advisory Board',40,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:40:\"Obama Transition Economic Advisory Board\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',33161,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9041,'Obama-Biden National Security Policy Working Group',50,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:55:\"Obama Transition National Security Policy Working Group\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',33161,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9042,'Center for Global Development',29,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','CGD is an independent, not-for-profit think tank that works to reduce global poverty and inequality by encouraging policy change in the U.S. and other rich countries through rigorous research and active engagement with the policy community.','Org,NonProfit,ThinkTank',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9043,'United States Mission to the United Nations',43,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9044,'Lerner Reed Bolton & McManus',28,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business,LawFirm',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9045,'Yale Law School',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',14952,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9046,'Federal Open Market Committee',29,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:4:\"FOMC\";}','Org','The Federal Reserve controls the three tools of monetary policy--open market operations, the discount rate, and reserve requirements. The Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System is responsible for the discount rate and reserve requirements, and the Federal Open Market Committee is responsible for open market operations. Using the three tools, the Federal Reserve influences the demand for, and supply of, balances that depository institutions hold at Federal Reserve Banks and in this way alters the federal funds rate. The federal funds rate is the interest rate at which depository institutions lend balances at the Federal Reserve to other depository institutions overnight.','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9047,'Kissinger Associates, Inc.',26,NULL,'a:3:{i:0;s:0:\"\";i:1;s:24:\"Kissenger and Associates\";i:2;s:24:\"Kissinger and Associates\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-08 20:47:00',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9048,'Council on Foreign Relations',28,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:3:\"CFR\";}','Org','','Org,MembershipOrg,NonProfit,ThinkTank',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9049,'Group of Thirty',15,NULL,'','Org','The Group of Thirty, often abbreviated to G30, is an international body of leading financiers and academics which aims to deepen understanding of economic and financial issues and to examine consequences of decisions made in the public and private sectors related to these issues.\n\nThe Group aims to deepen understanding of international economic and financial issues, to explore the international repercussions of decisions taken in the public and private sectors, and to examine the choices available to market practitioners and policymakers.','Org,MembershipOrg,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-07 06:21:59',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9050,'Obama Transition Energy & Environment Policy Working Group',58,NULL,'','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',33161,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-07 06:21:59',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9051,'Obama Transition Health Care Policy Working Group',49,NULL,'','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',33161,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-07 06:42:23',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9052,'American Automobile Manufacturers Association',45,NULL,'','Org','','Org,MembershipOrg,IndustryTrade',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-07 06:42:42',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9053,'United Way of America',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Philanthropy',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9054,'Iraq Study Group',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Iraq Study Group made a forward-looking, independent assessment of the current and prospective situation on the ground in Iraq and how it affects the surrounding region as well as U.S. interests.\r\n\r\nThe study group examined four broad topics:\r\n\r\n    * the strategic environment in and around Iraq;\r\n    * the security of Iraq and key challenges to enhancing security within the country;\r\n    * political developments within Iraq following the elections and formation of the new government;\r\n    * and the economy and reconstruction.\r\n\r\nThe effort was undertaken at the urging of several members of Congress with agreement of the White House. A final report was released to Congress, the White House, and the public on December 6, 2006.','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9055,'Parker Drilling Company',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Parker Drilling Company provides drilling services on land and offshore including drilling rigs, project management and rental tools to the energy industry. Parkerâs expertise extends to every region of the worldâfrom the U.S. Gulf of Mexico to the jungles of Papua New Guinea and the mountains, seas and deserts in between.\r\n\r\nParker\'s land fleet of 28 rigs operates in 9 countries. The companyâs offshore fleet of 17 rigs consists of barge rigs in the Caspian Sea, Mexico and the U.S. Gulf of Mexico.\r\n\r\nThrough project management expertise, Parker operates rigs owned by third parties and provides additional services such as engineering, logistics, health, safety, and environmental programs, human resources, quality programs, preventive maintenance and alliance management.\r\n\r\nParker subsidiary Quail Tools is a leading provider of specialized rental equipment for drilling and workover operations, with six U.S. locations on the Gulf coast, in Texas and the Rocky Mountains.','Org,Business,PublicCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9056,'The Hamilton Project',20,NULL,'a