" in   _The Washington Report on Middle East Affairs_. at http://www.wrmea.com/backissues/0393/9303009.htm .','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9119,'Harvard Law Review',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:22:\"The Harvard Law Review\";}','Org','','Org',14713,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9120,'American Israel Public Affairs Committee (AIPAC)',48,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:5:\"AIPAC\";}','Org','Everyone in Washington agrees AIPAC has had a profound influence on Middle East policy set on Capitol Hill. From AIPAC.org: \"For more than half a century, the American Israel Public Affairs Committee has worked to help make Israel more secure by ensuring that American support remains strong.  From a small pro-Israel public affairs boutique in the 1950s, AIPAC has grown into a 100,000-member national grassroots movement described by The New York Times as \'the most important organization affecting America\'s relationship with Israel.\'\"\r\n\r\nAIPAC\'s policies are generally in line with the more hawkish end of the Israeli political spectrum. Former AIPAC officials have been embroiled in an espionage scandal involving former defence analyst Lawrence \"Larry\" Franklin.','Org,NonProfit,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9121,'Developing Communities Project',30,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9122,'ACTION',6,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','ACTION was a United States government agency described as, \"the Federal Domestic Volunteer Agency\".[1] It was formed in 1970 from VISTA; the Peace Corps; and the Foster Grandparents, Retired and Senior Volunteer, and Senior Companion Programs (later merged into the Senior Corps).[2][3] In 1993 the Corporation for National and Community Service was created by merging ACTION and the Commission on National and Community Service together, thus ending ACTION.','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9123,'Knox College',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9124,'Saban Center for Middle East Policy (The Brookings Institution)',63,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:25:\"The Brookings Institution\";}','Org','','Org,ThinkTank',33171,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9125,'The Australian National University',34,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9126,'The University of Sydney',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9127,'National Football League',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9128,'Stuyvesant High School',22,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9129,'Superior Court of the District of Columbia',42,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9130,'South Asian American Voting Youth',33,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9131,'Carr Center for Human Rights',28,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9132,'National Women\'s Law Center',27,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(9133,'Obama Transition Education Policy Working Group',47,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:47:\"Obama Transition