ement of Americans who promote mental wellness for the health and well-being of the nation â everyday and in times of crisis.','Org,LawFirm',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(12747,'American College of Surgeons',28,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,MembershipOrg',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(12748,'House Energy & Commerce Subcommittee on Health & Environment',60,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(12749,'Lewis-Burke Associates',22,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Our clients\' interests are best served when federal policy makers are fully informed. We make it a priority to understand all aspects of our clients\' public policy agenda so that we can expertly represent them in front of various federal decision makers. For more than a decade, we have used this approach to successfully develop and carry out comprehensive government relations and communications strategies for our clients.','Org,LobbyingFirm',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(12750,'Senate Legislative Counsel',26,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(12751,'Senate Select Nutrition & Human Needs Committee',47,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(12752,'Cavarocchi Ruscio Dennis Assoc',30,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Our clients include nonprofit organizations, corporations, municipalities and trade associationsâeach of which benefits from our years of experience and results-oriented approach to lobbying.','Org,LobbyingFirm',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(12753,'GGV Capital',11,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The firm was founded in 2000 by four managing directors: Scott Bonham, Joel Kellman, Hany Nada, and Thomas Ng.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(12754,'Mayfield Fund',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(12755,'Venrock',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(12756,'August Capital',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(12757,'Draper Richards, LP',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Draper name is well known in the venture capital industry. Bill Draperâs father, General William H. Draper, Jr., became the first professional west-coast venture capitalist when he founded Draper, Gaither & Anderson in 1958. Formerly Undersecretary of the Army, General Draper was responsible for economic reconstruction of Germany and Japan under the Marshall Plan. \r\n\r\nBill Draper began his venture capital career in 1962 with Pitch Johnson, when he started Draper & Johnson Investment Company. In 1965, together with Paul Wythes, he founded Sutter Hill Ventures which was managed with great success until 1981, when he was appointed Chairman of the U.S. Export-Import Bank. In 1985, he was selected to be Administrator and CEO of the United Nations Development Program. While in the venture capital business, Bill Draper was a founding investor in Apollo Computer (acquired by Hewlett Packard), Dionex, Integrated Genetics (Genzyme), Quantum, Qume (I.T.T.), Activision (Mediagenic), Xidex (Eastman Kodak), Measurex, Hybritech (Eli Lilly), and LSI Logic. In 1995, he returned to venture capital by founding Draper International which focused on venture investments in India. In 1996, he turned his attention to technology companies in the U.S. and co-founded a new domestic fund, Draper Richards L.P., with his partner, Robin Richards Donohoe. \r\n\r\nBill Draperâs son, Tim Draper, left Alex. Brown & Sons in 1985 to become the third generation of venture capitalists in his family with the formation of Draper Fisher Jurvetson. Tim restructured a family-owned Small Business Investment Company (SBIC) that had been set up by his father in 1979 and then created a highly successful early-stage venture capital fund. Draper Fisher Jurvetson has become synonymous with early-stage venture capital. Among other successes, Tim Draper was a founding investor in Parametric Technology, Digidesign, Parenting Magazine, Upside Publishing, PLX Technology, Four-1-1, Hotmail, and Skype.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(12758,'National Fuel Gas Distribution Corporation',42,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(12759,'National Fuel Gas Supply Corporation',36,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(12760,'Seneca Resources Corporation',28,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(12761,'National Fuel Resources, Inc.',29,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(12762,'Highland Forest Resources, Inc.',31,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(12763,'Keilin & Bloom',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(12764,'Jewish Labor Committee',22,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,LaborUnion',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),