:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13100,'Technology Crossover Ventures (TCV)',35,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','With 29 investment professionals and nearly $8 billion under management across seven funds, TCV is one of the largest growth equity firms focused solely on information technology companies.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13101,'Apollo Alliance',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Apollo was launched in the aftermath of the 9/11 tragedy to catalyze a clean energy revolution in America, a revolution in the way our country generates and uses energy so profound that it will touch literally every quarter of American life. Harkening back to President Kennedyâs visionary call to restore Americaâs technological leadership by landing the first man on the Moon within the decade, the Apollo Alliance spoke directly to the core values we share as Americans: our can-do spirit, our inherent optimism, and the pride we feel (or want to feel) about our countryâs place in the world. The subtext was clear: we did it before, we can do it again. This is America, the richest, most technologically advanced and industrious country in the world. If anyone can do it, we can. And we will.\r\nNot surprisingly, the Apollo message captured the imagination of people throughout the country. Soon our phone lines were buzzing with calls from political leaders of all stripes wanting to find out what they could do in their states, in their cities, and at the national level to advance Apolloâs clean energy agenda. Apollo responded to the increasing demand for our work by establishing Apollo coalitions in nine states and five cities to promote policy change consistent with our Ten-Point Plan for reducing Americaâs dependence on foreign oil. We released highly regarded energy analyses that confirmed the economic benefits of converting to a clean energy economy and published guides outlining specific strategies for investing in clean energy, greater energy efficiency, and innovative transit and transportation solutions.','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13102,'Canyon  -Johnson Urban Communities Fund',39,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Fund will acquire existing residential rental properties in select major U.S. markets - creating value by upgrading units, adding amenities, improving management, and creating a secure, high quality brand of urban living for working families. The Fund will break new ground in \"greening\" multifamily rental properties, and it will implement resident services programs such as English as a second language, financial planning classes, and after-school tutoring to build a strong sense of community and to create a pride of rentership.\r\n\r\nFormer California State Treasurer Phil Angelides, is chairman of the Fund. Angelides has earned a national reputation over the last 30 years in both the private and public sectors for his pioneering work in urban reinvestment, housing, green investment and smart growth.\r\n\r\nIn keeping with the long standing commitments of Canyon-Johnson and its principals, the Fund will focus on the \"triple bottom line\" investment strategy of achieving successful financial results, fostering opportunities for underserved urban neighborhoods and their residents, and embracing environmental responsibility.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13103,'Johnson Development Corporation',31,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13104,'Financial Crisis Inquiry Commission',35,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13105,'California State Assembly Committee Assignments',47,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13106,'California State Senate Committee',33,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13107,'Republican Main Street Partnership',34,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Republican Main Street Partnership was founded in 1998 to promote thoughtful leadership in the Republican Party, and to partner with individuals, organizations and institutions that share centrist values.\r\nThe Partnership is comprised of party members and public officials who are fiscally conservative deficit hawks. The Partnership is working to Grow Our Party through a pragmatic approach to governing that reaches out to a broad base of Americans who share the Republican ideals of fiscal responsibility and limited government. The Partnership contributes to the nation\'s governance through developing and promoting creative public policies for implementation at appropriate levels of government.','Org,Pac',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13108,'Matsui Victory Fund 2008',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Pac',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13109,'Business Industry PAC',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:44:\"Business-Industry Political Action Committee\";}','Org','BIPAC enables more effective business participation in the political process. It does not lobby. Instead, BIPAC offers a wide range of tools and strategies to help 3,600+ businesses and associations reach their public policy goals.  BIPAC, with deployment partners in more than 30 states, takes an integrated approach to political involvement, combining grassroots advocacy and PAC Resources, all directed by nationally recognized political analysis','Org,Pac,PoliticalFundraising,OtherCampaignCommittee',39682,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13110,'Sloat, Higgins, Jensen & Associates',35,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Successful governmental advocacy today requires political and policy knowledge, strategic abilities, and communication skills. SHJ&A staff uses these skills to best serve the clientâs interests to their fullest capabilities.\r\n\r\nSHJ&A assists their clients in identifying their advocacy goals, and creates a strategy to achieve those goals. SHJ&A ensures that appropriate governmental officials understand the policy and political implications of the clientâs goals, and works with communication professionals to market the clientâs perspective to the media and the public. SHJ&A has proven grass-roots lobbying and coalition building skills, helping to achieve its clientsâ goals by successfully working with other organizations and people who share the same objectives.\r\n\r\nTerm limits, campaign reform, and reduction in government services have changed the way businesses, trade associations and local government agencies work with state government agencies and officials. SHJ&A successfully helps organizations achieve their advocacy goals through professional representation and a unique understanding of the governmental process.','Org,LobbyingFirm',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13111,'California Democratic Party',27,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13112,'Bay City Capital',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Bay City Capital LLC (Bay City Capital) was established in 1997 for the purpose of managing investment funds in the life sciences industry. Since that date, we\'ve managed six venture funds representing $1.5 billion in capital invested in over 70 companies. Five of these funds are general life sciences funds, and one is a nutrition and agribusiness sector fund.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13113,'M/C Venture Partners',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13114,'Adelphi University',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13115,'Fund For Wisconsinn Scholars',28,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Fund for Wisconsin Scholars provides grants that open the door to a better world, helping ensure that higher education is accessible and affordable, and that degree completion is achieved. The intellectual capacity of every person is of more value than ever in our global, knowledge-based economy. We hope to expand this capacity for the enrichment of all. Increasing the number of students who complete post-secondary education will improve the quality of life for Wisconsin citizens by benefiting both the individual and society.','Org,School,Philanthropy',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13116,'CARE (humanitarian)',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','CARE is a leading humanitarian organization fighting global poverty. We place special focus on working alongside poor women because, equipped with the proper resources, women have the power to help whole families and entire communities escape poverty. Women are at the heart of CARE\'s community-based efforts to improve basic education, prevent the spread of HIV, increase access to clean water and sanitation, expand economic opportunity and protect natural resources. CARE also delivers emergency aid to survivors of war and natural disasters, and helps people rebuild their lives.','Org,Philanthropy',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13117,'Cisco Learning Institute (501c3 Organization)',45,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13118,'Morgridge Institute of Research',31,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Morgridge Institute for Research is a new, private, not-for-profit interdisciplinary biomedical research organization dedicated to the vision of âDiscovery to Delivery,â  of accelerating the movement of science from the laboratories of researchers to public use around the world as treatments and cures.  It is associated with and located on the campus of the University of Wisconsin-Madison, consistently one of the top research universities in the world.\r\n\r\nThe Morgridge Institute  is part of the twin institutes of the Wisconsin Institutes for Discovery a public-private initiative that facilitates interdisciplinary research and breakthrough discoveries to advance human health and well-being. The new state-of-the-art facility housing the institutes will open in December 2010.','Org,Business,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-21 23:59:46',NULL,0,'deleted',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13119,'The Morgridge Family Foundation',31,NULL,'','Org','','Org,Philanthropy',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-07 06:21:59',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13120,'Freedom Action',14,NULL,'','Org','','Org,MembershipOrg,NonProfit',41886,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-07 06:21:59',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13121,'Haas Center for Public Service',30,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13122,'Morgridge Center for Public Service',35,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13123,'SKS Investments',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13124,'McCain-Palin Victory In California-Republican',45,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active