s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13161,'Longleaf Pine PAC',17,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13162,'nafta',5,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13163,'Institutional Venture Partners (IVP)',36,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','IVP\'s founder, Reid Dennis, is one of the pioneers of the venture capital industry. In 1952, six months after leaving Stanford University armed with his BSEE and MBA degrees, Reid invested $20,000, which was virtually all he had to his name, in privately-held Ampex Corporation in Redwood City. Fortunately for Reid, that first investment was very successful, and after Ampex went public, that $20,000 stake grew to over $1 million in market value during the next several years. \r\n\r\nIn 1974, backed by a $5 million commitment from American Express (his former employer), Reid formed Institutional Venture Associates (IVA) and raised $19 million from six institutions. That was roughly half of all the capital raised in the United States that year by private venture capital partnerships. Over the life of IVA, the original $19 million grew to over $180 million. In 1980, Reid then formed Institutional Venture Partners (IVP) and the firm has grown into one of the most successful venture capital and growth equity firms in the industry.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13164,'Mobius Venture Capital',22,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13165,'San Francisco Republican County Central Cmte Federal Fund',57,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13166,'Taxpayers\' for Better Government',32,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13167,'Cigna Corporation Political Action Committee',44,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13168,'Morgenthaler Ventures',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13169,'Qiming Venture Partners',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13170,'California Republican Party',27,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalParty',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13171,'NO ON 8 EQUALITY CALIFORNIA',27,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Pac',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13172,'Norwest',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13173,'University of Texas System',26,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:25:\"Univerity of Texas System\";}','Org','The System administration is based in Austin, Texas. Offices are also located in Midland, Texas (University Lands/West Texas Operations) and Washington, D.C. (Federal Relations). These offices are responsible for the central management and coordination of the academic and health institutions.','rg,School,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-22 00:29:39',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13174,'California Commission for Jobs and Economic Growth',50,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13175,'Brookfield Properties Corporation',33,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Brookfield Properties is a commercial real estate corporation that owns, develops, and operates premier assets in the downtown cores of high-growth North American cities. Our signature properties define the skylines of many major metropolises including New York, Boston, Washington, D.C., Los Angeles, Houston, Toronto, and Calgary. Brookfield Properties is a publicly traded company, and is listed under the ticker symbol BPO on both the New York and Toronto Stock Exchanges.\r\n\r\nFrom the World Financial Center in New York to Brookfield Place in Toronto, from Bankers Hall in Calgary to Bank of America Plaza in Los Angeles, Brookfield Properties\' distinguished portfolio attracts major financial, energy and professional services corporations which have high credit ratings and maintain long-term leases. The companyâs performance through the years is distinguished by strong, consistent financial results and a track record of steady growth.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13176,'Aetna Foundation',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','John H. Filer is widely recognized as the \"Father of Corporate Philanthropy.\" He strongly believed that corporations have an obligation to their communities, and believed both giving and volunteering are vital to building and maintaining healthy communities. As Aetna\'s Chairman in 1972, Filer created the Aetna Foundation, the independent philanthropic arm of Aetna.\r\n\r\nIn 1973, President Richard Nixon asked Filer to head the Commission on Private Philanthropy and Public Needs to study the role of philanthropy in the United States. The Commission became known as the \"Filer Commission.\"','Org,Philanthropy',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13177,'Council for Affordable Quality Healthcare',41,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','CAQH, an unprecedented nonprofit alliance of health plans and trade associations, is a catalyst for industry collaboration on initiatives that simplify healthcare administration. CAQH solutions promote quality interactions between plans, providers and other stakeholders; reduce costs and frustrations associated with healthcare administration; facilitate administrative healthcare information exchange and encourage administrative and clinical data integration.','Org,NonProfit,IndustryTrade',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13178,'Connecticut Science Center',26,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','How do you get young people interested in science? Engage them.\r\n\r\nWith 150 hands-on exhibits, a state-of-the-art 3D digital theater, four educational labs, plus daily programs and events, the Connecticut Science Center offers endless exploration for children, teens and adults. Every part of science will be at a visitor\'s fingertips, from Physics to Forensics, Geology to Astronomy.\r\n\r\nThe Connecticut Science Center has changed much more than a skyline. Our unique features will captivate millions of visitors over the years. The constant stream of visitors will mean business for Connecticut hotels, restaurants and retailers year round.','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13179,'MIT North America Executive Board',33,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13180,'Alford P Sloan Management Society',33,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Fifteen of the nation\'s most seasoned business executives have been selected Founding Members of a new MIT Sloan School of Management organization that will enable them to bring their expertise directly into the classroom while serving as an informal âsounding boardâ on curriculum and other issues for MIT Sloan administrators and faculty members.','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13181,'National Intelligence Senior Advisory Group',43,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13182,'Wesleyan University in Indiana',30,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13183,'United States Government - Central Intelligence Agency',54,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Don\'t ask me how I know. Just look into it, unless you\'re afraid of them coming for you also.','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13184,'Vista Health Care Group',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13185,'Control Data Corporation',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13186,'Syntegra',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Syntegra specializes in managing the full life cycle deployment of IT solutions, creating next-generation IT competitive advantages, and leading transformational business initiatives. Our unique approach, emphasizing Syntegra enables our clients better respond to rapidly changing business needs and meet Managementâs demands for return on IT spending, while maintaining focus on their core business. We do this through our core solution offerings: Syntegra Enterprise Management, Syntegra Applications, Syntegra Securityâs, Syntegra Learning, Syntegra Outsourcing and Syntegra On Demand\r\n\r\nSyntegra provides project management, systems architecture, development, integration, implementation, and maintenance services to support Infrastructure, Packaged Software, Custom Applications, Security, Training, Outsourcing, and Staff Augmentation.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13187,'Integrative Systems',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13188,'Syncor International Corporation',32,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13189,'Cardinal Health 414 Inc',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Cardinal Health 414, Inc. provides radio pharmacy services in the United States. The company offers Total Solution, which is used in compounding, delivery, safety, consulting, information technology, and business support services. It also offers services in regulatory compliance, reimbursement, practice development, continuing education, and information management. The company, through its network of pharmacies, offers radiopharmaceuticals and ancillary products used in nuclear medicine to create images that aid in diagnosing disease, planning treatment regimens, and evaluating a patientâs progress and response to therapy. Cardinal Health 414, Inc. was founded in 1974 as Syncor International Corporation and changed its name to Cardinal Health 414, Inc. in April 2003 following its acquisition by Cardinal Health, Inc. The company is based in Woodland Hills, California. Cardinal Health 414, Inc. operates as a subsidiary of Cardinal Health, Inc.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13190,'Sentigen Holding Corporation',28,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','It operates in two divisions, Sentigen Biosciences and Cell & Molecular Technologies. The Sentigen Biosciences division engages primarily in the development and commercialization of novel bioassay systems that elucidate the underlying biology of protein-protein interactions. It offers its Tango assay system to address the functionalization of G protein-coupled receptors for pharmaceutical drug discovery and development. The Cell & Molecular Technologies division provides contract research and development services to companies, which engage in the drug discovery process; as well as works in cooperation with Sentigen Biosciences to commercialize specific applications of the Tango assay system. Sentigen Holding was founded in 1987. It was formerly known as Prime Cellular, Inc. and changed its name to Sentigen Holding Corp. in 2000. The company is based in Phillipsburg, New Jersey. Sentigen Holding Corp. is a subsidiary of Life Technologies Corporation.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13191,'YMCAA',5,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Nearly 10 million children ages 17 and under engage in a wealth of enriching YMCA activities. \r\nTogether, YMCAs are the nationâs largest provider of child care, with nearly 10,000 child care sites across the country that provide high-quality, affordable care to more than 500,000 children. \r\nYMCAs help families build bonds, connect with community resources and become strong and self-sufficient. \r\nFor more than eight decades, YMCAs have offered Adventure Guides and similar programs that bring parents and children together. \r\nYMCAs are collectively the nationâs largest providers of health and well-being programs. \r\nYMCAs are working to promote healthy living for millions of Americans through YMCA Activate AmericaÂ®. Learn more about YMCA Activate America. \r\nFinancial assistanceâmade possible annually by more than $1.6 billion in public and private support, as well as YMCA membersâopens all YMCA programs to those in need. \r\nVolunteer founded and volunteer led, YMCAs depend on the generosity and dedication of their 548,926 volunteers across the United States. \r\nAmericaâs 2,686 YMCAs are collectively one of the largest not-for-profit community service organizations in the United States. \r\n64 million households and 32 million children ages 14 and under live within three miles of a YMCA, while 1,518 YMCAs serve communities where the median family income is below the U.S. average. \r\nThe YMCA is one of the largest volunteer organizations in the world, serving more than 45 million people in 124 countries. Learn more about YMCA World Service. \r\nThe nationâs YMCAs collectively represent one of the largest collaborative organizations in the country.','Org,Philanthropy',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13192,'SRI International',17,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13193,'DaimlerChrysler AG',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13194,'Bestfoods',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13195,'Thomson Reuters Foundation',26,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The charitable arm of Thomson Reuters, it leverages the skills and expertise across the corporation to increase trust and access to the rule of law, to save lives through the provision of trusted information and to improve standards of journalism.','Org,Philanthropy,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13196,'Milliken & Company, Inc.',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13197,'The Cue Ball Group LLC',22,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','We help take nascent opportunities to scale by connecting great people to pioneering ideas. The capabilities of our investment professionals are amplified through collaboration with The Cue Ball Collective â a brain trust of experienced executives, industry thought leaders, and entrepreneurs. Our Limited Partners are invited to participate in Cue Ball Capital based on their ability and desire to play value-added roles rather than their ability to provide capital.\r\n\r\nA core tenet of Cue Ballâs strategy is to look for investment opportunities where others are not. This outlook stems from an entrepreneurial heritage coupled with a deeply strategic approach.  We have a strong bias for under-the-radar, pioneering companies which demonstrate the potential to redefine their category.  The companies we typically back have $1 to $25M in annual revenue and positive earnings. We will consider opportunities outside of this scope, including seed and buyout opportunities.\r\n\r\nCue Ballâs founding team of investment professionals and advisory board members have known each other and, in many cases, worked together over the past decade. Together, we seek to build a firm to which entrepreneurs and business owners turn to first when they decide to reach the next level of growth.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13198,'Norwalk Community College Foundation',36,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13199,'John Hopkins Bloomberg School of Public Health',46,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-21 23:58:30',NULL,0,'deleted',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13200,'Hillcrest Health Service Systems, Inc',37,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13201,'Vical Incorporated',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13202,'Journal of Health Economics',27,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,MediaOrg',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13203,'National Bureau of Economics Research',37,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:36:\"National Bureau of Economic Research\";}','Org','','rg,ThinkTank,NonProfit,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04