e.  Benefits brokers and financial services organizations of all sizes â from the industryâs largest and strongest brands to smaller regional firms â trust their customers and reputations to Digital Insurance.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13595,'Water Street Healthcare Partners',32,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13596,'North Peak Capital LLC',22,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Our goal is to work in partnership with talented managers to build profitable, sustainable businesses, with the ultimate objective of realizing superior risk-adjusted returns for our investors, our management partners and ourselves.  \r\n\r\nThe following operating principles guide our operating model and our investment approach:\r\n\r\nPartnership.   We are active investors â committed to providing responsible, long-term oriented, strategic and operational guidance to our companies.\r\nFocus.  By explicitly limiting our investment activities to a narrow range of opportunities, we are able to offer greater value to our management partners and to provide better stewardship of capital for our investors.\r\nIntegrity.   We operate with unwavering honesty and integrity.\r\nCourage.  We act boldly and intelligently at all times, measuring risk and seeking it when the reward is more than commensurate.\r\nIn order to enable us to operate under the above principles, we do relatively few investments and invest significant personal capital in each investment.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13597,'inVentiv Health Inc',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Thousands of pharmaceutical and healthcare products are conceived and developed in labs every year â yet only a small percentage will receive regulatory approval, and even fewer will ever achieve robust commercial success. The journey to bring such products from molecule to market is complex and filled with unforeseen challenges. You need a powerful partner to forge a clear path to success.\r\ninVentiv Health brings clarity to the intricate issues facing the healthcare industry and provides the tools and talent that you need to succeed. An unmatched depth and breadth of expertise in clinical development, launch, and commercialization gives us a big picture perspective. Using this insight, we develop and deploy innovative, multidisciplinary solutions to help brands make their mark.\r\nHow can inVentiv Health accelerate your vision for success? Explore our site and see how inVentiv makes it happen.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13598,'Union Street Acquisition Corporation',36,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13599,'Tower Three Partners LLC',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13600,'National Campaign to Prevent Teen and Unplanned Pregnancy',57,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13601,'Information Technology Innovation Foundation',44,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13602,'John Marshall Law School',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The John Marshall Law School provides one of the most comprehensive and\r\naggressive professional skills training curricula in the country, including trial and appellate advocacy, alternative dispute resolution, client counseling, negotiations and legal drafting.','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13603,'First Berkshire Hathaway Life',29,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13604,'Emergency Medical Services Corporation',38,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','EMSC operates two business segments: American Medical Response, Inc. (AMR), the Companyâs healthcare transportation services segment, and EmCare Holdings Inc. (EmCare), the Companyâs outsourced emergency department and hospital-based physician services segment.\r\nAMR is the leading provider of ambulance services in the United States.\r\nEmCare is the nationâs leading provider of outsourced emergency department and hospital-based physician services.\r\nIn 2007, EMSC provided services to 10.6 million patients in more than 2,000 communities nationwide.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13605,'Skilled Healthcare Group Inc',28,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The skilled nursing facility operations have a reputation for treating patients who require a high level of skilled nursing care and extensive rehabilitation therapy. Each of the operating company subsidiaries has local leadership for greater community integration while receiving a full range of administrative and consultative support services from our administrative service subsidiary, Skilled Healthcare, LLC.\r\n\r\nOur subsidiaries operate skilled nursing facilities and assisted living facilities, together comprising approximately 10,500 licensed beds. Skilled Healthcare Group subsidiaries collectively own approximately 74% of these facilities, which are located in California, Texas, Kansas, Missouri, New Mexico, Nevada and Iowa and are generally clustered in large urban or suburban markets.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13606,'Carestream Health Inc',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Carestream Health, Inc., is an internationally successful company providing medical and dental imaging systems and information technology solutions; molecular imaging systems; and non-destructive testing products to a broad base of customers around the world.\r\nOnex Corporation, Toronto, Canada, acquired the Health Group of Eastman Kodak Company in a multi-billion-dollar transaction in May 2007.  Upon closing, the business began operating as a standalone entity (i.e., Carestream Health, Inc.) within the Onex family of companies.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-21 23:44:50',NULL,0,'deleted',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13607,'Connecticut Children\'s Medical Center',37,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Services\r\nConnecticut Children\'s Medical Center is a caring, full-service hospital for the benefit of all of our patients. Our philosophy is child-and family-centered with sensitivity to cultural diversity. We provide leadership in developing child health services in our communities and in advocating for children. \r\n\r\nEducation\r\nConnecticut Children\'s Medical Center is committed to advancing child health through education and serves as a major regional pediatric resource. We encourage and support programs for health professionals, children, families, and the community. \r\n\r\nResearch\r\nConnecticut Children\'s Medical Center is committed to advancing child health through research. We encourage and support basic, clinical, and health services research of regional and national significance.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13608,'Evolution Benefits Inc',22,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13609,'Tekelec',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Telecom operators are in the process of making the transition from TDM/SS7 systems to next-generation IP, and then beyond that, IMS. Industry watchers agree this transition could be a 10-year or more cycle, and they concur the transition is evolutionary.\r\n\r\nTo manage the transition, Tekelec provides practical solutions that enable operators to offer new, revenue-generating multimedia services while leveraging their existing infrastructure and taking a stepped approach to all-IP networks.\r\n\r\nTekelec solutions are already trusted in the core of major telecom operator networks around the globe, including eight of 10 of the worldâs largest wireless telecom operators and six of 10 of the worldâs largest wireline telecom operators. In 2007 alone, Tekelec solutions went into 23 new customer networks.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13610,'Saif Partners',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13611,'Advance Technology Ventures (ATV)',33,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:3:\"ATV\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13612,'http://www.esctriangle.org/',27,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13613,'Executive Service Corps: Durham',31,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Executive Service Corps of the Greater Triangle has been helping nonprofits in the Research Triangle area since 1987. Originally founded as the International Executive Service Corps in 1966 by David Rockefeller, it recruited retired corporate executives to work overseas on assignments in developing countries.\r\n\r\nA decade later, this concept was reshaped to permit retired executives to use their managerial skills on behalf of American nonprofit agencies.\r\n\r\nESC of the Greater Triangle is one of approximately 30 similar agencies that are affiliated with the Executive Service Corps Affiliate Network. This relationship gives us a perspective on the challenges and opportunities facing nonprofits throughout the U.S. and allows us to access programs and services that can help local nonprofits.','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13614,'Domain Associates',17,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13615,'GSR Ventures',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13616,'Orion Healthcare Equity',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13617,'Trinity Ventures',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13618,'Wachovia Capital Partners',25,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13619,'James Irvine Foundation',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Philanthropy',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13620,'Azure Capital Partners',22,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13621,'Venture Investors LLC',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13622,'Norwest Venture Partners',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13623,'New Leaf Ventures (NLV)',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Sprout Group was formed in 1969 and has historically been one of the leading venture capital firms in the country. The team started to invest in healthcare technology in 1993 and since then, has become a leading venture investor in that sector. In 2005, the entire healthcare technology team of Sprout spun out into NLV. This team continues to manage the healthcare technology portfolio of the Sprout funds in 2005, the team closed on its first directly-managed fund, New Leaf Ventures I, L.P., a $310 million healthcare technology-dedicated fund. In 2007, the team closed on its second fund, New Leaf Ventures II, L.P., a fund also dedicated to healthcare technology, which was capitalized with $450 million of limited partner commitments.\r\nBoth New Leaf Ventures I and New Leaf Ventures II are capitalized primarily by commitments from large corporate and public sector pension funds, endowments, and other private investors -- many of whom have invested with the NLV team through investments in previous Sprout funds.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13624,'Atlas Venture',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13625,'Worldview Technology Partners',29,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13626,'Spark Capital',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13627,'LifeLock',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Based in Tempe AZ and backed by Bessemer Investment Partners.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13628,'T-Mobile',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13629,'Deutsche Telekom',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13630,'Entrisphere',11,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13631,'Jamestown College',17,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-