ity and Tulsa, Oklahoma; Wichita, Kansas; Long Beach, California; Huntsville, Alabama; Arlington and Irving, Texas; and Gaithersburg, Maryland.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13787,'Donald Danforth Plant Science Center',36,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','All human life depends on plants. Given the steady growth of world population and the current use of unsustainable agricultural practices, we face the likelihood of increasing malnutrition, starvation, and the inevitable social unrest that will accompany such scourges. If we are to survive in a peaceful world, we must urgently look to a new revolution, a revolution in plant science.\r\n\r\nThis revolution must logically arise from a deeper understanding of how plants grow and develop, how they resist disease and drought, heat and cold, and what adaptations must be made to decrease the need for chemical fertilizers and pesticides. The mandate of the Donald Danforth Plant Science Center is to lead that revolution.','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13788,'Monsanto Fund',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Philanthropy',306,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13789,'Penneypac - J.C.Penney Corp., Inc. Political Action Committee',61,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13790,'Congressional Victory Fund',26,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13791,'Gopac Incorporated',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13792,'Association of Massachusetts Republican Town and City Chairman',62,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13793,'Gerson Lehrman Group Inc. PAC, Inc. (Gerson Lehrman Group PAC, Inc.)',68,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13794,'South Asian American Forum (Saaf)',33,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13795,'Connecticut Democratic State Central Committee',46,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13796,'American Aids Political Action Committee',40,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13797,'Allegiance Telecom Inc. PAC',27,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13798,'Hatch Victory Committee Non Fed Acc',35,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13799,'New York Mercantile Exchange Political Action Committee',55,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13800,'WY Democratic State Central Committee',37,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13801,'American Friends of Bilderberg',30,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1954, the Bilderberg Group holds \"by invitation only\" annual meetings of the rich and powerful. About two-thirds of the attendees are European, the rest American. Informally named for the site of the group\'s first meeting, the Hotel de Bilderberg in Oosterbeek, Netherlan','Org,MembershipOrg',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13802,'Forestar Group',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Our mission is to create significant value for our shareholders, customers, partners and employees by growing our business and generating the greatest benefit from each and every acre of our land.\r\n\r\nToday, we own directly or through ventures about 281,000 acres of real estate located in 9 states and 12 markets, 622,000 net acres of oil and gas mineral interests, about 231,000 forested acres and over 224,000 acres currently leased for recreational purposes.\r\n\r\nOur real estate, mineral and fiber resources, in combination with our strategy, financial strength, management expertise, stewardship and continuous reinvestment in our business, uniquely position Forestar to maximize long-term value now, and well into the future.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13803,'National Museum of African-American History Council',51,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','In many ways, there are few things as powerful and as important as a people, as a nation that is steeped in its history. Often America is celebrated as a place that forgets. This museum seeks to help all Americans remember, and by remembering, this institution will stimulate a dialogue about race and help to foster a spirit of reconciliation and healing.\r\n\r\nThere are four pillars upon which this museum will stand. The first is to create an opportunity for those that care about or who are interested in African American culture to explore and revel in this history. We will utilize wonderfully interactive exhibitions that are ripe with the best new technologies â but we will never lose the voices and the memories of the people who lived the history. In these exhibitions and presentations the visitors can explore the world, the pain and the resiliency of the enslaved; tap their toes to the music of Duke Ellington, Aretha Franklin, and LL Cool J; appreciate the individual heroism and the collective creativity that was the Civil Rights Movement; celebrate African American cultural expressions like art, dance, theatre; understand what was lost and what was gained as millions of African Americans left the south in the Great Migrations of the World Wars; examine scientific and technological inventiveness; and reflect upon the impact of African Americans on athletics, religion, and urban life. And these are just a few of the riches of African American culture that this museum will make accessible to the millions who visit the Smithsonian Institution.','Org,Cultural',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13804,'Democratic Unity',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13805,'E.I. DU Pont De Nemours Company Good Government Fund (Dupont Good Government Fund)',82,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13806,'Monterey County Republican Central Committee (Fed.)',51,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13807,'Del Webb Corporation Employees Fund for Better Government - C00170480',69,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13808,'Gallagher & Kennedy Good Government Committee',45,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(13809,'Solar Energy Industries Association PAC',39,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL)