 and litigation costs, redetermine worker classification, determine relief from joint and several liability on a joint return, review certain collection actions, and review awards to whistleblowers who provide information to the Commissioner of Internal Revenue on or after December 20, 2006.','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14094,'United States Court of Appeals: Fifth Circuit',45,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14095,'Vancouver Board of Trade',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,MembershipOrg',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14096,'Corporate Environmental Advisory Council',40,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14097,'Dorinco Reinsurance Company',27,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14098,'Liana Limited',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14099,'Teradata Corporation',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Teradata is the worldâs largest company solely focused on raising intelligence through data warehousing and business analytics. \r\n\r\n\"If we wanted to be serious, if we wanted to approach our data in a significant way and leverage that data in a significant way, then we wanted an enterprise data warehouse â a single source of truth, a single repository of all of that data. And, if weâre going to do that, then the best in class was, still is, will probably be for a long time, Teradata.\"\r\n\r\nJohn Stewart, Senior Manager of Customer Analytics, Vodafone New Zealand, Podcast, 2007','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14100,'American Chemical Society',25,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,MembershipOrg',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14101,'Alexis de Tocqueville Society of the United Way of Midland County',65,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Philanthropy',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14102,'MidMichigan Innovation Center',29,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-22 01:34:05',NULL,0,'deleted',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14103,'Mid Michigan Innovation Center',30,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:29:\"MidMichigan Innovation Center\";}','Org','','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-22 01:34:05',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14104,'Miami Dade College',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14105,'University of Texas at Brownsville',34,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14106,'National Conservative Challengers PAC',37,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14107,'Oakland County Democratic Party',31,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14108,'9th Congressional District Democratic Party',43,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14109,'InVenture Fund',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:9:\"InVenture\";}','Org','While traditional philanthropy, micro-enterprise and market-driven approaches can be effective, they alone are not the answer in creating community change. The key to sustainable community change is a mutually beneficial re-investment by our entrepreneurs which yields both financial and social returns for themselves and for their communities.  \r\n\r\nInventure Fund makes the critical link between business and community development. Inventure Fund instills in its entrepreneurs the value of generating sustained social and economic change through our \"social investment binary tree\" concept. Through a formal requirement and a specialized training and education program, Inventure Fund entrepreneurs make strategic re-investments into their own communities, which foster both business market development opportunities and open doors to greater community development possibilities. Inventure Fund believes that combining mutually beneficial reinvestment with behavioral change can create âcommunity citizensâ, who will go on to provide the sustainability and continuity required to improve the broader community, both socially and economically.','Org,Business,Philanthropy',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14110,'National Association of Chain Drug Stores',41,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:30:\"Natl Assn of Chain Drug Stores\";}','Org','','Org,MembershipOrg,NonProfit,IndustryTrade',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14111,'National Newspaper Publishers Association (NNPA)',48,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','National Newspaper Publishers Association (NNPA): The National Newspaper Publishers Association, also known as the Black Press of America, is a 69-year-old federation of more than 200 Black community newspapers from across the United States.\r\n\r\nSince World War II, it has also served as the industry\'s news service, a position that it has held without peer or competitor since the Associated Negro Press dissolved by 1970. In 2000, the NNPA launched NNPA Media Services-- a print and web advertising-placement and press release distribution service. In 2001, the NNPA, in association with the NNPA Foundation, it began building the BlackPressUSA Network-- the nation\'s premier network of local Black community news and information portals. The BlackPressUSA Network is anchored by BlackPressUSA.com-- the national web portal for the Black Press of America.','Org,MembershipOrg',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14112,'SIFE (Students in Free Enterprise)',34,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','SIFE brings together a diverse network of university students, academic professionals and industry leaders around the shared mission of creating a better, more sustainable world through the positive power of business. By contributing their talents to projects that improve the lives of people worldwide, SIFE participants are demonstrating that individuals with a knowledge and passion for business can be a powerful force for change.','Org,MembershipOrg',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14113,'InterAg Technologies Inc.',25,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14114,'Southeast Missouri State University',35,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14115,'New Jersey General Assembly',27,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14116,'Meyer Agri-Products',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14117,'Association of Equipment Manufacturers',38,NULL,'a:2:{i:0;s:0:\"\";i:1;s:37:\"Association of Equipment Manufactures\";}','Org','','Org,IndustryTrade',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-07 05:10:29',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14118,'The Farm Foundation',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,ThinkTank',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL