 River, Massachusetts. On August 16, 2007, Quaker Fabric Corp., alongwith its affiliates, filed a voluntary petition for reorganization under Chapter 11 in the U.S. Bankruptcy Court for the District of Delaware in Wilmington. The plan was later approved as Chapter 11 liquidation on August 27, 2008.','Org,PublicCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-05 23:25:05',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14285,'Willamette University',21,NULL,'a:2:{i:0;s:0:\"\";i:1;s:20:\"Willmette University\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-07 08:14:27',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14286,'Grupo Pliana, S.A.',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14287,'Eastern Utilities Associates',28,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Eastern Utilities Associates is an investor-owned holding company. The company\'s subsidiaries principally generate, transmit, distribute and market electricity, related services such as energy management, and promoting the conservation and efficient use of energy. The company serves a population of approximately 740,000 in an area of about 597 sq.miles in Brockton, Fall River, Massachusetts and in Rhode Island. - business.com\r\n\r\nEastern Utilities Associates was acquired by National Grid USA on 04/19/2000. Eastern Utilities Associates was engaged in the generation, transmission, distribution, and sale of electricity; energy related services, such as energy management; and promoting the conservation and use of energy, as of December 31, 1999. - business week.com','Org,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14288,'Vulcan Coal Holdings, LLC',25,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14289,'Triton Coal Company LLC',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16