ion.','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14373,'New York Bankers Association Community Political Action Committee',65,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14374,'Space Systems/Loral Inc PAC',27,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14375,'Financial Executives International',34,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,MembershipOrg',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14376,'National Investor Relations Institute',37,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business,MembershipOrg',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14377,'Alaska State Chamber of Commerce',32,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,MembershipOrg',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14378,'Resource Development Council for Alaska, Inc.',45,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','RDC is the Resource Development Council for Alaska, Inc., a statewide, non-profit, membership-funded organization made up of businesses and individuals from all resource sectors (oil and gas, mining, fishing, timber, and tourism), as well as Native corporations, support sectors, labor unions, and local governments. Through RDC these interests work together to promote and support responsible development of Alaska\'s resources.\r\n\r\nRDC was formed in 1975, originally as the Organization for Management of Alaska\'s Resources (OMAR). After three years working to obtain a trans-Alaska gas pipeline, RDC changed its name to reflect its broader agenda of education and advocacy on all resource issues in Alaska.','Org,MembershipOrg',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14379,'Alaska Support Industry Alliance',32,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','A nonprofit trade association, the Alliance is made up of more than 400 businesses, organizations and individuals that provide products and services to the oil, gas and mining industries, and represent approximately 40,000 Alaskan workers.','Org,ProfessionalAssociation',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14380,'Committee on Capital Markets Regulation',39,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','501(c)(3) research organization dedicated to improving the regulation of U.S. capital markets.  Twenty-eight leaders from the investor community, business, finance, law, accounting and academia comprise the Committeeâs membership.  The Committee co-Chairs are Glenn Hubbard, Dean of Columbia Business School, and John L. Thornton, Chairman of the Brookings Institution.  The Committeeâs Director is Professor Hal S. Scott, Nomura Professor and Director of the Program on International Financial Systems at Harvard Law School. The Committeeâs research regarding the regulation of U.S. capital markets provides policymakers with a nonpartisan, empirical foundation for public policy.','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14381,'Madison County Record',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','OUR GOAL at The Madison County Record is to cover Madison County\'s legal system in a way that enables you, our readers, to make the public business your business.\r\n\r\nIt\'s an understatement to say that Madison County\'s courts have become a lightning rod for the national press. We shouldn\'t be surprised by the attention, as companies from all across the United States have been forced to defend their actions here, in our small town, unassuming Edwardsville courthouse.\r\n\r\nWhether one agrees or disagrees with the happenings at 157 North Main Street, no one should believe that what happens here is the norm.\r\n\r\nMadison County\'s Courts are anything but average. A welcome mat to class action filings and lottery-like awards have helped create a \"judicial hellhole\" reputation.\r\n\r\nNot to suggest that normal always means good. In many cases throughout American history the norm has meant the wrong course. The country\'s greatest leaders have often been maligned for deviance long before receiving credit for courage and vision.','Org,MediaOrg',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14382,'West Virginia Record',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','OUR GOAL at the West Virginia Record is to cover West Virginia\'s legal system in a way that enables you, our readers, to make the public business your business.\r\n\r\nAs the state\'s first and only legal journal, The Record will focus upon civil actions in our courts. Torts- as they\'re known-- are too often ignored by the prevailing media, yet their progress has a profound impact on the people of our state.\r\n\r\nWe aim to protect the public\'s interest by reporting on West Virginia\'s civil justice system thoroughly and vigorously.\r\n\r\nTo be sure, whether one agrees or disagrees with the happenings at all of our courthouses, no one should believe that what happens at them is the norm. West Virginia\'s courts regularly rank among the most litigious in the land.\r\n\r\nThis doesn\'t mean to suggest that normal always means good. In many cases throughout American history the norm has meant the wrong course. The country\'s greatest leaders have often been maligned for deviance long before receiving credit for courage and vision.','Org,MediaOrg',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14383,'Southeast Texas Record',22,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','OUR GOAL at the The Southeast Texas Record is to cover Southeast Texas\' legal system in a way that enables you, our readers, to make the public business your business.\r\n\r\nAs the region\'s first and only legal journal, The Record will focus upon civil actions in our courts. Torts- as they\'re known-- are too often ignored by the prevailing media, yet their progress has a profound impact on the people of greater Beaumont and Port Arthur.\r\n\r\nWe aim to protect the public\'s interest by reporting on Southeast Texas\' civil justice system thoroughly and vigorously.\r\n\r\nTo be sure, whether one agrees or disagrees with the happenings at all of our courthouses, no one should believe that what happens at them is the norm. Jefferson County\'s courts regularly rank among the most litigious in the land.\r\n\r\nThis doesn\'t mean to suggest that normal always means good. In many cases throughout American history the norm has meant the wrong course. The country\'s greatest leaders have often been maligned for deviance long before receiving credit for courage and vision.','Org,MediaOrg',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14384,'Arcon Partners',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14385,'Vietnam Vets for the Truth LLC',30,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14386,'NY-20 Victory Fund',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14387,'New York State Naral Inc Women\'s Health Political Action Committee',66,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14388,'priceline.com',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14389,'Privatebancorp Inc.',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14390,'Pembroke Capital',