s receive mentoring, networking and public relations opportunities, access to equipment, and referral to professionals in order to help prepare them to move out into their own facility and become self-sustaining members of the business community.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14424,'University of Illinois at Champaign-Urbana',42,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14425,'MB Management Company',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','MB Management  has over thirty five years of experience specializing in multi-family residential housing.  Since 1971, we have taken pride in our long and outstanding history, as evidenced by a strong track record in real estate performance.  Our extensive capabilities serve a diverse array of properties and provide a multitude of services across the country. Presently, we manage a portfolio of over 70 residential properties consisting of over 4,200 residential apartments located in six states.  \r\n\r\nMB Management Company (MBMC) performs a full range of real estate consulting services including property development and acquisition, placement of equity and debt, management of  residential, condominium, and commercial real estate properties, as well as construction management.  \r\n\r\nWe have an especially strong track record in property performance, particularly where value added management is required.  We are dedicated to a very personal, hands-on approach to all the details of management. As such, we have established an enviable reputation for our professional and diligent approach to property management, which has been frequently noted by state and federal regulatory agencies in providing our properties with âExceptional Management Practicesâ ratings to the Company.  At MB Management Company, every member of our staff is thoroughly committed to bring their talents, creativity and professionalism to each clientâs project.  Our success is based firmly on the success of each property we undertake to manage.  \r\n\r\nMB Managementâs senior management staff, located at the Companyâs main office in Braintree, Massachusetts, oversee all the details of our real estate business.   Our property management staff are located in regional offices in Massachusetts, New York, New Hampshire, Maine, Rhode Island and Georgia.\r\n\r\nThe diversity and expertise of our personnel matches the diversity of our portfolio; as residential real estate managers, we manage new construction, older properties, luxury complexes, distressed properties, workouts and turnarounds, low income tax credit properties and government assisted housing. We are experienced in the management of properties that are permanently financed through HUD, MassHousing, New York Division of Housing and Community Renewal, Rural Housing Service (formerly Farmers Home Administration), and other public entities.   We have a first hand working knowledge of financing agency and reporting requirements as well as those that are associated with the provision of subsidy.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14426,'National Apartment Association Political Action Committee',57,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14427,'New York State Housing Trust Fund Corporation',45,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Housing Trust Fund Corporation (\"HTFC\" or \"the Corporation\") was established by Chapter 67 of the Laws of 1985, specifically under Section 45-a of the Private Housing Finance Law (PHFL), as a subsidiary public benefit corporation of the New York State Housing Finance Agency (HFA). The Law conferred a number of privileges, tax exemptions and powers to HTFC including the authority to contract with the Division of Housing and Community Renewal (DHCR) to administer the Corporation\'s activities. HTFC was also authorized, among other things, to create its own by-laws for the management of its affairs, make and execute its own contracts, engage the services of consultants for professional and technical assistance services, and determine policies for the investment of its funds.\r\n\r\nThe Law also established the membership of the Corporation\'s three-person governing body. The Commissioner of Housing and Community Renewal was designated as the Corporation\'s Chairperson; the Chairman of HFA was named as a Member, while the third Member was to be appointed by HTFC\'s Chairperson.\r\n\r\nThe mission of the Corporation, as originally established under Section 45-a and Article18 of the PHFL, was to create decent affordable housing for persons of low-income by providing loans and grants for the rehabilitation of existing housing or the construction of new housing under the Low-Income Housing Trust Fund Program. This mission has reinforced since then by the adding many State and Federal programs to HTFC\'s portfolio, including these which are currently active:\r\nState-funded Programs:\r\n\r\n    * Low-Income Housing Trust Fund Program\r\n    * Homes for Working Families Program\r\n    * HOPE/RESTORE Program\r\n    * Public Housing Modernization Program\r\n    * Public Housing Drug Elimination Program\r\n    * New York Main Street Program\r\n    * Access to Home Program\r\n    * Urban Initiatives Program\r\n    * Rural Area Revitalization Program\r\n\r\nFederally-funded Programs:\r\n\r\n    * HOME Investment Partnerships Program\r\n    * Section 8 Project-based Contract Administration Program\r\n    * Small Cities Community Development Block Grant Program','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14428,'Robinson, Lerer & Montgomery',28,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14429,'U.S.-Vietnam Trade Council',26,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,IndustryTrade',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14430,'Leading Edge Policy and Strategy',32,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Leading Edge provides consulting, strategy, policy, business development and Federal government relations.   These are exciting times in these policy arenas.  Leading Edge can:\r\n\r\n    * Provide research, counsel, and analysis\r\n    * Provide government relations for legislative and regulatory activities\r\n    * Promote additional opportunities for collaborations with other stakeholders through contacts and meetings\r\n    * Assess and promote business development in areas related to new Federal policies\r\n\r\nLeading Edge has provided services in the area of health information, health care reform, comparative effectiveness, and medical product safety.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14431,'Sierra Health Foundation',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14432,'Strat PAC',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14433,'Sutro & Co',10,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14434,'Capital Pacific Holdings',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14435,'Makar Properties',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14436,'New Majority California',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14437,'GenNext',7,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}',