010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14594,'Kings College',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Kingâs College was founded in 1938 in Belmar, New Jersey by Dr. Percy B. Crawford. In 1949, Crawford initiated Youth on the March, the first nationwide television show of any kind. (A 1.5 minute segment of archival footage from the program is available here.) CNN later honored Crawford on the 50th anniversary of the first Youth on the March broadcast. \r\n\r\nIn 1955, Crawford moved King\'s to Briarcliff Manor, New York. When Dr. Crawford died of a heart attack in 1960, Dr. Robert Cook became the collegeâs second president.\r\n\r\nIn 1985, Dr. Friedhelm Radandt, a former professor at the University of Chicago and President of Northwestern College in Iowa, became the collegeâs third president. King\'s ran into financial difficulties in the early 1990s and closed in 1994. In 1998, J. Stanley Oakes, in coordination with Dr. Bill Bright, led the effort to re-capitalize the school. Radandt continued as president. \r\n\r\nIn 1999, The Kingâs College acquired Northeastern Bible College, of Essex Fells, New Jersey. That year the revived King\'s leased 34,000 square feet on two floors of Empire State Building, where it remains today. \r\n\r\nOn January 1, 2003, the Board of Trustees of The Kingâs College selected J. Stanley Oakes, Jr. to be the collegeâs fourth president. President Oakes, a graduate in Classical Greek from the University of Minnesota and in political theory from the University of Dallas, had spent nearly 20 years building a nationwide network of Christian professors.','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14595,'Independent Sector',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','ndependent Sector serves as the premier meeting ground for the leaders of America\'s charitable and philanthropic sector. Since our founding in 1980, we have sponsored ground-breaking research, fought for public policies that support a dynamic, independent sector, and created unparalleled resources so staff, boards, and volunteers can improve their organizations and better serve their communities.\r\n\r\nIndependent Sector fulfills our mission by:\r\n\r\nConvening opportunities for sector leaders to work together on key issues. The most prominent forum of this kind is the Independent Sector Annual Conference, but IS committees are another key part of developing collective strategies.\r\nPromoting policies that enable the charitable community to engage with public officials on a nonpartisan basis. IS is currently focusing on issues such as protecting advocacy rights of nonprofits, promoting tax incentives for charitable giving, and addressing federal and state budget concerns.\r\nSupporting the development and dissemination of strategies to strengthen volunteering, voting, giving, and other forms of citizen engagement.\r\nEncouraging the sector to meet the highest standards of ethical practice and effectiveness. As part of our continuing efforts in this area, IS has convened the Panel on the Nonprofit Sector, which is making recommendations in the areas of governance, fiduciary responsibility, government oversight, self-regulation, and financial accountability.\r\nServing as the voice of the independent sector to the media, government, business, and international voluntary communities.','Org,MembershipOrg',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14596,'Communidades Group',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Our plan is to own, build and operate property in a culturally-relevant and culturally-sensitive manner.\r\n\r\nAt The Comunidades Group, we celebrate cultural diversity. We recognize that ethnic and minority communities have earned the right to be serviced in a manner that is respectful of their cultural traditions and nuances. Our commitment is to provide our residents with not only a comfortable and engaging place to call home, but to provide them with learning and empowering opportunities as well.\r\n\r\nWith The Comunidades Group, Everyone Wins\r\nOur customers win because we provide them with a welcoming, embracing and empowering community in which to live;\r\nOur investors win because our \"cultural customization\" program results in higher returns;\r\nOur team members win because we receive the daily satisfaction that we are running a profitable business AND improving the lives of people; and\r\nOur nation, states and cities win because our customers become better equipped for and thus more contributory to American society.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14597,'United Dominion Realty Trust',28,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Today, we have 240,000 smart residents living in over 70,000 apartment homes in our 200-plus communities spread across the country. Our formula is: Great Locations & Service + Excellent Values for all Lifestyles = Smart, Happy Residents! Add yourself to our solution today, Welcome Home! \r\n\r\nâWhat is Smart Apartment Living?â Well, if you could find an apartment community that is conveniently located yet peaceful enough that you can kick back & relax, worry free, in your apartment, would it feel like home? What if your apartment home came equipped with a new kitchen and bathrooms featuring energy-efficient appliances? We at UDR reflected upon what makes us feel at home and came to the conclusion that, if we could combine all of these factors into one apartment community, then that would truly be Smart Living! âWhat do you mean youâre always there for me?â \r\n\r\nEver get up in the middle of the night to grab a glass of water and realize that your sink is leaking? What about speeding home from work, dodging traffic just to try and pay your rent before the leasing office closes? Are your lunch breaks sometimes so hectic that you just donât have time to go apartment shopping to find the best price & floor plan? Part of our Smart Living concept is that your home never closes so neither should your community! Our website, www.UDR.com, allows you to file an online service request, check real-time pricing and availability, and even pay your rent from the comfort of your couch. Our âweâre always there for youâ mantra means that even though the work day is over, our commitment to providing great service and making apartment living easier never sleeps!','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14598,'National Association of Hispanic Real Estate Professionals',58,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','We are the National Association of Hispanic Real Estate Professionals (NAHREP), a non-profit 501 c6 trade association with 15,000 members in over 60 affiliate chapters in 48 states, including: California, Connecticut, Arizona, Nevada, Texas, New Mexico, Illinois, Indiana, Tennessee, New Jersey, New York, Pennsylvania, Georgia and Florida.\r\nBased in Washington, D.C., our members are real estate agents, brokers, loan officers, mortgage brokers, title officers, escrow officers, appraisers, insurance agents and more. They are from diverse cultural backgrounds as membership is not limited to professionals of Hispanic descent.\r\nNAHREP\'s mission is to increase Hispanic homeownership rates by empowering the advisors that serve them. We accomplish this by providing educational tools and a networking forum, and through the power of advocacy.\r\nA board of directors, advisory and executive committees govern NAHREP and include highly successful practitioners, entrepreneurs, former government appointed officials and industry leaders from Fortune 100 companies.','Org,ProfessionalAssociation',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14599,'St. Mary\'s University, School of Law',36,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Universityâan independent, coeducational Catholic university administered by the Marianists. \r\n\r\nThe Law Schoolâthe only private, coeducational Catholic law school in the state of Texas. It was founded in 1927 by the San Antonio Bar Association and became known as St. Maryâs University School of Law in 1934. \r\n\r\nThe LocationâSan Antonio, Texas, the eighth largest U.S. city, is known for its excellent quality of life and its fascinating blend of history, culture, and progress. San Antonio offers a robust economy; a strong, legal job market; and ties to Mexico and international business. \r\n\r\nThe Facultyâ43 full-time faculty known for teaching, scholarship, public service, and an open-door policy; also 30 adjunct professors and distinguished visiting professors. \r\n\r\nStudent/Faculty Ratioâ22:1','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14600,'Sacramento County Democratic Central Committee: United Campaign Committee - Federal',83,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14601,'Western League of Savings Institutions; Fka California League Savings Inst Fedpac',81,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14602,'Sternhell Group',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,LobbyingFirm,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14603,'Sobba Public',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,LobbyingFirm',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14604,'International Derivatives Clearing Group',40,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14605,'White House Council on Environmental Quality (CEQ)',50,NULL,'','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',28677,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-07 06:21:59',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14606,'Bonner & Associates',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','This firm is the one that got caught sending forged letters to Representative Tom Perriello and a few other Congress members in the summer of 2009.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14607,'Committee for a Constructive Tomorrow',37,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:5:\"CFACT\";}','Org','In 1985, the Committee For A Constructive Tomorrow (CFACT) was founded to promote a positive voice on environment and development issues. Its co-founders, David Rothbard and Craig Rucker, believed very strongly that the power of the market combined with the applications of safe technologies could offer humanity practical solutions to many of the worldâs pressing concerns. A number of leading scientists, academics, and policy leaders would also agree with them and soon joined their effort, along with thousands of citizens from around the country. Today, this Washington DC-based group is a highly respected organization and its voice can be heard relentlessly infusing the environmental debate with a balanced perspective on environmental stewardship.  With an influential and impressive scientific advisory board, aggressive collegiate program, CFACT Europe, United Nations representation,  Adopt-A-Village project, Global Social Responsibility program, and âJust the Factsâ national radio commentary, CFACT has and continues to offer genuine positive solutions to todayâs global challenges. The organization has been termed \"invaluable\" by the Arizona Republic, it has been lauded for its \"effort to bring sound science to the environmental debate\" by a former president of the National Academy of Sciences, and has been praised by a respected Boston Globe columnist for \"a record of supplying absolutely solid information.\"','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14608,'Grinell Col