ess',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14862,'Harvard Alumni Association',26,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Offers a variety of services for alumni and seeks financial support for the university.','Org,School,MembershipOrg',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14863,'Cablevision Systems NY PAC',26,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14864,'Puerto Rico 21st Millennium PAC (NY)',36,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14865,'United Mine Workers of America - Coal Miners Political Action Committee',71,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14866,'Climate Solutions',17,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14867,'Lakeside High School',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14868,'United Victory 2004',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14869,'Safer Together 04',17,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14870,'HBJ Investments',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14871,'Biocraft Laboratories',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14872,'Government Development Bank for Puerto Rico',43,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','As Puerto Rico has evolved, so has GDB, adapting itself time after time to meet the islandâs most pressing economic and social problems. Through its history, the Bank has proven to be a dynamic institution, with the flexibility and creativity required to generate alternative solutions to the islandâs ever-changing needs.\r\n\r\nDuring the early years, the Bank intervened directly in Puerto Ricoâs development investing in projects that were needed to get the economy moving but which private investors found too risky. In its later years, GDB has emerged as a promoter and facilitator, helping to create a favorable environment for private sector investments that will generate economic growth.\r\n\r\nThe Bank has been the catalytic agent in Puerto Ricoâs transformation from an agrarian framework into an economy that is competitive in multiple and diverse areas. From promoting, during a specific time in history, an âentrepreneur government,â it came to understand that the governmentâs role should be more that of a facilitator of processes for private enterprise.\r\n\r\nAct 252 of May 13, 1942 of the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico created GDB âfor the purpose of carrying out the complete development of Puerto Ricoâs human and economic resources.â But the Bank would not acquire its final form until the enactment of Act 272 of May 15, 1945, which authorized it to act as fiscal agent and financial advisor of the central government and its agencies; and Act 17 of September 23, 1948, which includes the Charter of the Bank and established all of its duties and powers.\r\n\r\nInitially, GDB was little more than a section of the Puerto Rico Department of Treasury with a mere handful of employees. Today, the Bank is one of the islandâs most important and prestigious institutions, with total assets of $8.9 billion and 514 employees.\r\n\r\nAs now constituted, the Bankâs primary functions are to act as a fiscal agent and financial advisor for the Commonwealth and its agencies and to provide financing mechanisms to both public entities and private enterprises in order to boost the islandâs economic development. Throughout its history the Bank has undertaken ventures that go well beyond the boundaries we normally identify with banking institutions. When circumstances require it, the Bank has pioneered in breaking new ground to advance Puerto Ricoâs economic and social development.\r\n\r\nUndoubtedly, GDB has been one of the engines of our economic development. It financed the first efforts of our government to promote industrialization, the first restorations, the first condominiums, the first office buildings, the first hotels, and the first bond issues of our public corporations and municipalities. It has contributed to the creation of job opportunities for our families. And as a fiscal agent, it has been instrumental in the task of providing our country with the infrastructure required to facilitate our economic development.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14873,'Puerto Rico Federal Affairs Administration',42,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','As such, t he Washington office is the primary liaison between Puerto Rico\'s officials, the White House, Congress, and the federal agencies. Additionally, the office interacts with national organizations representing Governors from other states, including the National Governors Association (NGA) and the Southern Governors\' Association to advance Puerto Rico\'s interests.\r\n\r\nLike many other states, Puerto Rico\'s focus areas include economic stimulus and development, transportation funding, energy, health care including Medicare and Medicaid, as well as issues that affect veterans and our national defense.','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14874,'Chlopak, Leonard, et al',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','We work with clients ranging from Fortune 500 companies to nonprofit organizations and foreign governments.  Corporations enlist our help to promote and enhance their reputations.  Organizations trying to influence policymakers take advantage of our expertise in designing successful, results-oriented public affairs campaigns.  Our international practice provides clients with advice and services to move products, issues and initiatives in the global arena.\r\n\r\nStaffed by veterans of political campaigns, former journalists and corporate communications experts, the firm thrives in highly adversarial and competitive situations.  Thoughtful strategy, often validated by market research, is at the core of everything we do.  We also adapt nimbly to rapid shifts in the environment.   But the most important key to our work is that we treat our clients as our partners, bringing zeal to win, delivering the best service possible and operating with the respect and candor that clients expect.\r\n\r\nPerhaps that is why so many of our clients, in industries marked by churn, have stood the test of time and become long-term relationships.','Org,Business,LobbyingFirm,PublicRelationsFirm',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14875,'College Democrats of America Inc Non Federal',44,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14876,'Davidson County Democratic Executive Committee',46,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14877,'RFR Holdings',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14878,'York Capital Management',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(14879,'Think New Mexico',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";