L),(15504,'American Federation of Teachers, Afl-Cio Committee on Political Education',73,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15505,'Public Accountability Initiatve',31,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:32:\"Public Accountability Initiative\";}','Org','','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15506,'Business for Conservative Government',36,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15507,'Aviation Partners, Inc',22,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','In creating Aviation Partners, Clark gathered together a highly and uniquely experienced team of aerospace professionals consisting primarily of retired Boeing and Lockheed engineers and flight test department directors.\r\n\r\nBlended Wingletâ¢ Technology made its initial market debut as a Performance Enhancement Program for the Gulfstream II. This program was highly successful, resulting in an unprecedented range boost and fuel efficiency improvement in excess of 7% for the IISP. In the mid-90s, The Boeing Company adopted Blended Winglet Technology for the Boeing Business Jet and Next Generation Boeing 737 series aircraft. Today, Aviation Partners Boeing, a joint venture between Aviation Partners Inc. and The Boeing Company, has supplied Blended Winglet shipsets to over 3,500 Boeing aircraft worldwide. A typical Blended Winglet-equipped 737 saves 100,000 gallons of fuel per year. In addition, Aviation Partners Boeing has developed Blended Winglet programs for the Boeing 757, which can save 300,000 gallons per year, and created a launch program for 767 series aircraft.\r\n\r\nAviation Partners also offers patented* Blended Winglet Technology for Raytheon Hawker 800/800XP series business aircraft. A Hawker 800 Performance-Enhanced with Blended Winglets becomes an 800SP while a Hawker 800XP upgraded with Blended Winglet Technology becomes an 800XP2. This revolutionary visible technology has been so well received by the global Hawker 800 series operator community that Aviation Partners is now looking at developing Blended Winglet Programs for additional makes and models of popular series business aircraft.\r\n\r\nPerformance Enhancement Blended Winglet Technology has succeeded in the marketplace because it produces measurable benefits on a scale unheard of in the history of aircraft capability improvement. The world aviation community has recognized that Blended Winglet Technology not only saves fuel and protects the environment but it modernizes aircraft and makes them perform better. The future, as we like to say, is \"on the wing\".','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15508,'Seaspan Corporation',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','We currently own a large modern fully contracted fleet of 68 vessels of which we have entered into long-term contracts. We deploy all our vessels on long-term, fixed rate charters to take advantage of the stable cash flow and high utilization rates that are associated with long-term time charters. Our primary objective is to continue to grow our business through accretive acquisitions over the mid to long-term and as market conditions allow.\r\nOur customer selection process is targeted at well-established container liner companies that charter-in vessels on a long-term basis as part of their fleet expansion strategy. Currently, 22 containerships in our fleet are under time charters with CSCL Asia. CSCL Asia, a British Virgin Islands company, is a subsidiary of CSCL. Nine containerships in our current fleet are under time charters with HL USA, an affiliate of TUI AG, or TUI. Our four 4800 TEU vessels are chartered to APM, the worldâs largest containers shipping company. Our two 3500 TEU vessels are under time charters with COSCON. Additionally, we have three vessels chartered to MOL and two vessels to CSAV.\r\nMost of our charterersâ container shipping business revenues are derived from the shipment of goods from the Asia Pacific region, primarily China, to various overseas export markets in the Unites States and in Europe.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15509,'Washington Marine Group',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Within the Group are three shipyards, an intermodal ferry business, and a tug and barge transportation company that serves both domestic and international markets. The scope of Washington Marine Group\'s services, the quality of its employees and equipment, and over a century of successful participation in coastal commerce, makes this group a major partner in the economy of the Pacific Northwest.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15510,'Montana State Senate',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15511,'CDS IndexCo',11,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15512,'Markit Group',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15513,'Scene7, Inc.',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15514,'Emerging Markets Private Equity Association',43,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15515,'National Coal Corporation',25,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15516,'Patrick Henry Party',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,MembershipOrg',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15517,'Nextel Communications',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15518,'URS Corporation',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Company offers a full range of program management; planning, design and engineering; systems engineering and technical assistance; construction and construction management; operations and maintenance; and decommissioning and closure services for power, infrastructure, industrial and commercial, and federal projects and programs.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15519,'Montana Republican Party',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalParty',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15520,'Thomas Jefferson University',27,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15521,'University of Central Oklahoma',30,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15522,'Oklahoma City University',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15523,'Continental Resources, Inc.',27,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Continental Resources, Inc. is an independent oil and natural gas exploration and production company with operations in the Rocky Mountain, Mid-Continent and Gulf Coast regions of the United States. The Company focuses its exploration activities in large new or developing plays that provide it the opportunity to acquire undeveloped acreage positions for future drilling operations. As of December 31, 2006, its estimated proved reserves were 118.3 million barrels of oil equivalent (MMBoe), with estimated proved developed reserves of 87.1 MMBoe, or 74% of its total estimated proved reserves. Crude oil comprised 83% of the Company\'s total estimated proved reserves. At December 31, 2006, it had 1,772 scheduled drilling locations on the 1,775,000 gross (1,071,000 net) acres that it held. As of December 31, 2006, the Company had interests in approximately 1,589 wells and serves as the operator of 1,302 of these wells.\r\n(from nyse - http://www.nyse.com/events/1186743758075.html\r\nMay 15, 2007)','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-22 01:38:24',NULL,0,'deleted',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15524,'Campaign Contributions',22,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Center for Responsive Politics produces the web site OpenSecrets.org. From its mission statement: The Center tracks money in U.S. politics and its effect on elections and public policy. Nonpartisan, independent and nonprofit, the organization aims to create a more educated voter, an involved citizenry and a more responsive government.','Org',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15525,'Merlin Entertainment',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15526,'Dubai International Capital',27,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15527,'China Investment Corporation',28,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Gse',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15528,'Keyspan Corporation Political Action Committee',46,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15529,'Brooklyn Union Gas Company Federal PAC',38,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15530,'Washington Leadership PAC',25,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15531,'Friends of Our Troops',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15532,'Busch Entertainment Corporation',31,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:31:\"Busch Entertainment Corporation\";}','Org','\"BEC operates 10 entertainment parks throughout the United States including three SeaWorld parks in Orlando, Florida, San Antonio, Texas, and San Diego, California, two Busch Gardens parks in Tampa, Florida and Williamsburg, Virginia, and other family entertainment attractions in Orlando, Florida, Tampa, Florida, Williamsburg, Virginia, and Langhorne, Pennsylvania.\" - blackstone.com','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15533,'Summit Materials',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15534,'Silverhawk Capital Partner',26,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15535,'Relational Investors LLC',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Relational Investors LLC is a San Diego-based, Registered Investment AdviserÂ¹ that serves some of the largest pension funds in the world.\r\n\r\nRelational invests in and strives to create long-term growth in publicly traded, underperforming companies that it believes are undervalued in the marketplace.  Through intense and focused research, Relational develops an engagement plan to unlock value in its portfolio companies. The Firm seeks to engage the management, board of directors, and shareholders of a portfolio company in a productive dialogue designed to build a consensus for positive change to improve shareholder value.\r\nRelational is a privately owned asset management firm founded in 1996.\r\n\r\nRelationalâs two products each have concentrated portfolios of generally 8-12 U.S. and Canadian-listed companies:\r\nRelational Investors fund: Large-Cap Equity\r\nMid-Cap fund: Mid-Cap Equity\r\n\r\nRelational manages approximately $6 billion in total.\r\n\r\nThe Relational Investors fundÂ², from inception in 1996 through December 31, 2009, has materially outperformed its benchmark, the S&P 500 Total Return Index, on a cumulative basis.\r\n\r\nRelationalâs nine-person executive management team averages over 20 years of investment experience.  Relationalâs two founders have worked together since 1985.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15536,'Encore Acquisition Company',26,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','\"Encore Acquisition Company is engaged in the development of onshore North American oil and natural gas reserves. Since 1998, Encore has acquired high-quality assets and grown through drilling, waterflood, and tertiary projects. Encore\'s properties are located in the Rockies, the Mid-Continent, and the Permian Basin.\" It has acquired over $850 million of these properties since 1998. - encoreacq.com','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15537,'Texas Petrochemicals, Inc.',26,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','From the Texas Petrochemicals, Inc. website: \r\n\"Headquartered in Houston, Texas, TPC Group is a leader in providing highly specialized lines of chemical products to major chemical and petroleum-based companies worldwide.\r\n\r\nAs North Americaâs largest producer of finished butadiene and the largest producer of butene-1, companies around the globe rely on us as their dependable supplier for hydrocarbon processing and other specialty chemicals. We are the sole producer of chemical grade diisobutylene in North America and the second largest active merchant producer of high purity isobutylene in North America. Our products are sold to a wide range of performance, specialty and intermediate markets, including synthetic rubber, fuel additives, plastics and surfactants. Put simply, we make the products that go into making the worldâs tires, carpets, gasoline additives and many other essential items used in our daily lives.\r\n\r\nTPC Group operates manufacturing facilities in the industrial corridor adjacent to the Houston Ship Channel, the heart of the worldâs largest chemical processing center. In addition, we operate facilities in Port Neches and Baytown, Texas, as well as a product terminal in Lake Charles, Louisiana.\"','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15538,'British Salt Holdings',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15539,'Trimeris',8,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15540,'HealthCor Management',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business,PrivateCompany',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15541,'Bank United',11,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:11:\"Bank United\";}','Org','May 2009 - \"Investors led by John Kanas announced today that they have invested $900 million in a new depository institution that acquired the operations of BankUnited, FSB from the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation, as Receiver. The investors include funds advised by The Blackstone Group, The Carlyle Group, Centerbridge Partners and WL Ross & Co.\" - http://www.blackstone.com/cps/rde/xchg/bxcom/hs/news_pressrelease_3220.htm','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15542,'Talley Industries, Inc',22,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Since 1960, Nammo Talley has been a pioneer in developing aircrew escape systems, automobile airbag components, submunition dispensing systems, shoulder-launched weapons, and other key propellant-loaded devices. Located on approximately 550 acres in Mesa, Arizona, twenty miles east of Phoenix, Nammo Talley operates a complete industrial complex designed for the development, testing and manufacturing of a wide range of propellant-based products.\r\n\r\nAs an ISO 9001:2000 certified business Talley continues to provide superior service, design innovation, and creative technical solutions to meet our customers\' propellant related needs. In our effort to exceed customer expectations, we are committed to continually improving the quality of our people, products, processes, and relationships.\r\n\r\nIn 2007 Nammo Talley became a member of the Nammo Group.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15543,'CMS Computers Ltd',17,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Formed by \"carving out the IT Infrastructure Management and Outsourced Business Services divisions (comprising Card Solutions, Transaction Printing Solutions and ATM Cash Management) of CMS Computers Ltd.\" \r\n\r\nCEO is Rajiv Kaul, ex-CEO of Microsoft India.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15544,'Actis',5,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Manages $4.8 billion in funds, focused exclusively on emerging markets. Formed as a spin-off from the Commonwealth Development Corporation (UK) in 2004, the British-government fund devoted to investment in emerging markets. This move generated major controversy, as \"a 60 per cent stake was sold to CDC managers and staff for a total of Â£373,000\" - while it was estimated in 2007 by the House of Commons Public Accounts Committee to be worth between Â£182m and Â£535m. (Guardian, 11/25/07)','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15545,'Microsoft India',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',44,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15546,'Kinetic Systems, Inc',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1973, Kinetics is the world\'s largest full-service mechanical contractor providing process and mechanical system installations for customers in the electronics, biopharmaceutical, healthcare, data centers, and general industries. Kinetics has also been serving the international solar energy market for over 10 years. During this time, we designed and installed gas, chemical, water and waste systems for photovoltaic manufacturing lines with an unparalleled combination of experience, quality, capacity and versatility.\r\n\r\nWe combine support equipment manufacturing, design engineering and an unmatched global installation capability for complete process and mechanical system installations at client locations worldwide. In addition, our services include pre-construction services, building information modeling, state-of-the-art fabrication, chemical delivery solutions, field operations and project management. We also have extensive engineering design capabilities to execute mechanical scopes of work for solar power generation projects utilizing various Concentrated Solar Power (CSP) technologies, i.e. parabolic trough technology. \r\n\r\nWith a large number of mechanical contractors, competing in the construction industry, Kinetics is set apart by its higher than industry-average Safety ratings, global reach, and extensive experience in performing large, fast-track, complex projects.\r\n\r\nSpecifically and most importantly as it pertains to safety, our goal is not simply having zero incidents but to encourage our employees to hold safety values as part of everything they do in the workplace and in their everyday lives. Kinetics has implemented a \"Beyond Zero\" program to focus on the awareness of everyday behavior that will keep our employees safe at work and at home.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15547,'Conway DelGenio Gries & Co., LLC',32,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Conway Del Genio Gries & Co., LLC is a financial advisory firm providing restructuring, crisis and turnaround management, and merger and acquisition services. CDG provides senior level attention in a collaborative process which draws upon over 70 years of engagement experience of its principals and the collective ability of its professionals. CDG has developed unique skills and knowledge from successfully completing financial restructurings and mergers and acquisitions in numerous industries and in many different capacities. It has successfully managed businesses and conducted turnarounds and provided clients with advice from professionals with the business judgment and ability to effectively execute sound strategies.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15548,'Inner-City Scholarship Fund',27,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Inner-City Scholarship Fund (ICSF) provides funding to lower income parents to send their children to Catholic School within the Archdiocese of New York. Its biggest donors are Stephen and Christine Schwarzman. \"Founded in 1971, the fund supports 107 Catholic schools in Manhattan, the Bronx and Staten Island. Nearly two-thirds of the students enrolled in qualifying schools live at or below the poverty line. (To qualify, at least 50 percent of a schoolâs student population must be at or below that level.)\" (NYTimes, 2/29/08)','Org,Philanthropy',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15549,'Rockford College',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15550,'Tiger Foundation',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Philanthropy',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15551,'American Legislative Exchange Council',37,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:4:\"ALEC\";}','Org','Advances policies of free markets, limited government, federalism, and individual liberty, through a nonpartisan public-private partnership of America\'s state legislators, members of the private sector, the federal government, and general public.','Org,MembershipOrg,LobbyingFirm,ThinkTank',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15552,'Jaffe, Raitt, Heuer & Weiss',27,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15553,'Free Enterprise Fund Political Action Committee',47,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15554,'Compass Lexecon',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15555,'Milken Family Foundation',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Philanthropy',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15556,'Modern Machinery Company',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Modern Machinery is in business to sell and rent high quality heavy equipment and provide exceptional product support to the construction, mining, and forestry industries. Modern Machinery began in 1944 with a single location in Spokane, Washington. Today, Modern operates full service branches in Missoula, Billings and Kalispell, Montana; Boise and Pocatello, Idaho; Kent, Spokane and Rochester, Washington; Portland and Eugene, Oregon; and Magadan, Russia. \r\n\r\nA diverse product line gives Modern the capability to satisfy the equipment needs of our customers. Modern represents product lines from Komatsu, Dressta, Haulpak, Valmet, Timbco, Wirtgen/Hamm/Vogele, Cedarapids, P&H, Terex O&K, Moxy, Sakai, Kolberg-Pioneer, Atlas Copco, Denharco, Sennebogen, Allied Construction Products and Madill LLC. \r\n\r\nOur products include hydraulic excavators, wheel loaders, crawler tractor dozers, backhoe loaders, skid-steer loaders, pavers, milling machines, graders, crushing plants, screens, drills, compactors, off-highway trucks, mining shovels, articulated trucks, feller-bunchers, harvesters, forwarders, processors, log loaders, conveyors, and a variety of other equipment.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15557,'Montana Rail Link',17,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Montana Rail Link, Inc. is an FRA Class II regional railroad with more than 900 miles of track serving 100 stations in the states of Montana, Idaho and Washington, and employs approximately 1,000 people.\r\n\r\nIn operation is a fleet of nearly 2,000 freight cars and 176 locomotives.\r\n\r\nMontana Rail Link connects with the Burlington Northern & Santa Fe Railway (BNSF) at Laurel and Garrison, Montana and Spokane, Washington and the Union Pacific Railroad at Sandpoint, Idaho.\r\n\r\nMRL is one of the independently operated Washington Companies and is headquartered in Missoula, Montana. It is privately held.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15558,'Montana Resources',17,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Montana Resources at a Glance\r\nMontana Resources operates an open pit copper and molybdenum mine in Butte, Montana. The operation comprises the Continental mine, crushers and a concentrator facility where tons of raw ore are processed into high-quality metal concentrates. We serve an international market for these important metals.\r\nA Proud and Skilled Workforce\r\nMontana Resources employs approximately 350 peopleâa proud and skilled workforce, heir to a tradition of mining in Butte dating back to the 1870âs. Butte grew as an early urban industrial center in the Rocky Mountain West to become legend as The Mining City. Montana Resources, one of The Washington Companies, has operated in Butte since 1985, continuing the mining tradition there. We are proud to be a Montana company and accordingly value our beautiful environment and our friendly communities.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15559,'Envirocon',9,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Envirocon provides full-service environmental remediation, demolition, geotechnical, and water-related services to public and private sector clients. We apply multidisciplinary scientific, engineering, and construction expertise to serve the environmental needs of our national and international clientele. Our focus is on implementing the highest quality and most cost-effective solution to each environmental challenge faced by our clients.\r\n\r\nFrom a creek remediation project in Tennessee to a levee construction project in California, and from a sludge stabilization project in Oklahoma to a sediment removal project in Washington State, no matter the location Envirocon partners with its clients to achieve common goals using the most skillful project teams in the industry. Our projects are performed with pride in the safest, most cost-effective manner with the right amount of resources.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15560,'Carlyle Capital Corporation',27,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15561,'The Washington Corporation',26,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:26:\"The Washington Corporation\";}','Org','The company offers business development, taxation, and real estate assistance services. Additionally, it offers aviation, travel, facilities, and hospitality management services. Washington Corporations was founded in 1979 and is headquartered in Missoula, Montana. Washington Corporations operates as a subsidiary of The Washington Companies.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15562,'Reely Law Firm',14,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,LawFirm',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15563,'University of Montana Foundation',32,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The University of Montana Foundation was established in 1951 on the belief that excellence in higher education could be greatly augmented through the infusion of private gifts. The UM Foundation serves as a charitable non-profit organization under Internal Revenue Service 501(c)(3) designations and is the official development office for The University of Montana. The Foundation has resolved that the support of its donors not replace the obligation of the State of Montana to provide for the basic needs of the University\'s programs, but that it will enhance the quality and scope of UM programs.\r\nA 40-member Board of Trustees maintains fiduciary responsibility for the foundation and embraces its goals to work with the University community to ascertain financial needs of the University, to raise private funds to meet the University\'s needs, and to provide sound stewardship of private assets.','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15564,'H.E. Butt Grocery Company',25,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15565,'Horatio Alger Montana Scholarships',34,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','50 $5,000 Scholarships Awarded\r\n\r\nThe University of Montana Foundation matches this award so that the total grant amount will equal $10,000 to be disbursed over the student\'s college career\r\n**IMPORTANT**\r\nRecipients must pursue a bachelor\'s degree at The University of Montana, The University of Montana-Western, The University of Montana-Missoula College of Technology, \r\nHelena College of Technology of The University of Montana, or Montana Tech of The University of Montana\r\n\r\nEligibility\r\n\r\nTo be eligible to apply for the Horatio Alger Montana Scholarship, applicants must meet the following criteria:\r\n\r\nbe enrolled full time as a high school senior in Montana, progressing normally toward graduation, and planning to enter college no later than the fall following graduation;\r\nmust pursue a bachelor\'s degree at The University of Montana, The University of Montana-Western, The University of Montana-Missoula College of Technology, Helena College of Technology of The University of Montana, or Montana Tech of The University of Montana. The colleges listed above have pledged to match the scholarship amount dollar for dollar for each scholarship recipient.;\r\ncritical financial need ($50,000 or less adjusted gross income per family is preferred; if higher, an explanation must be provided);\r\ninvolvement in co-curricular and community activities;\r\ndemonstrate academic achievement (minimum grade point average of 2.0);\r\nbe a resident of Montana; and\r\nbe a citizen of the United States','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15566,'Headington Institute',20,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15567,'Fuller Theological Seminary',27,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15568,'Travis Research Institute',25,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15569,'The Irving Company',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15570,'YMCA of Greater Long Beach',26,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15571,'San Antonio Winery',18,NULL,'a:1: