e camps, leaders earn the right to be heard and the Gospel is experienced. It is always communicated through unconditional love that reflects the agape love of the Father.\r\n\r\nToday, Young Life is at work in 30 high schools and middle schools within 13 different communities across Montana. We have planted seeds at the Native American Reservations of Flathead, Crow and Lame Deer. This ia a pioneering work that requires a resilient spirit. Thank you for taking the time to get to know us as we forge forward on this great mission in the amazing place known as Big Sky Country!','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15578,'Steinhardt Partners',19,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:29:\"Steinhardt, Fine, & Berkowitz\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15579,'Steinhardt Foundation for Jewish Life',37,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Philanthropy',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15580,'Connecticut Victory 2004',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15581,'New Futures PAC',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15582,'Aviation Partners Boeing',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Created in 1999, Aviation Partners Boeing (APB) is a joint venture of Aviation Partners, Inc. and The Boeing Company developed to equip Boeing airplanes with Blended Wingletâ¢ technology. APB combines the innovative spirit of Aviation Partners with the global strength of Boeing.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15583,'Washington Development',22,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','We carefully structure and coordinate the design/build process from predevelopment through buildout. We have experience ranging from early-stage communication with municipal planning boards to working with the construction trades to ensure timely finish dates.\r\nOur management experience includes handling the leasing of lands for a regional railroad, plus building, leasing, and operating shopping centers. In total, Washington Development manages over 5,000 leases.\r\n\r\nWe are a privately held company, being one of the Washington Companies in which noted industrialist Dennis R. Washington holds a significant ownership position. Washington Development enjoys the excellent reputation, prudent philosophy, and significant resources of the Washington Companies organization.\r\n\r\nIf you have an opportunity and are looking for a highly reliable company that can stand behind a commitment, we invite your consideration.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15584,'Gateway Limited Partners',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','We offer some of the best opportunities in the Western Montana market with commercial retail properties in prime high-visibility, high-traffic locations. Our tenants range from national chain anchors to local enterprises. With our office conveniently nearby, we are attentive to the best presentation of our properties, the satisfaction of our tenants, and the success of their businesses. Gateway Limited Partnership is affiliated with The Washington Companies.\r\nIn addition to an excellent location, Gateway offers services you expect from a professional commercial property management company, including:\r\nSecurity\r\nCommon area maintenance\r\nLease management\r\nMarketing','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15585,'Southern Railway of British Columbia',36,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','With over a century tradition of providing the best possible service, SRY is a major transporter of freight in British Columbia\'s Lower Mainland, and Fraser Valley. Almost one-half of the traffic we handle originates or terminates on Annacis Island, where major automobile and forest product distribution facilities are located. SRYâs diverse customer base includes over 150 shippers of forest, building, agricultural, chemical, consumer and steel products.\r\n\r\nSRY handles over 70,000 carloads annually and owns over 125 miles of track, of which 62 miles are mainline, and interchanges with four North American Class I railroads at six locations. We are âalways the bestâ in personalized, market driven, customer oriented and neutral shortline service. Combined with our long-haul partners: Canadian Pacific Railway, CN, BNSF, and Union Pacific SRY has connections to all rail-served points in North America.\r\n\r\nIn addition to maintaining its own fleet of 29 locomotives, SRYâs locomotive and car shops provide repair services to both Canadian and U.S. customers. SRY provides specialty railcars to customers and currently has over 2,000 cars in its fleet. It is part of the Rail Link System of the Washington Companies.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15586,'Seaspan International Ltd',25,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Within the Group are three shipyards, an intermodal ferry business, and a tug and barge transportation company that serves both domestic and international markets. The scope of Washington Marine Group\'s services, the quality of its employees and equipment, and over a century of successful participation in coastal commerce, makes this group a major partner in the economy of the Pacific Northwest.\r\nFor more detailed profiles please click on the photos below.\r\n\r\n \r\nMarine Transportation\r\n	\r\nSeaspan International Ltd.\r\nBeginning as a small coastal company, in 1898, servicing BC\'s coastal communities, Seaspan International Ltd., has evolved into a prominent marine transportation company serving the West Coast of North America. \r\n\r\nIn addition to marine transportation, Seaspan also provides shipdocking services to the Port of Vancouver, Victoria Esquimalt and other BC out ports.\r\n\r\n \r\n	\r\nSeaspan Coastal Intermodal Company \r\nSeaspan Coastal Intermodal Company is a commercial roll on - roll off ferry service providing regularly scheduled transportation between British Columbia\'s Lower Mainland and Vancouver Island\'s Nanaimo and Swartz Bay terminals. Based in Delta, Seaspan Coastal Intermodal transports truck trailers, containers, and railcars on self-propelled ferries and integrated tug-barge units.\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\nShipyards\r\nConvenient to Pacific Northwest shipping lanes, Washington Marine Group Shipyards are an important resource for the region\'s marine industry. The Group\'s operations consist of three shipyards that are all currently certified to ISO 9001 for quality, OHSAS 18001 for safety and ISO 14001 for environmental standards.\r\nVancouver Drydock Company Ltd.\r\nConveniently located in Vancouver Harbour, Vancouver Drydock operates two floating drydocks with lifting capacities of 36,000 tonnes in a Panamax beam dock, and 30,000 tonnes in a self contained deployable dock.\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\nVancouver Shipyards Co. Ltd.\r\nVancouver Shipyards has forged a solid reputation for the design, construction, maintenance, and repair of all types of vessels. The yard\'s facilities include a major steel forming shop, a large fabrication and assembly hall, a totally enclosed paint facility, and a SyncroLift capable of lifting vessels up to 1200 tonnes.\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\nVictoria Shipyards Co. Ltd.\r\nUtilizing the Esquimalt Graving Dock, owned and operated by Public Works and Government Services of Canada, Victoria Shipyards can drydock and repair vessels up to 100,000 DWT. Victoria Shipyards can perform a wide range of repairs up to and including complete vessel conversions.\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\nOther Services\r\n	\r\nMcKay Creek Technologies Ltd.\r\nMcKay Creek Technologies licenses a patented process for the treatment of industrial wastewater. The process, known as \"electrocoagulation\", can remove a wide range of contaminants from industrial wastewater.\r\n\r\n \r\n	\r\nMarine Petrobulk Ltd.\r\nFor over a quarter of a century, Marine Petrobulk has supplied all grades of bunker fuels to vessels entering the ports of Vancouver, New Westminster, Victoria, Prince Rupert, Kitimat and Nanaimo.','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15587,'Zionist Organization of America',31,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15588,'One Jerusalem',13,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15589,'Carl C Icahn Charter School',27,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15590,'Icahn Management',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15591,'George Soros',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15592,'Foundation for a Greater Opportunity',36,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Philanthropy',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15593,'Cbs Corporation Political Action Committee',42,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15594,'Farm Credit Administration',26,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,GovernmentBody',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15595,'Blue Dog PAC',12,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00'