nProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15763,'Champion Charities',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Harris Barton created Champion Charities, a 501(c)3 non-profit organization, in 2004 with his business partner, former teammate and friend, Ronnie Lott, after both of his parents passed away from brain tumors.','Org,Philanthropy',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15764,'Chicago Public Library Foundation',33,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Foundation also provides on-going funding, through its endowments and annual fundraising for collections, book acquisition and a variety of community-based programs that contribute to the excellence of the Library. In 2008, these gifts provided $3.6 million to the Chicago Public Library','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15765,'International Federation of Red Cross',37,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Founded in 1919, the International Federation comprises 186 member Red Cross and Red Crescent societies, a Secretariat in Geneva and more than 60 delegations strategically located to support activities around the world. There are more societies in formation. The Red Crescent is used in place of the Red Cross in many Islamic countries.\r\n\r\nThe Federation\'s vision: We strive, through voluntary action, for a world of empowered communities, better able to address human suffering and crises with hope, respect for dignity and a concern for equity.','Org,Philanthropy,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15766,'Museum of Science and Industry',30,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:28:\"Museum of Science & Industry\";}','Org','Chicago\'s Museum of Science and Industry, one of the largest science museums in the world, is home to more than 35,000 artifacts and nearly 14 acres of hands-on exhibits designed to spark scientific inquiry and creativity.','Org,Cultural,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-04-22 01:33:14',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15767,'Take Action Minnesota',21,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:21:\"Take Action Minnesota\";}','Org','','Org,MembershipOrg,PoliticalFundraising,LobbyingFirm,Pac',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15768,'Center for Economic Progress',28,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Center for Economic Progress was founded in 1990 by Michael OâConnor, a veteran public benefits lawyer. Formerly the Center for Law and Human Services, the agency first focused on helping homeless families and individuals access services.','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15769,'100 Women in Hedge Funds Foundation',35,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','To date 100 Women in Hedge Funds has raised over $17 million for charitable organizations focused on women\'s health, education and mentoring.','Org,Philanthropy',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15770,'100 Women in Hedge Funds',24,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15771,'Hedge Funds Care',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','What began as a single fundraiser has grown into an international nonprofit organization. Hedge Funds Care has distributed over $21 million through more than 600 grants.','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15772,'All Stars Helping Kids, Inc.',28,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','A trusted 501(c)(3) organization that athletes, corporations, and individuals enlist to assist with their philanthropic efforts and identify worthy charities to support.\r\n\r\nAn effective public benefit charity delivering successful events that raise awareness and support for high-performing non-profits that embrace the whole child.\r\n\r\nAn organization