assistance to more than 10,000 people of every racial and religious background at its headquarters in the Fairfax area and its office in North Hollywood and at more than 30 senior centers throughout Los Angeles County. With a dedicated staff of over 60 and more than 1,000 active volunteers, Bet Tzedek makes a crucial difference in the lives of the most vulnerable members of the community.','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15980,'Byrd Hoffman Foundation',23,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:23:\"Byrd Hoffman Foundation\";}','Org','The Foundation seeks to develop new approaches to the arts; to provide young people with opportunities for artistic growth; and to document the work of its Artistic Director, Robert Wilson, and his contemporaries. In addition to the Watermill Center, the Foundation manages the Robert Wilson Archive and the Watermill Collection. The Byrd Hoffman Watermill Foundation is a not-for-profit, 501(c)3 tax-exempt organization chartered in 1969 in the State of New York.','Org,NonProfit,Cultural',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15981,'Student Loan Guarantee Foundation of Arkansas',45,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15982,'Benjamin N Cardozo School of Law',32,NULL,'a:2:{i:0;s:0:\"\";i:1;s:18:\"Cardozo Law School\";}','Org','Founded in 1976 by Yeshiva University, one of the finest research universities in the United States.\r\nCardozoâs faculty is known for being widely-published legal scholars, most of whom have also practiced law. They are accessible and invite ongoing dialogue with their students--inside and outside of the classroom. In addition, nearly half of the faculty also hold advanced degrees in other disciplines, making them particularly qualified to provide a fully-rounded and rigorous legal education. Cardozo students also benefit from a curriculum that has a strong balance of theory and practice. The Law Schoolâs clinical program offers experiences in criminal, corporate, family, human rights, and immigration law, as well as others, and internships, externships, and job opportunities are diverse and abundant in the city that never sleeps. \r\n\r\nThere are certain qualities that set Cardozo apart and give it a unique character. Among them are flexibility and the desire and drive not to be complacent but to constantly improve for the benefit of students and societyâall with New York as a back drop. Cardozoâs special, nationally known programsâamong them the Innocence Project, Intellectual Property Law Program, Alternative Dispute Resolution, and Holocaust Claims Restitution Clinic--combine intellectual excellence and a visionary edge that is helping to shape the legal landscape.','Org,School',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 02:56:33',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15983,'Damon Runyan Cancer Research',28,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','t all began in 1946 with the death from cancer of Damon Runyon, the journalist and short story writer, whose beloved Broadway stories were later transformed into the hit show Guys & Dolls.  His good friend, Walter Winchell, renowned journalist and radio commentator, went on his famous radio program and appealed to âMr. and Mrs. Americaâ for contributions to help fight cancer.  The response was overwhelming, enabling Winchell to establish the âDamon Runyon Cancer Memorial Fundâ with the mission of supporting the most promising early career scientists across the nation.  He led the fund, with the help of such celebrities as Marlene Dietrich, Bob Hope, Milton Berle, Marilyn Monroe and Joe DiMaggio, until his own death from cancer in 1972.','Org,PoliticalFundraising',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15984,'Greater LA Zoo Association',26,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The Greater Los Angeles Zoo Association is a nonprofit corporation created to support the Los Angeles Zoo in its mission to nurture wildlife and enrich the human experience. GLAZA\'s primary responsibility is to seek and provide financial support for the Zooâs programs and capital projects. GLAZA performs other support functions as requested by the Zoo Director.','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15985,'Vail Valley Foundation',22,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','Through athletics, culture and education, the Vail Valley Foundation has been enriching our community, the lives of our residents, and those of our guests since 1981. Fueled by the generous support of our donors and an ongoing commitment to serve the people of the Valley, the Foundation is responsible for providing our community with some of its most treasured annual events, such as the Vail International Dance Festival,  AEI World Forum,  American Ski Classic,  Birds of Prey Race Week,  Honda Session,  Vilar Performing Arts Center and our summer and winter free concert series. We have also had the pleasure of bringing major international events to the Vail Valley, including the 1989 and 1999 World Alpine Ski Championships and the 1994 and 2001 World Mountain Bike Championships.\r\n\r\nWhile the impact of the events we bring to the Vail Valley is phenomenal, we believe some of the most important work we do is in supporting literacy programs for our communityâs youth and providing higher education scholarships for deserving graduates of our local high schools. Through annual grants, the Foundation also supports other worthy non-profits in the Valley. Organizations such as the Youth Foundation, the Magic Book Bus, the Vail Symposium and others work with us to help further the mission, helping us to have an even greater impact throughout our community.\r\n\r\nWe consider it a great privilege to have the ability to improve the quality of life we all experience in the Vail Valley. It is only through the dedication and support of our partners, who share our dedication to this community, that we are able to carry out our vision. With your help, we, the Vail Valley Foundation, pledge to continue our mission of bringing the world to the Vail Valley and the Vail Valley to the world.','Org,NonProfit',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15986,'Institute for Financial Markets',31,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,IndustryTrade',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15987,'Bank of Montreal',16,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15988,'Maryland Office of Financial Regulation',39,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15989,'Rose Grove Capital',18,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org,Business',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15990,'Cambridge Judge Business School',31,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','The School is an internationally recognised provider of innovative, intellectually challenging management education, encouraging critical reflection and creativity, and attracting the most able students to all its courses.\r\n\r\nCourses include a PhD programme, masters programmes whose focus ranges from research to professional practice, and undergraduate studies.\r\n\r\nAll students at Cambridge Judge Business School also join one of the Cambridge Colleges, which provides a social context for their work and an opportunity to meet students and academics from other disciplines.','Org,School',15110,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15991,'Portfolio Logic',15,NULL,'a:1:{i:0;s:0:\"\";}','Org','','Org',0,'2010-10-15 00:00:00','2011-03-16 01:28:49',NULL,0,'active',NULL,NULL,NULL),(15992,'The Advisory Board Company',26,NULL,'a:1:{